{"raw": {"https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/records-and-registration-specialist-wichita-kansas-united-states-4839343a-364c-4454-b31f-62932f93ccfe": {"title": "Records and Registration Specialist", "description": "Records and Registration Specialist - Wichita, Kansas, United States Records and Registration Specialist - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Records and Registration Specialist Strategic Enrollment Mgmt | Academic/Student Support, Staff Records and Registration Specialist 499798 Academic/Student Support Staff Department: Registrar's Office Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $17.73/hr, potential for slight adjustment based on qualifications Work Schedule: Mon-Fri, 8 a to 5 p; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. We are seeking a detail-oriented professional who values accuracy, enjoys organizing information, and thrives in a collaborative environment. In this role, you will play an important part in supporting students throughout their academic journey, from requesting their first transcript to earning their diploma. As a key member of our team, you will: Process all incoming and outgoing transcripts for WSU students. Review, process, and maintain student records with a high degree of accuracy and attention to detail. Use multiple applications and systems to complete tasks that help students remain enrolled and achieve their educational goals. Identify and resolve discrepancies while ensuring the integrity and accuracy of institutional data. Utilize Microsoft Excel and Word to manage information, prepare documentation, and support departmental processes. Provide exceptional service to students, faculty, staff, alumni, and external partners through clear, professional communication. Collaborate with colleagues to ensure timely completion of tasks and seamless office operations. Assist with departmental priorities and provide support wherever needed to help the team succeed. What Makes You Successful We're looking for someone who is: Detail-oriented and accurate, with a commitment to producing high-quality work. Highly organized, capable of managing multiple responsibilities while maintaining consistency and efficiency. Proficient in Microsoft Excel and Word, using technology effectively to support daily operations. Dependable and collaborative, willing to support teammates and contribute to a positive workplace culture. Service-focused, with a genuine desire to help students and colleagues succeed. Why This Role Matters This position is about more than processing records and managing information. It is about helping students navigate important milestones and ensuring they receive the support they need every step of the way. Your work will directly contribute to the accuracy of student records, the effectiveness of university operations, and the success of the students we serve. Every transcript processed, record maintained, and question answered helps students move closer to achieving their educational goals. If you are passionate about precision, enjoy meaningful work, and want to be part of a team that values reliability, collaboration, and service, we encourage you to apply. Join us and make a lasting impact on the student experience at Wichita State University. This position is an on-campus role with no allowance for WFH Job Summary Facilitates student registration and records services for one (1) or more registrar areas. Utilizes relevant technology platforms and recommends process and procedural changes as needed. Essential Functions Processes, manages, and troubleshoots transcript, enrollment, and record requests and verifications. May lead and train support staff, as needed. Provides customer service, guidance, and coordination for assigned area of responsibility. Ensures records and/or systems are accurate and reliable. Assists with testing, troubleshooting, and/or providing recommendations for system and/or process upgrades of new technologies. Provides and/or assists with prompt resolution to initial records and registration policy and procedural inquiries or concerns. Job Duties Front Desk & Student Support Serve as the first point of contact at the service counter and by phone, assisting students, faculty, staff, and external constituents with general inquiries. Assist students with computer use and other service counter needs. Process student system access requests. Respond to One Stop tickets in collaboration with the One Stop Office. Records & Verification Processing Process incoming and outgoing transcript requests. Process student reactivation requests through the Reactivation Application. Work with the National Student Clearinghouse to verify student enrollment and degree information. Handle third-party verification requests and time status updates. Create enrollment, certification, and other verification letters for organizations not utilizing the National Student Clearinghouse. Create invitation letters for international students. Manage the student verification email inbox and related requests. Diploma & Graduation Services Manage and track Anticipated Graduation Date (ARD) forms. Coordinate diploma distribution three times annually, including tracking mailing costs and distribution. Order diploma covers and maintain inventory. Process diploma requests using the Diploma Mailing Application. Mail & Document Processing Pick up, sort, and process incoming mail daily. Process Foster Care and Legacy Tuition forms. Apply official seals to university documents as required. Cashiering & Administrative Support Process payments using the CME (TouchNet) cashiering system. Prepare deposits as needed. Maintain departmental statistics and prepare reports for supervisor and team meetings. Team & Operational Support Maintain task statistics for the Records Verification Group. Provide cross-functional backup support for multiple operational areas within the Registrar's Office. Assist with special projects and other duties as assigned. Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent Two (2) years of experience in general office, clerical, administrative support or related field Required License/Certifications/Training: None Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Strong communication and Interpersonal skills. Proficiency with computer systems and the ability to learn institutional software quickly. Ability to handle sensitive information with confidentiality and professionalism. Detail-oriented with strong organizational skills Preferred Qualifications: Associate Degree or some college preferred. Experience working in higher education. Additional Information: This position is an on-campus role with no allowance for WFH Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) 374408ea Last Name (required) b8935d07 Email (required) 6f2535b7 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) e3b78f38 Last Name (required) 99e229c9 Email (required) 6e79bf44 Job Alert cf8bc189 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic/Student Support Staff Academic/Student Support Staff Department(s) Strategic Enrollment Mgmt Strategic Enrollment Mgmt Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 3aa40aa3 Last Name (required) 685ef0cb Email (required) 69e7f0f3 Send This Job To: a7203a77 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" \u2013 Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Student Assistant/Student Adminstrative Assistant The TRIO SSS STEM Program is seeking a detail-oriented and organized student to serve as a Student Administrative Assistant. This position will play an important role in supporting program operations and helping develop administrative processes for a growing federally funded student success program serving STEM majors. This position is ideal for a student interested in organizational leadership, business administration, project management, communications, higher education, nonprofit management, or related fields who would like practical experience supporting program operations and student services. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) cb99f6a8 Last Name (required) 45bcbbd1 Email (required) 45710fdc Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/litigation-paralegal-and-contracts-manager-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager", "description": "Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager - Wichita, Kansas, United States Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager General Counsel (College) | Staff Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager 499803 Staff Department: Office of the General Counsel Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range $57,000\u2013$75,000/yr, commensurate with qualifications Work Schedule: General business hours; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a \u201cU.S. Citizen\u201d. Job Story Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Some areas you'll be directly responsible for: Investigation & Research Pleadings & Drafting Discovery and Records Management Attorney Support Case & Deadline Management Work with university stakeholders across departments and leadership levels, helping navigate legal and regulatory requirements, coordinate contract development, and prepare documentation that supports agency actions, legal proceedings, and institutional decisions. The common thread? You know how to turn complex, detail-heavy work into an organized process with clear next steps. Priorities can shift quickly. Sensitive information must be handled appropriately. You'll need the judgment to recognize what needs immediate attention, the initiative to seek out missing information, and the persistence to see projects through to completion. If you're someone who values accuracy, exercises sound judgment, manages competing deadlines, and takes pride in making complicated work easier to navigate, this is an opportunity to put those strengths to work in a university-wide environment. Job Summary Supports the Office of General Counsel in drafting policies, contracts and legal documents pertaining to University activities and other initiatives. Responds to records requests and subpoenas; conducts interviews of witnesses; identifies, gathers, organizes and summarizes records in preparation for agency action or lawsuit; and performs support functions as it relates to managing outside counsel, records and database libraries and intake on legal guidance and counseling issues. Facilitates contract development as well as campus training and communication efforts. Researches and interprets regulations, guidelines, and standards and negotiates, drafts, edits, approves, and oversees the processing of contracts. Manages all office activities including business operations, facilities, overseeing all expenditures and coordinates financial reporting, administrative support for department programs and services, and work product of administrative personnel and student hires. Essential Functions Writes, reviews, and negotiates contracts and legal documents with internal and external partners. Researches and facilitates compliance with University, state, and federal laws, policies, and regulations in the daily operation of the contract lifecycle. Provides guidance to internal leaders and administrators on contract negotiation strategies. Serves as a liaison between senior leadership and employees. Drafts, edits and processes policies. Supports and manages litigation efforts, documents, evidence and witnesses. Conducts interviews of, and compiles key documents from, potential witnesses in internal and external hearings, claims against the University, agency actions, and litigation. Tracks case filings and developments and reports to attorneys and clients. Assists with review of outside counsel billing statements. Directs and coordinates office services and staff in the development and supervision of departmental operations and services, which includes hiring and onboarding for staff. Resolves office problems independently and facilitates solutions. Hires, supervises, trains, mentors, evaluates, and manages administrative assistant(s) and student employees, as applicable. Oversees administrative support and coordination for meetings, conferences, events, projects, and services. Provides ongoing monitoring and tracking of department budget. Job Duties \u2022 Provide advanced litigation and legal support for active and threatened litigation, administrative proceedings, claims, investigations, mediations, depositions, discovery, settlements, and other legal matters. \u2022 Manage and coordinate responses to complaints, charges, subpoenas, records requests, court orders, and governmental or regulatory inquiries, including matters involving the EEOC, KHRC, U.S. Department of Education, KBOR, and HLC. \u2022 Conduct and support internal investigations, including gathering and reviewing records, interviewing witnesses, preparing declarations, and drafting responses, correspondence, agreements, and other legal documents for attorney review. \u2022 Administer legal holds and document-preservation processes and maintain litigation, subpoena, claims, legal-hold, outside-counsel, and other legal matter tracking and reporting systems. \u2022 Coordinate with University leadership, departments, witnesses, governmental agencies, outside counsel, and affiliated organizations regarding legal matters, deadlines, document production, and compliance obligations. \u2022 Manage significant University-wide legal, regulatory, remediation, and compliance projects, including developing tracking systems, coordinating stakeholders, monitoring deliverables, and reporting progress to attorneys and University leadership. \u2022 Assist with outside counsel management, including engagement documentation, conflict waivers, invoice review and processing, scheduling, and matter coordination. \u2022 Develop and maintain Office of General Counsel procedures and assist with legal research, court-record searches, risk monitoring, legislative requests, and preventive legal compliance activities. \u2022 Assist attorneys with employee, student, labor-relations, and other institutional matters presenting legal or litigation risk, including participation in collective bargaining and meet-and-confer activities. \u2022 Perform other legal, compliance, and administrative duties necessary to support the effective operation of the Office of General Counsel. \u2022 Investigation & Research: Conduct searches and case compilation using platforms like Westlaw, Pacer, Findlaw, and gather evidence, locate and interview witnesses, and run background checks. \u2022 Pleadings & Drafting: Draft complaints, answers, agency responses, and discovery requests or responses under attorney supervision. \u2022 Discovery and Records Management: Oversee legal holds, discovery production, prepare key document and case chronologies, and manage and coordinate with outside counsel electronic discovery (eDiscovery). \u2022 Attorney Support: Prepare all documents, exhibits, and outlines for agency, court, and dispute matters; coordinate witness schedules; manage court filings (including federal systems like PACER/ECF), and provide real-time support. \u2022 Case & Deadline Management: Track strict court deadlines, maintain master calendars, and organize case files. Required Education and Experience: 60 hours of college coursework in business administration, law, or social science. Seven (7) years of experience in general office, clerical, administrative support or related field, with two (2) years of experience in project management or contract administration. An additional 60 hours of college coursework can be substituted for two (2) years of experience. Required License/Certifications/Training: None Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: \u2022 Knowledge of legal processes, litigation procedures, investigations, discovery, subpoenas, records preservation, and administrative proceedings. \u2022 Strong organizational and project-management skills, including the ability to manage multiple complex matters, competing priorities, and time-sensitive deadlines. \u2022 Ability to conduct factual investigations, interview witnesses, gather and analyze records, and summarize complex information. \u2022 Strong legal writing, research, analytical, and proofreading skills. \u2022 Ability to draft professional correspondence, legal documents, investigative materials, reports, and responses for attorney review. \u2022 Capable exercising sound judgment, discretion, initiative, and independent decision-making within assigned responsibilities. \u2022 Ability to handle confidential, privileged, and sensitive information appropriately. \u2022 Strong interpersonal and communication skills and ability to work effectively with attorneys, senior leadership, employees, students, outside counsel, governmental agencies, and other stakeholders. \u2022 Ability to develop and maintain effective tracking, records-management, and legal matter-management systems. \u2022 Proficiency with Microsoft Office and electronic document-management, collaboration, and research systems. \u2022 Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment and effectively manage significant or sensitive institutional matters. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in any field combined with substantial relevant legal, litigation, compliance, or investigative experience. Five or more years of progressively responsible experience in a law firm, corporate or governmental legal department, higher-education legal office, compliance office, or similar environment. Experience supporting litigation, administrative proceedings, investigations, discovery, subpoenas, legal holds, or regulatory responses. Experience managing complex projects involving multiple departments or stakeholders. Experience drafting legal documents and substantive correspondence for attorney review. Experience working with outside counsel, governmental agencies, senior leadership, or regulatory bodies. Higher-education, governmental, public-sector, employment-law, or regulatory-compliance experience preferred. Preferred License/Certifications/Training: One or more of the following may be preferred but should not necessarily be required: \u2022 Paralegal certificate from an ABA-approved or other recognized paralegal program. \u2022 Certified Paralegal (CP), Advanced Certified Paralegal (ACP), or comparable professional credential. \u2022 Training or experience in e-discovery, litigation support, investigations, records management, or legal-hold administration. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) 0eeb4257 Last Name (required) 8b10077c Email (required) 061177b1 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) eb3c65c5 Last Name (required) 21830a16 Email (required) 98cbadba Job Alert c22f9f13 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staff Department(s) General Counsel (College) General Counsel (College) Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 70d9ec1b Last Name (required) f9c409c5 Email (required) 5c8e299f Send This Job To: 58ef9483 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" \u2013 Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Student Assistant/Student Adminstrative Assistant The TRIO SSS STEM Program is seeking a detail-oriented and organized student to serve as a Student Administrative Assistant. This position will play an important role in supporting program operations and helping develop administrative processes for a growing federally funded student success program serving STEM majors. This position is ideal for a student interested in organizational leadership, business administration, project management, communications, higher education, nonprofit management, or related fields who would like practical experience supporting program operations and student services. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 0d297135 Last Name (required) 6bca8164 Email (required) 2a200d47 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number