WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Circulation \u2022 Checking library materials in and out, renewing them and placing holds on them \u2022 Answering basic questions about the library, its policies and services, and campus directions \u2022 Assisting library users with room bookings, locating items, etc. Interlibrary Loan \u2022 Retrieving materials from the stacks and packaging them for shipping for Interlibrary Loan \u2022 Scan print articles and chapters on overhead book scanner and deliver electronically to patrons Stacks \u2022 Searching for lost/missing library materials \u2022 Responsible for service, maintenance, and knowledge of WSU Library stacks \u2022 Assists with inventory control of the physical collection to include performing maintenance within the stacks All Areas \u2022 Demonstrating basic customer service skills \u2022 Gathering statistics for projects as requested by the staff \u2022 Must become adept with office equipment, including copier, scanner, and computer \u2022 Become familiar with our library catalog and journal databases \u2022 Other duties as assigned. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements \u2022 Morning (preferably 7am - 1pm) and weekend availability \u2022 Enrolled at WSU \u2022 Good communication skills \u2022 Able to follow written and oral instructions \u2022 Basic computer skills \u2022 Duties include: squatting, bending, lifting between 5 and 50 pounds, and other physical work Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications \u2022 Customer service experience \u2022 Library experience Additional Information Work study students are encouraged to apply. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) c5db8952 Last Name (required) f0b58759 Email (required) c261114e Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) aca16688 Last Name (required) d3aa4714 Email (required) ccbe3925 Job Alert f3796c14 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Library Library Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 2d3c7660 Last Name (required) b835c311 Email (required) 0308ad17 Send This 