to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/pathfinders-housing-and-residence-life-wichita-kansas-united-states-45c0e74c-03f1-4a08-aa5b-81db4aec1ae9": {"title": "Pathfinders- Housing and Residence Life", "description": "Pathfinders- Housing and Residence Life - Wichita, Kansas, United States Pathfinders- Housing and Residence Life - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Pathfinders- Housing and Residence Life Student Affairs (College) | Academic/Student Support, Student Pathfinders- Housing and Residence Life 499877 Academic/Student Support Student Department Housing and Residence Life Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $10/hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Variable dependent upon class schedule Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story The Pathfinders\u2019 position is a vital member of the Residence Life staff. Pathfinders contribute to residents' education by serving as mentors, role models, and academic resources, and by connecting them with other key departments across campus. The Pathfinders will play a key role in fulfilling the academic mission of the Housing and Residence Life department. It is important that Pathfinders develop and maintain open lines of communication with faculty and staff involved in LLC and Housing and Residence Life. To achieve these goals, the Pathfinders must be actively engaged with students in their LLC and with various campus departments. This person will report directly to the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement or designee. In addition, the Pathfinders will work closely with the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement and the Graduate Student for Educational Engagement. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Community Development Responsibilities \u2022 Assist residents in formulating academic objectives concurrent with their individual interests and potential skill levels. \u2022 Provide residents with information regarding registration, drop/add, and curricular requirements. \u2022 Facilitate opportunities for residents to develop in the areas of learning styles, study skills, and test-taking. \u2022 Facilitate review sessions, study hours, and other academic support activities for students on the floor. \u2022 Establish and maintain appropriate relationships with students in the LLC for the purpose of facilitating the transition to university life and ensuring academic success. \u2022 Provide opportunities for developing skills in choosing an academic major and planning a career. \u2022 Act as a referral agent by directing students, when appropriate, to various academic support services such as Academic Advising, the Writing Center, the Math Lab, and the Student Success Center. Administrative Responsibilities \u2022 Participate in training workshops prior to the beginning of each semester and throughout the academic year. \u2022 Help run events during Week Zero. \u2022 Attend and participate in staff meetings and one-on-ones. \u2022 Facilitate LLC educational programming for residents monthly. \u2022 Create and maintain one bulletin board in the building, changing it monthly. \u2022 Provide assistance to, and communicate with, faculty, staff members, and LLC Coordinators. \u2022 Become knowledgeable about academic services available to students and make appropriate referrals. \u2022 Actively participate in LLC floor, university/college programs, and activities, and facilitate residents\u2019 involvement with the same programs and activities. \u2022 Work closely with the LLC Coordinators to build community and accomplish academic initiatives. \u2022 Work closely with the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement and the Graduate Student for Educational Engagement to accomplish residence life goals and to ensure that the interests of participating students are integrated into the program. \u2022 Serve as a liaison between residents in LLC and other departments, specifically within the Division of Campus Life, Academics, and LLC Coordinators. \u2022 Assume other responsibilities related to the LLC floor and residence life programs as directed by the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement and the Graduate Student for Educational Engagement. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements \u2022 May carry a maximum academic course load of 16 hours during each semester of employment. Any exception must be approved in writing by the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement. \u2022 Be available for training the week before move-in. \u2022 Must maintain a minimum cumulative and semester GPA of 2.5 during the period of employment. \u2022 Attend and participate in one-on-ones with the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement or designee. \u2022 Attend and participate in staff meetings. \u2022 May not engage in additional part-time or full-time work, student teaching, internship, or assistantship without prior written approval from the Assistant Director of Educational Engagement Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications \u2022 Possess a motivating interest in working with the students in Shocker Hall. \u2022 Have a minimum cumulative and semester GPA of 2.5 on a 4.0 scale. \u2022 Be available to serve on the staff for two (2) consecutive semesters (Fall & Spring). \u2022 Have lived in a WSU residence hall for at least one (1) semester. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 001d72fb Last Name (required) 382cd911 Email (required) 047d679b Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) ac4e0fc6 Last Name (required) 848edfa1 Email (required) c94048ff Job Alert 805ebaa1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic/Student Support Student Academic/Student Support Student Department(s) Student Affairs (College) Student Affairs (College) Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 0302f7ba Last Name (required) 8b15d6e4 Email (required) 4e285b2c Send This Job To: b079befc Share Now! Please wait... Done