Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 743c40f5 Last Name (required) 8d6ab454 Email (required) 79b483b6 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-in-teacher-apprentice-program-ee-ecu-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Teacher Apprentice Program - EE/ECU", "description": "Assistant Professor in Teacher Apprentice Program - EE/ECU - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor in Teacher Apprentice Program - EE/ECU - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor in Teacher Apprentice Program - EE/ECU College of Education | Faculty Assistant Professor in Teacher Apprentice Program - EE/ECU 499440 On Site Faculty Department: Teacher Apprenticeship Pathways, Literacy, & Special Education Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $65,000 Work Schedule: Typically, 8am-5pm, with some flexibility for evenings as needed ; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The College of Education at Wichita State University seeks a dynamic and experienced colleague to enhance our Teacher Apprentice Program (TAP) Team. Housed in the Department of Teacher Apprentice Pathways, Literacy and Special Education, the Assistant Professor in TAP is a full-time, 9-month, tenure-track faculty position with a focus on teaching a variety of undergraduate courses related to specific content areas and foundational teacher preparation courses, mentoring TAP students and providing leadership to faculty and adjunct instructors, research, and service. Applicants must be committed to fostering an inviting environment and promoting the success of our students. The academic appointment for this position will be effective August 2, 2027. Serving over 700 students, TAP prepares students to complete their Bachelor of Arts in Early Childhood Unified/Elementary Education without leaving their current Para Educator job, earning field experience for work as a Para Educator. Courses are 100% online with some in-person options for general education course requirements. An inverted curriculum provides students opportunities to take education courses in their first semester in the program, increasing their skills as a para while working towards licensure as a Kansas teacher. Dedicated mentors provide guidance and support to students throughout their time in the program. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties The Assistant Professor in TAP EE/ECU will design and lead multi-disciplinary teaching initiatives including the redesign and continuous updating of content specific pedagogy courses as well as foundational education courses within TAP, to align with state and national accreditation, as well as program and student needs. Teaching will be informed by research and service in the field of alternative certification as well as content area and content specific pedagogical strategies. The Assistant Professor role will include 40% teaching in TAP EE/ECU will teach 9 credit hours in each fall and 9 credit hours in each spring semester, with a focus on core content specific pedagogy courses, exceptionality courses, core content concepts courses, foundational education courses, and/or internship or field experience courses. This also includes mentoring TAP students in their applied learning experiences throughout the program. Research and scholarship activities for the Assistant Professor in TAP EE/ECU will include 40% of the role, encompassing original research and program evaluation support. Specific research interest areas of candidates should include content specific pedagogies, alternative certification teacher pathways, student centeredness, and innovative teacher preparation programming. The faculty member would be expected to seek external funding grant opportunities for research and/or student supports and assist with current ongoing funded initiatives. The Assistant Professor in TAP EE/ECU will be expected to represent WSU by producing original works, both publications and presentations. Service ranging from program to national/international representation will be expected for 20% of the role of the Assistant Professor in TAP EE/ECU. Service to the program, department, college and university in the form of serving on and chairing committees of interest will be expected. Service to the program will include serving on the TAP Leadership Team, collaborating with faculty, supporting mentors and adjuncts instructors, and guiding program initiatives. Service to the field and profession, in the form of community, state-level, and national/international-level organization membership and engagement will be expected. This position requires regular on-campus presence at Wichita State University. The selected candidate must reside in Kansas within a reasonable commuting distance of the WSU main campus. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements Earned doctorate (Ph.D. or Ed.D.) in Early Childhood, Elementary, Special Education, or related field, completed prior to August 2027. Experience in K-12 teaching Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Willingness to accommodate a variety of learning styles and strategies in instructional delivery and learning activities, including online and blended learning, flexible teaching methods, and applied learning approaches. Ability to use various forms of technology to communicate with students, faculty, and other stakeholders in and outside of the university in 1:1, small group, and large group settings for varied purposes. Knowledge of and ability to describe practical implications of current trends, research, and education within the teacher preparation field. Familiarity with national and state standards and their implications to classroom instruction, teacher preparation, and curriculum design. Ability to design learning experiences and assessments that model best practices in education and are inclusive of special education students. Ability to make data-driven decisions that demonstrate continuous improvement in several settings (i.e. online instruction, K-12 curriculum design, teacher preparation program). Ability to learn program parameters and apply them to individual student programs of study and accreditation standards. Strong communication and interpersonal skills to work effectively with all students and colleagues. Commitment to fostering an environment in which all students, faculty, staff, and community partners feel welcome, valued, supported, and engaged. Preferred Qualifications: Experience mentoring pre-service or in-service teachers Experience in online course development and implementation Elementary Teaching Experience Demonstrated experience and capability in conducting and disseminating scholarly research Preferred License/Certifications/Training: Elementary (PK-6) Teaching License Additional Information: Please complete the Faculty Profile including the names and contact information of three (3) references and upload the following documents: 1. Cover letter 2. Curriculum Vitae 3. Teaching Statement 4. Research Statement Review of applications has been pushed back to November 30, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position \u2013 Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators \u2013 Frequent 60-90% Apply Now First Name (required) b86a4c35 Last Name (required) 821f1160 Email (required) 8f00b746 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 9a8416fa Last Name (required) 351777dc Email (required) 19d60f8a Job Alert dc153420 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Education College of Education Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) ca40fc98 Last Name (required) 8e138ecd Email (required) d14434d7 Send This Job To: c9d2aa9a Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" \u2013 Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) dd476d74 Last Name (required) f029f8ee Email (required) 210ecac0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/hr-assistant-shared-services-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "HR Assistant - Shared Services", "description": "HR Assistant - Shared Services - Wichita, Kansas, United States HR Assistant - Shared Services - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode HR Assistant - Shared Services Culture and HR | Staff HR Assistant - Shared Services 499812 Staff Department: Human Resources Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Beginning at $17.73/hr, adjustment dependent upon qualifications Work Schedule: General business hours (typical M-F 8-5); work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Making an impact happens in this position in so many ways and with so many people! Our team focuses on providing detailed and accurate service to our university partners in all aspects related to hiring, onboarding & after hire updates. This makes this position dedicated to customer service and problem resolution to solution focused. Downstream effects of our work impact multiple systems and partners. We seek an individual who can identify errors others miss & ensure the team is being as accurate, effective & efficient as possible. Your day can change from standard daily tasks to switching gears into problem solving mode or address customer concerns in an instant & then end with an appointment with an employee. The ability to move seamlessly from task to task when interruptions happen, but you are not rattled by this in order to be successful. Recovery from interruptions and regaining focus for attention to detail is a must. This position also provides you with variety in your day, as well as perpetual learning opportunities in the realm of HR. Join the team who helps new employees get started on the right foot, transitions across the university, departments seeking us out for guidance, & depend on us to ensure compliance with all employment aspects at the university! Job Summary Assists with day-to-day operations of human resources functions within a shared services framework. Essential Functions \u2022 Provides support to staff in various functional areas by assisting with administering, monitoring, and coordinating programs and processes. \u2022 Provides information and assistance to employees by ensuring effective communication and prompt resolution of requests and questions. \u2022 Collects, compiles, enters, and verifies data for payroll and employee records. Reviews and verifies incoming and outgoing documentation for completeness, accuracy and compliance. \u2022 Assists with the development, planning and implementation of meetings and events which may include scheduling space, room set-up, follow up with customers, and preparing materials, as needed. Job Duties Actively engage department(s) regarding the formal hiring processes and practices at the university, ensuring they fall within compliance &/or policy guidelines. Review of documentation, providing guidance within system operations & university practices. Carries out the daily operations of core HR functions, supporting the hiring processes and after hire transitions. Examples include: running background checks, form completion, storage of documentation, performing I-9 appointments, audit of employee information, & cross checking of info provided by depts pertinent to university processes. Ensures confidentiality and compliance with institutional policies and other regulations governing HR. Reviews, collects and validates data from systems, forms, or other sources to ensure accuracy. Conducting yourself as a professional, ethical, & trustworthy member of HR for the university. Develops training materials, guides, or reference documents for internal needs or the university at large. Triages questions and issues, determining when escalation or referral to another HR member is appropriate. Provide options to stakeholders/depts to operate within, steering them to the appropriate course of action for their needs; OR if not possible, providing them context as to why they cannot proceed. Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent Six (6) months of experience in human resources, office administration, or related field. Required License/Certifications/Training: None Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Provide customer service and communicate clearly both in verbal and written format. Communicate with clear, concise messages while asking deciphering & investigative questions to fully understand situation or scenarios faced with regularly. Ability to multi-task, including stopping and starting tasks to respond to needs. Organized in working through tasks, which may be interrupted, with the ability to pick up where you left off to meet deadlines. Recognize when data and processes appear different and understand the context the work has in a larger process. Understanding of the importance of details, why they need to be cross checked & ensure accuracy in all aspects of work. Take initiative and present solutions that meet compliance, policies & process gaps, if they exist. Basic knowledge related to overall HR guidelines, practices, concepts or laws. Preferred Qualifications: Experience within Human Resources field &/or direct application of common work in HR. Experience in higher education payroll, HR. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) 1d5caead Last Name (required) 005fe1b8 Email (required) e5e7ff56 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 6036b256 Last Name (required) 1cd55440 Email (required) 3616ab3f Job Alert e8338b03 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staff Department(s) Culture and HR Culture and HR Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 7469f333 Last Name (required) 2d191e42 Email (required) 626ecc8f Send This Job To: d3d35922 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" \u2013 Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) ac2b020e Last Name (required) a48e41cb Email (required) 2c386062 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/university-police-chief-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "University Police Chief", "description": "University Police Chief - Wichita, Kansas, United States University Police Chief - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode University Police Chief WSU Police Department | Staff University Police Chief 499719 Staff Department: WSU Police Department Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range from $108,000-$140,000/yr, negotiated based on qualifications Work Schedule: 8-5 Monday-Friday; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a \u201cU.S. Citizen\u201d. Job Story Wichita State University invites applications for University Police Chief (Chief). The Chief serves as the chief law enforcement and public safety executive for the Wichita State University and provides strategic leadership, direction, and oversight for all police and public safety operations. The Chief is responsible for developing and implementing a comprehensive campus public safety program that supports the University's academic, research, residential, healthcare, and administrative missions while promoting a safe, inclusive, and welcoming environment for students, faculty, staff, visitors, and the broader university community. Job Summary Directs, plans and manages all functions and operations of the University police department in the enforcement of laws and University regulations, the prevention of crime, and protection of life and property. Essential Functions Directs and coordinates University security, safety and protection programs to include traffic control, patrolling of physical property; enforcement of statues and University regulations, crime prevention and investigation of accidents, injuries and criminal acts. Serves as the face and spokesperson of the University for all law enforcement related issues. Maintains a high degree of visibility, represents the department in the local community and serves a central role in establishing and maintaining strong collaborative relationships with University staff and local, regional, state and federal public safety agencies. Develops department budget and monitors and adjusts plan as resource requirements change. Provides timely and accurate reports in compliance with local, state, and federal regulations and higher education guidelines including monthly criminal and conduct statistics, crime reports, and the annual DOE Clery Act report. Develops and leads managers and officers in the efficient and effective administration of law enforcement initiatives and programs. Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent Ten (10) years of experience in general law enforcement or related field, including progressively responsible supervisory and managerial experience at the command staff level. Every 30 hours of college coursework in criminal justice, fire science, law enforcement or related field can be substituted for one (1) year of experience. Required License/Certifications/Training: Meet minimum qualifications standards of the State of Kansas for certified police officer as outlined in K.S.A. 74-5605 Certified law enforcement officer or capability to become a Kansas certified law enforcement officer within one year of hire date, in accordance with Kansas law Completed basic law enforcement training program recognized by Kansas Law Enforcement Training Commission (KLETC) and obtained certification as a law enforcement officer from KLETC before given permanent status Complete and receive Criminal Justice Information Services (CJIS) and National Crime Information Center (NCIC) certification within one (1) year of hire date or will be terminated Valid Kansas driver's license Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to manage a full-service police department, budgets and daily operations. Ability to work effectively in collaborative environments and engage constructively with individuals from a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. Preferred Qualifications: Experience on a leadership team within a department High level of law enforcement experience. Experience in an educational environment Additional Information: Application Instructions: - Verification of Highest Level of Education (please provide a copy of your transcript or scanned copy of your diploma/equivalency as required by KSA 74-5605). Providing false or misleading statements within this application, whether intentional or not, will result in permanent removal from the application process. During the application process your background will be closely examined. Please review the following background \u201cdisqualifiers.\u201d If you think that any of these apply to you and you have questions, please call the Wichita State University Police Department at (316) 978- 3450 for clarification, or for more information. Must satisfy all requirements as set forth in Kansas Statute 74 \u2013 5605. Must satisfy all requirements as set forth by Wichita State University www.wichita.edu If military service has been rendered your DD214 must reflect a separation code and an Honorable Discharge or an Under Honorable Conditions (General). Uncharacterized discharges are reviewed on a case by case basis. Applicants may be eliminated from the process if they have not fully disclosed ALL information requested. Applicants WILL be eliminated from the process if they have falsified, intentionally misrepresented, or have not been completely truthful on a questionnaire, document, or application as part of the pre-employment process. Applicants will be permanently disqualified for the following if: Has been convicted, expunged, or received diversion on any state, municipality, or federal misdemeanor crime of domestic violence or its equivalent under the Uniform Code of Military Justice. As an adult or juvenile (17 years old or younger), has been involved, convicted, expunged, or on or after July 1, 1995, been placed on diversion by state or federal government for a crime which is a felony (includes sale of illegal or prescription drugs) or its equivalent under the Uniform Code of Military Justice. As an adult or juvenile (17 years old or younger) may not have been convicted of a crime involving an act of dishonesty, to include but not limited to; theft, insufficient funds (check), fraud, false police reports, etc. Applicants may be temporarily disqualified for the following: Must not have used or possessed any felony level drug or controlled substance, i.e. cocaine, heroin, opium, methamphetamine, etc. within the past 10 years of date of application. Convictions, diversions, expungements, or involvement in any misdemeanor crimes of violence, or use of physical force or threats within the past five years of date of application. Convictions, diversions, expungements or involvement in misdemeanor crimes within the past three years of date of application. Convictions, diversions, expungements or involvement in any misdemeanor crimes involving morals, or weapons charges within the past five years of date of application. Must not have used, bought, or possessed marijuana, LSD, hashish, mushrooms, K 2, peyote, ecstasy, etc., within the past three years of date of application. Must not have used, bought, or possessed illegal or non \u2013 prescriptive steroids within the past three years of date of application. Must not have been convicted of, plead guilty or no contest to, or been diverted on a serious traffic violation within the past three years of date of application. Serious traffic violations to include, but not limited to vehicular homicide, DUI, reckless driving, hit and run, and eluding a police officer. Must not have received three moving violations during the last twelve months or been involved in two accidents for which they were at fault during the past twelve months. Must not have been convicted, taken diversion, plead guilty or no contest to an MIP (minor in possession of alcohol) or MIC (minor in consumption) within the past twelve months of date of application. Must not be currently charged with, under indictment, or on probation for any criminal activity other than minor traffic violations. If previous law enforcement experience has been rendered, must not have a sustained violation of dishonesty to include but not limited to, lying, falsifying reports or documents, illegally obtaining narcotics, courtroom testimony/credibility For the purposes of this application process \u201cconviction\u201d includes rendering of judgement by a military court martial pursuant to the uniform code of military justice, by a court of the United States or by a court of competent jurisdiction in any state, whether or not expunged; and any diversion agreement entered into for a misdemeanor crime of domestic violence and any diversion agreement entered into on or after July 1, 1995, for a felony. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to inspect and/or surveil materials, equipment, reports, and/or incidents and identify any errors, needs and/or determining factors. Ability to drive state vehicle. Ability to position self to perform safety and security actions determined by police methods and procedures. Ability to use tools, equipment, and technology necessary to do the job. This includes dexterity in instrument manipulation. Additional Physical Requirement: Medium Work: Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally and/or up to 20 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force to constantly move objects. Apply Now First Name (required) f66cf7e8 Last Name (required) 78dd2604 Email (required) e93424ec Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 461b2d6f Last Name (required) df168d44 Email (required) ae932e70 Job Alert d463f10d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staff Department(s) WSU Police Department WSU Police Department Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 94899ef6 Last Name (required) a3bd8df6 Email (required) 06f3d2b2 Send This Job To: 8e9b8a4e Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" \u2013 Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) b924df6a Last Name (required) 1ce1f22b Email (required) dd2188b9 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-teaching-professor-main-campus-wichita-kansas-united-states-56acd5e4-d949-4aee-8d45-a9c063829bb1": {"title": "Assistant Teaching Professor, Main Campus", "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor, Main Campus - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Teaching Professor, Main Campus - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Teaching Professor, Main Campus College of Health Professions | Faculty Assistant Teaching Professor, Main Campus 499760 On Site Faculty Department: WSU-AVC School of Nursing Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Starts at $67,000 Work Schedule: Typically M-F 8-5, occasional weekend or evening shift; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The WSU - Ascension Via Christi School of Nursing is accepting applications for a 9-month Assistant Teaching Professor (DNP prepared) to provide instruction of didactic, clinical and/or technologies labs, and teaching/supervision in the undergraduate/graduate program as appropriate by educational preparation. This position will also participate in curriculum development and evaluation and will be expected to maintain academic and professional expertise. Participation in Department, College, and University activities and committees is expected. The nursing program is very robust with a traditional RN program, an RN-BSN completion program, and Masters\u2019 program with a focus on education, and a DNP program with foci in FNP, PMHNP, and AGPNP. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for teaching and service, as set forth by the department and college. Required Education and Experience: Graduate level degree Teaching experience Faculty Requirements DNP (Doctor of Nursing Practice) Valid Kansas State APRN License Valid Kansas State Nursing License Nurse Practitioner Certificate Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Excellent interpersonal skills Excellent verbal and written communication skills Computer competency Knowledge of clinical practice Additional Information: WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position \u2013 Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators \u2013 Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Medium Work: Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally and/or up to 20 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force to constantly move objects. Apply Now First Name (required) afdb8ea4 Last Name (required) f938aa87 Email (required) 2c75fde3 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) ba388dd0 Last Name (required) ae3392e5 Email (required) 25e9ebc8 Job Alert 258d4a17 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your