 the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties \u2022 Answer and direct incoming phone calls in a courteous and professional manner \u2022 Warmly welcome and assist visitors; check in guests and notify appropriate staff of arrivals \u2022 Respond to general inquiries and provide basic information about the college \u2022 Sort and distribute incoming mail to faculty and staff \u2022 Monitor and restock office supplies as needed \u2022 Help maintain a clean, organized, and welcoming office environment \u2022 Provide administrative support and assist with special projects as assigned Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements \u2022 Must be eligible for Federal Work-Study \u2022 Minimum GPA of 2.5 \u2022 Availability to work 10\u201315 hours per week between Monday\u2013Friday, 8:00 AM\u20135:00 PM \u2022 Strong communication and customer service skills \u2022 Dependable, detail-oriented, and able to work both independently and as part of a team \u2022 Self-motivated with a strong work ethic and initiative \u2022 Ability to manage multiple tasks and prioritize effectively \u2022 Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite; willingness to learn new systems \u2022 Prior phone or office experience is helpful; training will be provided Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Additional Information Selection will be based on work-study eligibility, schedule availability, and the ability to follow application instructions. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now