eking experience working directly with students to promote academic success. Job Summary A Graduate Staff Assistant (GSA) assistants university service and academic units in either non-teaching or non-research activities. Specific duties of the GSA vary widely, depending on the administrative or academic unit to which they are assigned, but should be at a level to make use of their education and abilities. Job Duties Meet individually with students to assess academic success needs and identify areas for growth. Assist students in developing effective study strategies and learning techniques. Support students in creating systems for organization, time management, and task prioritization. Provide accountability and follow-up regarding academic goals and action plans. Help students develop semester plans, study schedules, and academic routines. Collaborate with TRIO staff regarding student support needs and referrals. Maintain appropriate documentation of participant contacts and services. Assist with workshops and presentations related to academic success and study skills. Participate in training and professional development activities as assigned. Required Education Bachelor's degree Required Experience To be eligible for an assistantship, students must be admitted to a degree program in either full or conditional standing. Students admitted on probation or placed on academic probation following admission may be eligible for assistantship awards under certain circumstances. Preferred Qualifications Current graduate student in Education, Counseling, Student Affairs, Psychology, Organizational Leadership, Social Work, or a related field. Strong interpersonal and communication skills. Excellent organizational and time-management skills. Ability to establish rapport with a diverse student population. Experience mentoring, tutoring, teaching, coaching, or supporting students preferred. Commitment to supporting student success and educational attainment. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) dce08123 Last Name (required) a7c68bf5 Email (required) fa4dea6b Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 58a9b4a3 Last Name (required) e18a24c2 Email (required) 95c4712f Job Alert 990b296d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Strategic Engagement & Planning Strategic Engagement & Planning Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) a8e3aada Last Name (required) 35cbcd94 Email (required) 2d3d441d Send This Job To: d2272e83 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message 