rvices, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) d8365384 Last Name (required) 82b32509 Email (required) 607c359f Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/temporary-assistant-educator-assistant-teaching-professor-educational-psychology-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Temporary Assistant Educator/Assistant Teaching Professor - Educational Psychology", "description": "Temporary Assistant Educator/Assistant Teaching Professor - Educational Psychology - Wichita, Kansas, United States Temporary Assistant Educator/Assistant Teaching Professor - Educational Psychology - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Temporary Assistant Educator/Assistant Teaching Professor - Educational Psychology College of Education | Faculty Temporary Assistant Educator/Assistant Teaching Professor - Educational Psychology 499811 On Site Faculty Department: Counseling, Educational Leadership, Educational and School Psychology (CLES) Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $ 32,500 for Spring semester Work Schedule: Monday - Friday - afternoon and evening classes; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Counseling, Educational Leadership, Educational and School Psychology (CLES) department is accepting applications for a temporary, non-tenure track position to provides graduate instruction, student advising, and dissertation support, while contributing to curriculum development, faculty collaboration, and institutional service. This position is needed for the Spring 2027 semester beginning January 4, 2027. There is potential for the appointment to be extended through the 2027/2028 academic year. The position would be hired as an Assistant Educator or Assistant Teaching Professor based on the selected candidate\u2019s education and experience. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for teaching and service, as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties \u2022 Teach graduate courses in Educational Psychology and doctoral-level research methods. \u2022 Advise and mentor graduate students regarding academic progress, research development, and degree completion. \u2022 Serve on and/or chair doctoral dissertation committees and provide research-methodology support. \u2022 Contribute to curriculum planning, program operations, and student recruitment and retention efforts. \u2022 Collaborate with faculty across the Ph.D. in Education and Behavioral Studies. \u2022 Participate in appropriate departmental, college, and university service activities. Required Education and Experience: Graduate level degree Teaching experience Faculty Requirements Assistant Educator - graduate degree in Educational Psychology or a closely related field Assistant Teaching Professor - terminal degree in Educational Psychology or a closely related field Please note that the degree must be completed prior to January 2027 Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Evidence of effective teaching or the potential for effective teaching at the graduate level. Ability to teach in multiple instructional formats, including in-person, hybrid, and online courses. Commitment to supporting graduate students from varied academic, professional, and personal backgrounds. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, and university partners. Demonstrated expertise in quantitative research methods, with the ability to teach graduate-level quantitative methods courses and serve on dissertation committees involving quantitative research. Preferred Qualifications: Earned doctorate in Educational Psychology or a closely related field. Preference may be given to candidates with graduate preparation or demonstrated expertise in quantitative research methodology, learning and cognition, measurement, program evaluation, or a related area. Experience teaching graduate-level Educational Psychology or research-methods courses. Experience advising or mentoring master\u2019s or doctoral students. Experience serving on dissertation committees or supporting dissertation research. Experience teaching in online or hybrid formats. Evidence of scholarly activity, applied research, or interdisciplinary collaboration. Experience working within a doctoral program or research-intensive university environment Preferred License/Certifications/Training: No professional license or certification is required. Relevant training or certification in quantitative analysis, qualitative research, mixed methods, program evaluation, assessment, or online instruction is preferred. Additional Information: This position is for the Spring 2027 semester with the potential to extend into the 2027-2028 academic year. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position \u2013 Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators \u2013 Frequent 60-90% Apply Now First Name (required) fb030225 Last Name (required) 51e254b7 Email (required) 4cad6c4f Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 89e47b24 Last Name (required) 5c3f7787 Email (required) 8529ed6e Job Alert 5efa0029 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Education College of Education Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message 