ed States Health Professions Tutor, TRIO STEM Student Support Services - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Health Professions Tutor, TRIO STEM Student Support Services Strategic Engagement & Planning | Student Health Professions Tutor, TRIO STEM Student Support Services 499852 Student Department TRIO STEM Student Support Services Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $12.00 per hour, 10 hrs a week Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story The Health Professions Tutor provides high quality academic support to undergraduate participants in the federally funded TRIO STEM Student Support Services Program who are pursuing pre health and health professions pathways, including nursing, pre medicine, pre dental, pre pharmacy, dental hygiene, and other allied health programs. The tutor helps students master demanding science and health coursework, build study habits that hold up in rigorous programs, and grow the confidence they need to stay on track toward professional school and licensure. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Provide individual and small group tutoring in pre health and health professions courses such as Anatomy and Physiology, Microbiology, General Biology, General and Organic Chemistry, Biochemistry, Medical Terminology, and other course needs that arise. Help students understand key concepts, work through problems, and apply course content to clinical and real world health scenarios. Teach study strategies suited to health sciences coursework, including memorization techniques, concept mapping, lab practical preparation, and approaches to high stakes exams. Maintain accurate tutoring session records and communicate student progress or concerns to the Tutor Coordinator. Participate in tutor training and program events as scheduled. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements Minimum Sophomore standing; maintain a minimum GPA of 3.0; has achieved a grade of \u201cB\u201d or better in tutored courses. Major in a health professions field (such as Nursing, Dental Hygiene Health Sciences, Biology, Biomedical Sciences, or a pre health track). Prior tutoring, teaching, mentoring, or peer\u2011education experience. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications Experience supporting first\u2011generation, low\u2011income, or students with disabilities. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 019dc843 Last Name (required) 518274ee Email (required) 4a9fa2ba Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) c9daa0af Last Name (required) 39e78d63 Email (required) 00429a0d Job Alert a1ecbb0a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create