ssistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) efa8697b Last Name (required) 8cfdb25c Email (required) 7b7a6e6e Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-director-trio-communication-upward-bound-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Director- TRIO Communication Upward Bound", "description": "Assistant Director- TRIO Communication Upward Bound - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Director- TRIO Communication Upward Bound - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Director- TRIO Communication Upward Bound Strategic Engagement & Planning | Academic/Student Support, Staff Assistant Director- TRIO Communication Upward Bound 499777 Academic/Student Support Staff Department: TRIO-Communication Upward Bound Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Salary set $45,000/yr Work Schedule: Generally Mon-Fri 8:00AM-5:00PM, regular weekends and some evenings; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story You can talk career goals with a school administrator, coordinate a program with university partners, and then turn around and connect with a room full of high school students. You know how to read the room, meet people where they are, and make connections that stick. Working with students, families, schools, and university partners, you\u2019ll help create experiences that make college and future opportunities feel more accessible to the students you serve. You\u2019ll build relationships throughout the school and community, collaborate with other TRIO programs and university departments, and help shape an academic-year curriculum that keeps students engaged, curious, and moving forward. High school students don\u2019t always respond to a formal presentation or a one-size-fits-all approach. You\u2019re comfortable bringing personality, creativity, and a little playful energy into your work while keeping your goals clear and your professionalism intact. You can meet students on their level without losing sight of the bigger picture. You\u2019re also someone who can build rapport quickly with students and their families. You understand that trust comes from being approachable, following through, and making people feel seen and heard, not just through showing up with information to deliver. You\u2019re organized enough to turn ideas into plans, flexible enough to adapt when those plans need to change, and people-focused enough to know that the best programs are built around the students they serve. Apply now for this exciting role! Job Summary Manages assigned college readiness and/or retention program(s) to meet business objectives. Oversees the day-to-day program activities which may include project schedules, budget tracking and development, recruiting, and project and/or program administration. Essential Functions Collaborates with senior leaders to develop program goals and infrastructure to align with defined business strategy. Creates new or troubleshoots and improves upon existing processes, procedures or systems to meet program goals. Manages program through creation of program plans, grant proposals, management tools and/or reporting capabilities. Performs project research and develops plans to effectively use program resources. Develops metrics to measure program success against program goals. Manages, recruits, trains and/or leads cross-functional teams and ensures resources are appropriately assigned to meet program goals. Recommends program or project budget according to needs. Monitors and adjusts project and program plans as resource requirements change. Communicates and documents program quality outcomes and progress metrics to senior program leaders. Regularly contacts participants, counselors, and partners to ensure program success. Addresses and resolves major or complex issues to ensure program goals remain on track. Job Duties Attend field trips with high school students Facilitate summer programs Creation of curriculum for programs Required Education and Experience: Qualifications for this position are strictly defined by the approved grant proposal. See the education qualifications in the \"Additional Information for Posting\" section below. Required License/Certifications/Training: None Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Familiar with college access, admissions, financial aid, scholarships, and career readiness processes, including advising, student support services & post-secondary educational systems. Understands educational challenges faced by first-generation, low-income, and underrepresented student populations. Familiar with student engagement strategies as well as effective presentation and facilitation skills. Knowledgeable related to curriculum, curriculum resources &/or delivery of information to audiences. Ability to plan, implement, and evaluate educational programs and student development activities. Knowledge of community resources, educational partnerships, and outreach practices. Excellent oral and written communication skills with students, families, school personnel, and community partners. Strong organizational skills to coordinate activities, events, and student services. Motivate, mentor, and inspire high school students to pursue postsecondary education. Ability to work independently while managing multiple priorities and deadlines. Strong commitment to educational equity, student success, and fostering pathways to higher education. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working with TRIO, GEAR UP, college access, or educational outreach programs serving first-generation, low-income, and underrepresented students. Advising and mentoring high school students, coordinating college preparation activities, and supporting postsecondary enrollment initiatives. Experience developing partnerships with K-12 schools, community organizations, and higher education institutions, along with proficiency in program management, student data tracking, and compliance reporting. Additional Information: Required Education: Bachelor's degree or higher in education administration, communication, or related field. Required Experience: Working with TRIO participants or similar youth, and previous supervisory experience. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to travel in a vehicle for distances including but not limited to across city, county, and state. Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) 824fdfc2 Last Name (required) 58a6a248 Email (required) 97a9ce5a Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 9c97b331 Last Name (required) 181482dd Email (required) baf81eaa Job Alert 313e5283 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic/Student Support Staff Academic/Student Support Staff Department(s) Strategic Engagement & Planning Strategic Engagement & Planning Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 753c1aab Last Name (required) 83022849 Email (required) 3e317749 Send This Job To: 362408ae Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time