t messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/telecommunications-technician-it-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Telecommunications Technician- IT", "description": "Telecommunications Technician- IT - Wichita, Kansas, United States Telecommunications Technician- IT - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Telecommunications Technician- IT Information Technology | Information Technology, Staff Telecommunications Technician- IT 499782 Information Technology Staff Department: IT Services - Telecommunications Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range begins at $20.48/hr, adjustments determined by qualifications Work Schedule: Monday - Friday, 8AM - 5PM; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a \u201cU.S. Citizen\u201d. Job Story We are looking for a versatile specialist who can flex between hands-on troubleshooting, behind-the-scenes configuration, and supportive team collaboration like a seasoned pro. Do you thrive in environments where the network never sleeps and neither does your curiosity? If someone asked your work style, you\u2019d say \u201cThink Mandalorian meets Matrix operator \u2014 calm, resourceful, adaptable. This is the way.\u201d If you\u2019re someone who likes your work like your Wi-Fi \u2014 fast, reliable, and always on \u2014 keep reading. We need a kind of person who can be: Independent Operator \u2014 60\u201370% of your day is self-directed and you love it Team Conduit \u2014 you offer help as fast as you ask for it Mode-Switch Master \u2014 lead or backup, whatever the project calls for Doc Ninja \u2014 document solutions & build SOPs that future teammates will thank you for Communication Router \u2014 meet users at any knowledge level, bringing clarity to their world Cool Under Latency \u2014 things glitch? You don\u2019t; you pivot with it & keep things moving Self-Starter with Initiative \u2014 you don\u2019t wait for tasks; you queue them up Support and maintain campus telecom and network systems. Troubleshoot issues with the calm confidence \u2014 you\u2019ve rebooted entire situations, so you got this. Document everything from work orders to new SOPs (because if it\u2019s not documented, did it even happen?). Collaborate with a tight-knit tech crew while still owning your workload and making independent decisions. Occasionally work a flexible modified or non-traditional schedule \u2014 Infrastructure upgrades occur in the maintenance window, typically post-business hours for optimal uptime. Participate in an On-Call Trouble Tech rotation - tech emergencies don\u2019t punch a clock. Hit \u201cApply Now\" so you can answer the call! Job Summary Performs basic tasks relating to telecommunications monitoring, operations, installation, and/or maintenance. Essential Functions Installs and maintains structured cabling infrastructures and all related hardware. Performs basic maintenance on telephone and network connections to locate issue and make necessary repairs. Installs and services telephone and network equipment, including voice gateways, telephone end points, network switches, and wireless access points. Provides documentation to work performed, cable plant infrastructure, and inventory of connections. Job Duties Install and program phone, voicemail, and E911 information for end users. Installs, terminates, and tests category cabling in a wide range of campus environments. Works with other members of ITS for network programming, desktop support, and camera support. Some outdoor work required to perform utilities locates. Participate in an on-call trouble rotation to provide 24/7 IT support and ability to work after hours for scheduled network maintenance and upgrades. Qualified candidates are required to operate manual transmission vehicles regularly as a part of travel for work needs. Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent None Required License/Certifications/Training: Valid Kansas Drivers License Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Analyze data, recognize problems, and draw logical conclusions Use electronic test and repair equipment to test and repair telecommunications equipment and systems Clean and handle delicate electronic equipment Communicate with users of all knowledge levels, with clarity & professionalism as well as actively listen for instructions &/or issues Effectively communicate orally and in writing to convey technical information in non-technical terms Use a Windows based PC to organize work, generate records & reports, and configure equipment Control and configure legacy and IP enabled telecommunications equipment using data network communication and legacy phone infrastructure. Qualified candidates are required to operate manual transmission vehicles regularly as a part of travel for work needs. Preferred Qualifications: Avaya PBX software experience. Pinnacle software experience or equivalent ticket system Fluke Versive testing and certifying experience. Fiber optic cleaning and fusion splicing experience. Installing large cabling projects from beginning to end. Visio experience MDF/IDF stack replacements Preferred License/Certifications/Training: BICSI Certification Fiber Optic Splicing Certification Additional Information: Qualified candidate must be able to work non-traditional work schedule including regular on call rotations for 2 week timeframes. Qualified candidates are required to operate manual transmission vehicles regularly as a part of travel for work needs. Physical Requirements: Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to position self for inspection, construction or maintenance of equipment and/or buildings including confined, elevated and loud noise spaces. Ability to move, transport, and/or deliver items, supplies, or equipment. Ability to move or traverse across campus, within buildings and offices, and/or across external environments. Ability to ascend and descend ladders and/or stairs. Ability to drive state vehicle. Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) ea4555f2 Last Name (required) b20f476c Email (required) b9d5a91f Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) de8fd013 Last Name (required) bdb73be1 Email (required) 20dc7618 Send This Job To: 5bf215ff Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" \u2013 Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 1b034620 Last Name (required) fc0d0caa Email (required) b3672b51 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/resource-lending-specialist-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Resource Lending Specialist", "description": "Resource Lending Specialist - Wichita, Kansas, United States Resource Lending Specialist - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Resource Lending Specialist Library | Staff Resource Lending Specialist 499764 Staff Department: University Libraries Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Part Time Pay: Range begins at $17.73 per hour Work Schedule: 20 hours (average) per week, schedule may vary. See Additional Information below. Work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Do you like a fast-paced environment with a variety of tasks to accomplish? Are you a problem solver who is highly organized, detail oriented, adept at managing multiple priorities and skilled at improving processes? University Libraries has openings for two Resource Lending Specialists to cover afternoons, evenings, and weekends. The Resource Lending Specialist is part of Access Services, the forward-facing unit of the WSU Libraries responsible for connecting our campus community to information resources that support intellectual discovery, scholarship, creative activity, and innovation. Resource Lending Specialists help ensure that borrowers \u2013 who can be individuals or other libraries\u2013 receive what is requested efficiently and cost effectively, all while helping fulfill these requests on a busy service desk at the WSU Libraries. This role will navigate multiple Library software systems to maintain accurate records, troubleshoot typical issues with printers and scanners, and work with Microsoft Office products and cloud-based office software. When issues arise with requested Library materials, Resource Lending Specialists identify the source of the issue and suggest potential solutions. If you want to help provide a robust and accessible Library collection that meets the evolving needs of the university community, please apply! Job Summary Performs a variety of professional and administrative duties that facilitate the operations of a function(s), program(s), and/or department(s). Essential Functions Supports the programs and services provided by the department(s) by performing varied or related processes which may include creating and maintaining databases and websites, monitoring, facilitating, and enforcing compliance with established criteria, guidelines and standards, etc. May coordinate, attend, prepare materials for and/or take minutes at meetings and special events. May prepare or assist in the preparation of budgets, grant applications, proposals, status reports and/or financial statements. May identify and pursue ways to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of administrative procedures used by students, faculty, visitors and staff. May order and maintain sufficient inventory of office supplies and equipment. May be assigned to lead, assist, coordinate or support special projects as needed. Job Duties Enter or modify data in databases and applications Search databases and the internet for bibliographic data or other data in support of library systems (ex. Catalog) or applications Interpret and apply policies, best practices and procedures Attend department and unit meetings, training sessions and special events Maintain data on unit activities and prepare routine reports Identify and report on recommendations for continuous improvement of the unit\u2019s efficiency and effectiveness Monitor unit supplies Order office supplies as necessary Participate in unit and departmental projects Other duties as assigned Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent Two (2) years of experience in general office, clerical, administrative support or related field Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Demonstrated experience working in databases, including accurate data entry and searching Excellent attention to detail; ability to maintain high level of quality Ability to enter metadata using established standards and best practices Demonstrated excellent oral and written communication skills in English; strong interpersonal skills Ability to learn new skills, technology, and computer applications quickly Ability to adapt to new practice and theory Demonstrated experience working well independently and in teams with varied user communities Ability to operate office equipment (including, but not limited to, computers, photocopiers, and scanners) Working knowledge of Microsoft Office Strong customer service orientation Strong problem-solving, organizational and analytical skills Effective web and scholarly database searching Ability to interpret bibliographic data correctly Ability to work in a high production environment Additional Information: Shifts scheduled will be based on chosen candidate's availability with some flexibility offered for course schedules or other recurring obligations. A typical schedule would be 3-5 days per week including weekends; scheduled hours will be afternoons and/or evenings. Closing hours vary throughout the year. Availability to work on Saturday is required. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Additional Physical Requirement: Light Work: Exerting up to 20 pounds of force occasionally and/or negligible amount of force to constantly move objects. Light work involves remaining stationary most of the time. Apply Now First Name (required) ebf409b5 Last Name (required) bb438bf8 Email (required) b4b1dbb3 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 55e73ade Last Name (required) e4afb2f9 Email (required) ef2818e5 Job Alert e3900ed4 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staff Department(s) Library Library Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 3a8d2883 Last Name (required) 2343b468 Email (required) fa47d506 Send This Job To: 99754870 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" \u2013 Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 5c515682 Last Name (required) c06030f4 Email (required) 00fc39b7 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-clinical-psychology-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Clinical Psychology", "description": "Assistant Professor, Clinical Psychology - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor, Clinical Psychology - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor, Clinical Psychology College of Liberal Arts & Sciences | Faculty Assistant Professor, Clinical Psychology 499795 On Site Faculty Department: Department of Psychology Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $70,000.00 Work Schedule: Monday - Friday, 8am to 5pm; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Psychology Department at Wichita State University seeks to hire a 9-month tenure-track, Assistant Professor in Clinical Psychology to begin August 2, 2027. We welcome applications from individuals with a cognitive-behavioral orientation as broadly-defined. We are open to all areas of research and clinical interests, but are especially interested in scholars who could contribute in one or more of the following areas: integrated behavioral healthcare in the primary care setting, family systems approaches, and third-wave behavioral therapies. Applicants should be PhD graduates of an APA- accredited program in clinical psychology, (completed prior to August of 2027), licensed (or licensed-eligible) as a psychologist in the state of Kansas, and have a strong record of peer-reviewed publications. The Clinical Psychology PhD Program at Wichita State is fully-accredited by the American Psychological Association and embraces a scientist\u2013practitioner model, within a clinical\u2013community framework. The department has three Ph.D. programs in clinical, community, and human factors psychology, as well as a large undergraduate student body. The department is research oriented and has an expectation for faculty to seek external funding. Wichita State also has an in-house clinical psychology training clinic that serves the greater Wichita area. Salary is $70,000.00. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels, mentor Ph.D. students, conduct research, apply for grants, publish in peer reviewed journals. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements PhD graduate of an APA- accredited program in clinical psychology. Degree should be completed prior to August of 2027. Experience publishing in peer-reviewed journals Required License/Certifications/Training: Licensed (or licensed-eligible) as a psychologist in the state of Kansas. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Training in clinical psychology Ability to contribute to building an inclusive and welcoming environment for colleagues and students Ability to work effectively in a highly collaborative, engaging, and dynamic environment comprised of individuals with a range of backgrounds, skills, and perspectives. Ability to attract external funding Commitment to teach both graduate and undergraduate courses Additional Information: Please complete the Faculty Profile including the names and contact information of three (3) references and upload the following documents: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Statement of research philosophy Description of how you work to create a cooperative and welcoming work place. (attach as Faculty Document 1) Review of applications will begin November 20, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. For questions, please contact Samantha Slade at samantha.slade@wichita.edu WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position \u2013 Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators \u2013 Frequent 60-90% Apply Now First Name (required) d6dc725f Last Name (required) 71dc2751 Email (required) 0b856bb1 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 568dbd71 Last Name (required) 54c0f283 Email (required) 4461e1f5 Job Alert f4a363be Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Liberal Arts & Sciences College of Liberal Arts & Sciences Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 7f77eb34 Last Name (required) f090fe1d Email (required) 06782ad3 Send This Job To: 8ac57d08 Sha