p one of the nation\u2019s leading research environments running smoothly. We\u2019re looking for a proactive, organized administrative professional who thrives in a fast\u2011moving setting and enjoys supporting meaningful work. If you\u2019re someone who takes initiative, communicates clearly, and excels at managing details, this on\u2011site role at Wichita State University could be a great fit! Job Summary Performs a variety of professional and administrative duties that facilitate the operations of a function(s), program(s), and/or department(s). Essential Functions Supports the programs and services provided by the department(s) by performing varied or related processes which may include creating and maintaining databases and websites, monitoring, facilitating, and enforcing compliance with established criteria, guidelines and standards, etc. May coordinate, attend, prepare materials for and/or take minutes at meetings and special events. May prepare or assist in the preparation of budgets, grant applications, proposals, status reports and/or financial statements. May identify and pursue ways to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of administrative procedures used by students, faculty, visitors and staff. May order and maintain sufficient inventory of supplies and equipment, as needed. May be assigned to lead, assist, coordinate or support special projects as needed. Job Duties Coordinates meetings and events which may include, but is not limited to, catering, guestlists, entertainment, supplies, reservations, and set up. Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent Two (2) years of experience in general office, clerical, administrative support or related field Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Strong interpersonal and customer service skills, with the ability to consistently and positively interact with internal and external partners. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Expertise with MS Office and other office technology. Ability to document information in a timely manner with high degree of accuracy. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to travel in a vehicle for distances including but not limited to across city, county, and state. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Apply Now First Name (required) c828428e Last Name (required) ca49f27e Email (required) ea5c2af8 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 4ccf9d1e Last Name (required) e91d51c4 Email (required) 6e32aedf Job Alert f11fcefe Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Office/Administrative Support Staff Office/Administrative Support Staff Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 20df3564 Last Name (required) bde8c043 Email (required) 4b592017 Send This Job To: 82e98ea5 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By su