m to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 91d424e9 Last Name (required) ec267eb9 Email (required) 2e92d62b Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/reverse-engineering-lab-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Reverse Engineering Lab Student Assistant", "description": "Reverse Engineering Lab Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States Reverse Engineering Lab Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Reverse Engineering Lab Student Assistant NIAR Institute | Student Reverse Engineering Lab Student Assistant 495423 Student Department NIAR Reverse Engineering Lab Campus Location Wichita, KS - Other Wichita Location Hire Type Part Time Pay $15 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a \u201cU.S. Citizen\u201d. Job Story The Reverse Engineering Lab is looking for a student assistant to assist with the 3D scanning and processing of scan data. 3D Scanning equipment will be used in obtaining accurate 3D data from various aircraft to support programs within NIAR. There will also be tasks of reading CAD Drawings to be able to locate components and properly position scan data in CAD software. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties \u00b7 Operating 3D Scanners and diligently capturing the geometry of aircraft parts. \u00b7 Work may contain some lifting and moving heavy parts up to 50 lbs. \u00b7 Working with 3D Scan data, processing, and positioning pieces in software relative to adjacent aircraft parts. \u00b7 Report daily activities to the supervisor at the end of each shift worked. \u00b7 All equipment and software training needed for this job are provided through the lob. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Additional Requirements \u00b7 Excel spreadsheet experience \u00b7 Excellent written and oral communication is a must \u00b7 Must be detailed oriented \u00b7 Must be able to work independently and in groups \u00b7 20hrs per Week required and up to 30hrs per Week allowed during regular semesters \u00b7 Must have reliable transportation to and from work daily \u00b7 Working in 3D modeling software, Reading drawings, blueprint reading Additional Information for Posting The job position will require both manual operation of various scanning equipment and software processing tools of scan data. Most scanning will require being on your feet most of the day and actively maneuvering around large items. Some scanning will require positioning scanners under, inside, and above aircraft and can require a good amount of physical activity to lift and move scanners and accessories into location and sometimes be in tight spaces. The position will also require computer skills for processing scan data and keeping the data organized. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phones, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) d11bb6b4 Last Name (required) 1cd99216 Email (required) 4057df4d Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 9d0c00d9 Last Name (required) 784a40e8 Email (required) cefe909f Job Alert 1404b2cf Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone E