0.50 - $12.00 per hour, depending on experience Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Dependent on Class Schedule, during Office hours of Mon-Fri, 8AM-5PM Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story The ITS Network group administers support for data and network services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of wired and wireless network connections and supporting services throughout Wichita State\u2019s main and satellite campuses. This position is a part time position. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Job Purpose: The ITS Network Student Assistant is an entry-level position. The person in this position will perform routine tasks, participate in projects, and gain technical working skills. To apply for this position, you MUST have excellent Microsoft Office skills. You should know how to open and modify a Word document, enter formulas in Excel and navigate through Outlook. Job responsibilities: \u00b7 Audit network support services \u00b7 Unbox, mount, and prepare networking equipment for installation \u00b7 Troubleshoot network connectivity issues \u00b7 Document network processes \u00b7 Errands for the department \u00b7 Audit network support services \u00b7 Monitoring and updating ticketing system Equipment used: \u00b7 Computer \u00b7 Telephone \u00b7 Calculator Qualifications: \u00b7 Typing, computer skills, office knowledge \u00b7 Microsoft Office experience \u00b7 Ability to work independently \u00b7 Demonstrated ability to learn Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications \u00b7 Experience in Linux and MacOS operating systems \u00b7 Experience using Microsoft Office and learning from an advanced user \u00b7 Ability to interact effectively with customers \u00b7 Knowledge of office responsibilities \u00b7 Customer service experience Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 0afedbeb Last Name (required) a52cbc17 Email (required) c5fc1022 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) caabdf8e Last Name (required) 4c077eec Email (required) 2abd632c Job Alert ad8cddba Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Information Technology Information Technology Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about wo