cluding Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) d8180f74 Last Name (required) c8e51286 Email (required) b305e98c Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-researcher-wichita-kansas-united-states-2ce72a69-3f6b-489c-af7b-4a1b3a0b511c": {"title": "Postdoctoral Researcher", "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher - Wichita, Kansas, United States Postdoctoral Researcher - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Researcher College of Engineering | Staff Postdoctoral Researcher 498265 Staff Department: Mechanical Engineering Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Salary range is $45,000 to $50,000 annually Work Schedule: Generally 8am - 5pm, Monday - Friday. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Department of Mechanical Engineering at Wichita State University invites applications for a postdoctoral researcher position focusing on the design, synthesis, and characterization of advanced inorganic nanomaterials for wastewater treatment, energy harvest, and environmental engineering-centric applications. This position is part of an NSF-funded program, and the successful candidate is expected to engage in a broad range of research and academic activities supporting the program\u2019s goals. Key responsibilities include: \u2022 Design and synthesis of advanced inorganic nanomaterials (e.g., transition-metal-based nanoparticles) by adopting state-of-the-art chemical and physical techniques. \u2022 Structural characterization of synthetic inorganic nanomaterials through modern instrumentation techniques (e.g., XRD, BET, XPS, SEM, and TEM). \u2022 Development of functional membranes incorporated with enabling inorganic nanomaterials for wastewater treatment and energy harvest. \u2022 Collaboration with the modeling and simulation team on the design, engineering, and optimization of functional membranes and associated integrated application systems. Job Summary Administers a variety of studies within scientific or scholarly area of expertise. Performs research study analyses, writes reports and publications, and coordinates with others in carrying out research. Essential Functions Participates with others on research projects. Builds upon previous or concurrent research. Develops research projects through a variety of methods, collaborations and analyses. Gathers data and develops statistical analyses to assimilate and interpret research results. Resolves data and/or research issues. Researches, writes, and communicates research progress and outcomes. Maintains research facility data, equipment, and specimens to ensure compliance with applicable rules and regulations. May supervise the work of others. Job Duties The job duties include: conducting experimental syntheses of inorganic nanomaterials, characterizing synthetic nanomaterials, and fabricating functional membranes for water/energy applications, performing computational analyses, preparing technical reports, drafting scientific publications, and collaborating with interdisciplinary research team members. Required Education and Experience: Doctorate degree in a related field One (1) year of experience in research, laboratory, scholarly setting, or related field Required License/Certifications/Training: None Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Strong written and verbal communication skills. Logical analysis and critical thinking. Proficient laboratory bench capabilities in materials synthesis and instrumentation characterization. Proven ability to work effectively in large collaborative teams. Preferred Qualifications: PhD earned in materials engineering, chemistry engineering, or a closely related discipline. Academic credentials (peer-reviewed journal publications) in the synthesis and characterization of advanced inorganic nanomaterials. Established expertise in the design, fabrication, and scale-up of functional membranes. Relevant experience in environmental engineering applications in areas such as wastewater treatment and energy harvest. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to use tools, equipment, and technology necessary to do the job. This includes dexterity in instrument manipulation. Ability to move, transport, and/or deliver items, supplies, or equipment. Additional Physical Requirement: Medium Work: Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally and/or up to 20 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force to constantly move objects. Apply Now First Name (required) 6c3ae0d8 Last Name (required) 64dee7a4 Email (required) 9e29bebf Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 0eba4466 Last Name (required) 61750a65 Email (required) 114b4bdc Job Alert 1c1f0fe8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staff Department(s) College of Engineering College of Engineering Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 5084bc08 Last Name (required) e9071142 Email (required) c18b9422 Send This Job To: 017b5cd7 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" \u2013 Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 5198e66c Last Name (required) 012f2d0b Email (required) fc920bf9 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/director-broadcast-maintenance-engineering-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering", "description": "Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering - Wichita, Kansas, United States Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering Academic Affairs Direct | Staff Director Broadcast Maintenance Engineering 499683 Staff Department: KMUW Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Old Town Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Commensurate with experience Work Schedule: 9-5, M-F and on call outside of normal business hours; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Come be the technical leader of our thriving public radio station in Wichita, Kansas. The station is in a historic structure in Old Town, the heart of downtown. Dozens of restaurants, shops, museums, clubs, and breweries are within walking distance, along with live music and public art around each corner. KMUW-FM, Wichita is looking for a Chief Engineer who is a collaborative thinker to work closely with the General Manager and Director of Content. This position will oversee the daily technical broadcast and IT operations. The Chief Engineer is responsible for keeping abreast of changing technologies and upgrades. The role includes maintenance of the station facilities, transmitter site, and nine in-house studios. The role does have support from a part-time assistant production and broadcast engineer. KMUW operates a single 100K watt transmitter with antenna, no translators or repeaters. We recently invested in a new transmitter, studio boards, UPS modules, studio telecom, as well as ENCO and RDS upgrades. Job Summary Provides leadership and strategic direction for the planning, development and implementation of all technical station maintenance, improvement, and system compliance efforts to ensure achievement or quality control objectives, compliance with regulatory agencies, and University goals. Essential Functions \u2022 Provides leadership for and execution of the maintenance and repair of broadcast studio equipment and systems. May supervise work of technicians. \u2022 Leads the continuous improvement of operational capabilities and supports the development of all revenue and audience producing efforts. \u2022 Records and produces live events, ensuring broadcast quality and compliance. \u2022 Provides support for audio, administrative, and industry specific software. \u2022 Develops, implements and maintains policies, objectives, projects and short- and long-range plans to accomplish goals. \u2022 Develops and manages annual engineering budget. \u2022 Maintains up-to-date knowledge and understanding of evolving industry advancements and requirements. Identifies and informs the department of the potential impact of trends and changes. Required Education and Experience: 60 hours of college coursework in media or broadcast engineering. Six (6) years of experience in engineer broadcasting or related field, with two (2) years of experience in a leadership role. An additional 60 hours of college coursework can be substituted for two (2) years of experience Required License/Certifications/Training: Society of Broadcast Engineering (SBE) broadcast technician certification or ability to obtain within 6 months of hire. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: FM Transmitter maintenance, knowledge of high voltage maintenance practices Facility maintenance skills (including but not limited to coordinating contractors) Satellite downlink repair and maintenance Windows and Mac configuration and repair IP and baseband audio setup and troubleshooting Equipment repair to component level Ability to plan, determine costs for and direct a project, including planning and appropriate and complete documentation, delegating assignments, directing contractors and follow-up. Preferred Qualifications: AOIP configuration / maintenance (Axia and STL gear) ENCO automation operation / configuration Some basic programming skills in: JavaScript, PHP, HTML, batch files Server and network switch configuration and maintenance Physical Requirements: Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to position self for inspection, construction or maintenance of equipment and/or buildings including confined, elevated and loud noise spaces. Ability to move, transport, and/or deliver items, supplies, or equipment. Ability to move or traverse across campus, within buildings and offices, and/or across external environments. Ability to ascend and descend ladders and/or stairs. Additional Physical Requirement: Heavy Work: Exerting up to 100 pounds of force occasionally and/or up to 50 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 20 pounds of force to constantly move objects. Be able to lift 60lbs to shoulder height. Comfortable on ladders and roof tops. Able to climb onto satellite dishes. High Voltage in transmitters, loud environment in transmitter building and at concerts, temperature extremes during outside work for maintenance or concert recording. Safely work in the dark during power outages. Apply Now First Name (required) 974e1a78 Last Name (required) 6fc358a3 Email (required) 608be8d8 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 607f7fa7 Last Name (required) abbb9f7a Email (required) 7c9eca71 Job Alert 55618530 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staff Department(s) Academic Affairs Direct Academic Affairs Direct Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 18c12afa Last Name (required) fb5033e8 Email (required) a8f9fe89 Send This Job To: f6001a1e Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" \u2013 Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 094124f0 Last Name (required) f68a3ee9 Email (required) aac67e82 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/robotics-mechanical-engineering-assistant-professor-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Robotics Mechanical Engineering Assistant Professor", "description": "Robotics Mechanical Engineering Assistant Professor - Wichita, Kansas, United States Robotics Mechanical Engineering Assistant Professor - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Robotics Mechanical Engineering Assistant Professor College of Engineering | Faculty Robotics Mechanical Engineering Assistant Professor 499616 On Site Faculty WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Department: Mechanical Engineering Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range beginning $95,000-$110,000/yr, commensurate with qualifications Work Schedule: Dependent on teaching assignment and research program needs.; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Department of Mechanical Engineering in the College of Engineering at Wichita State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Mechanical Engineering (mechanism design/robotics area). We seek an innovative scholar and educator who will contribute to our academic programs and research profile. The successful candidate will be expected to teach undergraduate and graduate courses, develop a productive research program, and provide service to the university and profession. This position is a 9-month appointment with an anticipated start date of Fall 2027. The Department has three-degree programs (one bachelor\u2019s, one master\u2019s, and one PhD program), and three graduate certificate programs. Our undergraduate program is accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET, which means the curriculum has met rigorous benchmarks and goals, as has our graduate programs. Additionally, our department is committed to experience-based instruction and research, so students have the opportunity to engage in paid applied learning experiences and research with our faculty even as undergraduates. Graduates of our programs go on to design products and machines, as well as develop processes for manufacturing. New faculty will find supportive colleagues and opportunities to engage in interdisciplinary initiatives across the university. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Teaching: Develop and teach courses at the undergraduate and/or graduate level in mechanical engineering in mechanism design/robotics. This includes designing curriculum and instructional materials, delivering high-quality instruction in various modalities (in-person, online, or hybrid), and assessing student learning. The faculty member will mentor and advise students, including supervising research projects or theses/dissertation as appropriate, and incorporate applied learning opportunities (e.g. projects with industry or community partners) into the coursework whenever possible. Research/Scholarly Activity: Successful applicants for the position will demonstrate deep expertise and establish and maintain an active research program in one or more of the following topics: mechanism design; robotics and intelligent system design; design and manufacturing of engineered materials systems; design cognition; design collaboration; data science and artificial intelligence in design; immersive design; and design at extreme scales and in extreme environments. The research activity should advance the next generation of engineers and researchers by developing a deep understanding of the design, manufacturing and engineering of devices, products, processes, platforms, materials, organizations, systems, and systems of systems. The design of a modern intelligent system, in which the designers, the artifacts they create, the methods they use to create them, and the environment in which this occurs are all subject to rigorous scientific inquiry, along with the interactions among these elements; is of particular importance. Publishing peer-reviewed scholarly work and disseminating results in academic venues if of great importance. The faculty member is expected to seek external funding (grants or industry collaboration) to support research activities and, where applicable, engage in interdisciplinary projects or partnerships with industry, and advising and supervising undergraduate and graduate students\u2019 thesis and dissertation projects. Excellence in scholarship should be demonstrated by a record of research accomplishments or clear potential for high-quality research output. Service: Participate in service activities within the department, college, and university, as well as in professional organizations. Service duties include committee work, curriculum development, program assessment, student recruitment, and community outreach. The faculty member will contribute to the governance and strategic initiatives of the department and may also engage in service to the broader profession (e.g. reviewing for journals, involvement in academic societies). Other: Fulfill other duties as assigned, in accordance with the faculty member\u2019s talents and departmental needs. All Wichita State faculty are expected to uphold professional and ethical standards in teaching, research, and service. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements Required Education: An earned doctorate (Ph.D.) in Mechanical Engineering or a closely related field is required. Candidates must have completed the requirements for the Ph.D. by the time of appointment. Demonstrated potential for effective teaching in mechanism design; robotics and intelligent system design; and design and manufacturing of engineered materials systems. Evidence may include prior teaching experience, student evaluations, teaching awards, or a teaching philosophy that reflects best practices in instruction. Demonstrated potential for productive research and scholarship. This can be shown by publications, conference presentations, dissertation work, or other scholarly activities indicating the ability to develop an independent research program Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Excellent written and oral communication skills, and the ability to work effectively with colleagues and students. The candidate should be able to collaborate in a collegial academic environment and adapt to the interdisciplinary and applied learning focus of Wichita State. Ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, staff, and external partners in an academic environment. Potential to obtain external research funding, or evidence of previous success in securing grants, contracts, or industry-supported research funding. Ability to develop collaborations as part of a multidisciplinary research teams. Ability to provide instruction curriculum to a variety of learners. Interest in interdisciplinary work or industry collaboration. Preferred Qualifications: Interdisciplinary/Applied Focus: Experience or interest in interdisciplinary work or industry collaboration. For example, a history of working on research projects across disciplines or partnerships with industry and the community (aligned with Wichita State\u2019s emphasis on applied learning and innovation) is desirable. Additional Information: WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. APPLICATION PROCEDURE 1. Cover Letter: A letter of application addressing how the candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience align with the position, including a summary of teaching philosophy and research interests. 2. Teaching Statement: A statement (1-2 pages) describing teaching approach and experience (including course topics the candidate can teach, mentoring experience, and any evidence of teaching effectiveness). 3. Research Statement: A statement (1-3 pages) outlining current research accomplishments and future research plans. Emphasize how these might involve students or connect to interdisciplinary and industry-related opportunities at WSU. Review of applications will begin on November 1, 2026. The start date for this appointment is August 2027. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position \u2013 Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators \u2013 Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" \u2013 Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/autonomous-machines-mechanical-engineering-assistant-professor-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Autonomous Machines Mechanical Engineering Assistant Professor", "description": "Autonomous Machines Mechanical Engineering Assistant Professor - Wichita, Kansas, United States Autonomous Machines Mechanical Engineering Assistant Professor - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Autonomous Machines Mechanical Engineering Assistant Professor College of Engineering | Faculty Autonomous Machines Mechanical Engineering Assistant Professor 499615 On Site Faculty Work Authorization and Immigration Sponsorship Wichita State University may be able to sponsor certain faculty positions for employment-based immigration status where authorized by the hiring department and university policy. Sponsorship eligibility varies by faculty position and will be identified in the individual job posting. For faculty positions eligible for sponsorship, international candidates generally must be eligible for sponsorship in a visa classification compatible with the faculty position. For tenured and tenure-track faculty appointments, visa classifications incompatible with such appointments include F-1 Optional Practical Training (OPT), J-1 Research Scholar, and J-1 Academic Training statuses. Department: Mechanical Engineering Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range beginning $95,000-$110,000/yr, commensurate with qualifications Work Schedule: Dependent on teaching assignment and research program needs.;work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Department of Mechanical Engineering in the College of Engineering invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Mechanical Engineering -Autonomous and Complex Systems, Computational Dynamics area. We seek an innovative scholar and educator who will contribute to our academic programs and research profile. The successful candidate will be expected to teach undergraduate and graduate courses, develop a productive research program, and provide service to the university and profession. This position is a 9-month appointment with an anticipated start date of Fall 2027. The Department has three-degree programs (one bachelor\u2019s, one master\u2019s, and one PhD program), and three graduate certificate programs. Our undergraduate program is accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET, which means the curriculum has met rigorous benchmarks and goals, as has our graduate programs. Additionally, our department is committed to experience-based instruction and research, so students have the opportunity to engage in paid applied learning experiences and research with our faculty even as undergraduates. Graduates of our programs go on to design products and machines, as well as develop processes for manufacturing. New faculty will find supportive colleagues and opportunities to engage in interdisciplinary initiatives across the university. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Teaching: Develop and teach courses at the undergraduate and/or graduate level in mechanical engineering in Autonomous and Complex Systems/Computational Dynamics. This includes designing curriculum and instructional materials, delivering high-quality instruction in various modalities (in-person, online, or hybrid), and assessing student learning. The faculty member will mentor and advise students, including supervising research projects or theses/dissertation as appropriate, and incorporate applied learning opportunities (e.g. projects with industry or community partners) into the coursework whenever possible. Research/Scholarly Activity: Successful applicants for the position will demonstrate deep expertise and establish and maintain an active research program in one or more of the following topics: Autonomous and Complex Systems, Computational Dynamics, Vehicle Dynamics and Control, (Vibro)-Acoustics and Noise Control and Autonomous Matter and Machines. The research activity should advance the next generation of engineers and researchers by developing a deep understanding of the dynamics of complex engineering systems focusing on creating advanced methods for control, estimation, planning, and learning that enable intelligent autonomous systems to operate safely, efficiently, and adaptively in dynamic environments. These foundational capabilities are essential for the autonomous technologies of the future, to design and realize smart autonomous systems that address critical challenges in industry and society, fostering innovation, sustainability, and improved quality of life. Publishing peer-reviewed scholarly work and disseminating results in academic venues if of great importance. The faculty member is expected to seek external funding (grants or industry collaboration) to support research activities and, where applicable, engage in interdisciplinary projects or partnerships with industry, and advising and supervising undergraduate and graduate students\u2019 thesis and dissertation projects. Excellence in scholarship should be demonstrated by a record of research accomplishments or clear potential for high-quality research output. Service : Participate in service activities within the department, college, and university, as well as in professional organizations. Service duties include committee work, curriculum development, program assessment, student recruitment, and community outreach. The faculty member will contribute to the governance and strategic initiatives of the department and may also engage in service to the broader profession (e.g. reviewing for journals, involvement in academic societies). Other: Fulfill other duties as assigned, in accordance with the faculty member\u2019s talents and departmental needs. All Wichita State faculty are expected to uphold professional and ethical standards in teaching, research, and service. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements An earned doctorate (Ph.D.) in Mechanical Engineering or a closely related field is required. Candidates must have completed the requirements for the Ph.D. by May 2027. Applicants who are at an advanced stage of their doctoral studies will be considered if they provide strong evidence that all degree requirements will be completed prior to July 2027. Demonstrated potential for effective teaching in (computational/experimental) dynamic analysis, and design of complex multi-physics, multi-disciplinary, and cyber-physical engineering systems. Evidence may include prior teaching experience, student evaluations, teaching awards, or a teaching philosophy that reflects best practices in instruction. Demonstrated potential for productive research and scholarship. This can be shown by publications, conference presentations, dissertation work, or other scholarly activities indicating the ability to develop an independent research program. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Excellent written and oral communication skills, and the ability to work effectively with colleagues and students. The candidate should be able to collaborate in a collegial academic environment and adapt to the interdisciplinary and applied learning focus of Wichita State. Ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, staff, and external partners in an academic environment. Potential to obtain external research funding, or evidence of previous success in securing grants, contracts, or industry-supported research funding. Ability to develop collaborations as part of a multidisciplinary research teams. Ability to provide instruction curriculum to a variety of learners. Interest in interdisciplinary work or industry collaboration. Preferred Qualifications: Interdisciplinary/Applied Focus: Experience or interest in interdisciplinary work or industry collaboration. For example, a history of working on research projects across disciplines or partnerships with industry and the community (aligned with Wichita State\u2019s emphasis on applied learning and innovation) is desirable. Additional Information: Work Authorization and Immigration Sponsorship Wichita State University may be able to sponsor certain faculty positions for employment-based immigration status where authorized by the hiring department and university policy. Sponsorship eligibility varies by faculty position and will be identified in the individual job posting. For faculty positions eligible for sponsorship, international candidates generally must be eligible for sponsorship in a visa classification compatible with the faculty position. For tenured and tenure-track faculty appointments, visa classifications incompatible with such appointments include F-1 Optional Practical Training (OPT), J-1 Research Scholar, and J-1 Academic Training statuses. APPLICATION PROCEDURE 1. Cover Letter: A letter of application addressing how the candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience align with the position, including a summary of teaching philosophy and research interests. 2. Teaching Statement: A statement (1-2 pages) describing teaching approach and experience (including course topics the candidate can teach, mentoring experience, and any evidence of teaching effectiveness). 3. Research Statement: A statement (1-3 pages) outlining current research accomplishments and future research plans. Emphasize how these might involve students or connect to interdisciplinary and industry-related opportunities at WSU. Review of applications will begin on November 1, 2026. The start date for this appointment is August 2027. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position \u2013 Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators \u2013 Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) 07d13aba Last Name (required) 77f0b328 Email (required) 8462bd65 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 32aee678 Last Name (required) 8ddc6ebd Email (required) 67ba91af Job Alert 737558cc Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Engineering College of Engineering Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your