to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/arts-leadership-management-and-music-industry-studies-asst-educator-teaching-professor-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Arts Leadership & Management and Music Industry Studies- Asst Educator/Teaching Professor", "description": "Arts Leadership & Management and Music Industry Studies- Asst Educator/Teaching Professor - Wichita, Kansas, United States Arts Leadership & Management and Music Industry Studies- Asst Educator/Teaching Professor - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Arts Leadership & Management and Music Industry Studies- Asst Educator/Teaching Professor College of Fine Arts | Faculty Arts Leadership & Management and Music Industry Studies- Asst Educator/Teaching Professor 499438 On Site Faculty WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Department: School of Music Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Commensurate with qualifications and experience. Work Schedule: Varied depending upon class schedule;work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Master of Arts in Arts Leadership and Management program prepares emerging and established arts leaders for careers in nonprofit, commercial, and community-based arts organizations. The program emphasizes leadership, entrepreneurship, strategic planning, fundraising, audience development, advocacy, and organizational management. The School of Music and the College of Fine Arts at invites applications for a 9-month, non-tenure track Assistant Educator/Assistant Teaching Professor of the Master of Arts in Arts Leadership and Management (MAALM) and Music Industry Studies beginning August 2027. This joint appointment supports Wichita State University's commitment to applied learning, interdisciplinary collaboration, and engagement with the evolving arts and entertainment industries. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and graduate education through teaching, scholarship, industry engagement, and service that bridges arts leadership, entrepreneurship, music industry studies, and related creative-sector fields. Music Industry Studies prepares students for careers across the contemporary music ecosystem, including artist development, music business, live events, publishing, management, marketing, and digital media. The program emphasizes experiential learning and engagement with industry professionals and organizations. The faculty member will be expected to teach courses across Music Industry Studies and MAALM; develop innovative curriculum responsive to changes in the creative economy; maintain an active scholarly, creative, or professional agenda; mentor students; and contribute to program development, recruitment, and partnerships with arts, cultural, and entertainment organizations. This joint appointment provides opportunities to collaborate across academic units and with community and industry partners throughout Wichita and the region. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for teaching and service, as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Teaching: Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Music Industry Studies, Arts Leadership and Management, and related areas. Develop and revise curriculum that reflects contemporary practices in arts administration, entrepreneurship, music business, and the creative industries. Deliver high-quality instruction in face-to-face, online, and hybrid environments as appropriate. Mentor and advise undergraduate and graduate students, including internships, capstone projects, independent studies, and applied learning experiences. Foster partnerships that connect students with arts organizations, music industry professionals, and community stakeholders. Service: Participate in service activities within the MAALM program, School of Music, College of Fine Arts, and Wichita State University. Contribute to curriculum development, program assessment, accreditation activities, student recruitment, and strategic planning. Engage with professional organizations and community partners in ways that enhance program visibility and student opportunities. Support university initiatives related to applied learning, innovation, and community engagement. Other Duties: Administration of program: devise recruitment strategies to grow enrollment in MAALM. Perform other responsibilities consistent with faculty expertise and departmental needs. All faculty members are expected to uphold professional and ethical standards in teaching, scholarship, and service. Required Education and Experience: Graduate level degree or Equivalent Experience in the Field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements Master\u2019s degree or other appropriate degree in Arts Administration, Arts Leadership, Music Industry, Music Business, Music, Entrepreneurship, Higher Education, Business, or a closely related field. Required Qualifications: Teaching at the undergraduate and/or graduate level; evidence may include prior teaching experience, student evaluations, teaching awards, or a teaching philosophy that reflects best practices in instruction. Demonstrated professional achievement relevant to arts leadership, arts management, music industry studies, music business, entrepreneurship, or related fields. Evidence of professional engagement in arts, entertainment, music, nonprofit, cultural, or creative-sector organizations. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to contribute to both Music Industry Studies and MAALM curricular and programmatic needs. Excellent written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, industry professionals, and community partners. Commitment to applied learning and student success. Demonstrated interest in interdisciplinary collaboration. Knowledge and understanding of program design, development, implementation, and evaluation, including leadership strategies and best practices. Familiarity with curriculum development. Ability to provide instruction curriculum to a variety of learners. Commitment to collaborative processes and environments. Preferred Qualifications: Professional leadership experience within arts, cultural, entertainment, or music-sector organizations. Experience teaching arts administration, entrepreneurship, music business, fundraising, marketing, event management, strategic planning, nonprofit management, artist management, or related subjects. Record of scholarship, creative activity, professional accomplishment, or industry engagement. Experience developing partnerships with arts organizations, music businesses, community agencies, or creative-sector enterprises. Experience with online and hybrid instruction. Experience mentoring graduate students and supervising internships or capstone projects. Experience developing partnerships with arts organizations, music businesses, community agencies, or creative-sector enterprises. Additional Information: WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. REQUIRED APPLICATIONS MATERIALS Cover Letter/Letter of Application addressing qualifications and interest in the position. Teaching Statement describing instructional philosophy, experience, and courses taught with examples. Other upload 1: Professional Engagement Statement with examples. Review of applications will begin on November 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position \u2013 Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators \u2013 Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) 9b535e71 Last Name (required) bf0e32ff Email (required) 8f05835a Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 931a5e83 Last Name (required) 04a78bdf Email (required) 9a8603ee Job Alert 98371b6a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Fine Arts College of Fine Arts Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply.