ss Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 272c7b3a Last Name (required) 8bc6c1f4 Email (required) 8ebf6d48 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-cybersecurity-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Cybersecurity", "description": "Assistant Professor of Cybersecurity - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor of Cybersecurity - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Cybersecurity College of Engineering | Faculty Assistant Professor of Cybersecurity 499423 On Site Faculty Work Authorization and Immigration Sponsorship Wichita State University may be able to sponsor certain faculty positions for employment-based immigration status where authorized by the hiring department and university policy. Sponsorship eligibility varies by faculty position and will be identified in the individual job posting. For faculty positions eligible for sponsorship, international candidates generally must be eligible for sponsorship in a visa classification compatible with the faculty position. For tenured and tenure-track faculty appointments, visa classifications incompatible with such appointments include F-1 Optional Practical Training (OPT), J-1 Research Scholar, and J-1 Academic Training statuses. Department: Electrical and Computer Engineering Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range beginning $95,000/yr, commensurate with qualifications Work Schedule: Dependent on teaching assignment and research program needs;work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering in the College of Engineering invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Cybersecurity . We seek an innovative scholar and educator who will contribute to the department\u2019s teaching mission, research profile, and applied learning initiatives. The successful candidate will be expected to teach undergraduate and graduate courses, develop and sustain a productive and externally visible research program, mentor students, and provide service to the department, college, university, profession, and community. We are seeking applicants whose technical interests in cybersecurity complement and augment the department\u2019s existing strengths and who are well positioned to develop collaborations as part of multidisciplinary research teams. Applicants with expertise in all areas of cybersecurity are encouraged to apply. Our hiring priorities include network defense, cloud security, secure software development, digital forensics, wireless security, human factors in cybersecurity, and emerging domains such as data science and AI for security, as well as the trustworthiness and security of AI. The committee will also consider candidates with strong research backgrounds in cybersecurity applications such as cyber-physical systems (e.g., satellite constellations and uncrewed aerial systems) and threat intelligence. The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering hosts three undergraduate programs (BS in Computer Engineering, BS in Cybersecurity, and BS in Electrical Engineering), one master's program (MS in Electrical and Computer Engineering), and a Ph.D. program in Electrical Engineering and Computer Science. In addition, the department houses eight graduate certificate programs. The department serves over 500 undergraduate students and 100 graduate students. WSU has been designated as a Center of Academic Excellence in Cyber Defense (CAE-CD) by the National Security Agency. This designation recognizes that WSU cybersecurity programs meet rigorous academic standards and prepare cybersecurity professionals to that will reduce vulnerabilities in our national infrastructure. The department is highly integrated with industry partners across the country and is home to the Hub for Cybersecurity Education and Awareness, the Center for Energy Studies, CommSys Lab, CAPPLab, and the Energy Systems Lab. In addition to these companies, the campus is home to Airbus, NETApp, the National Institute for Aviation Research (NIAR), the Deloitte Smart Factory @ Wichita, the Crash Dynamics Lab, the Hub for Advanced Manufacturing and Research (HAMR), and the National Institute for Health Solutions and Innovation (NIHSI). Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Teaching: Developing and teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in cybersecurity and closely related computing areas. Potential teaching areas include network security, cyber operations, secure software development, digital forensics, cyber-physical systems security, cloud and edge security, Internet of Things (IoT) security, risk management, privacy, and related topics. Responsibilities include curriculum development, instructional delivery in appropriate modalities, assessment of student learning, academic mentoring and advising, and supervision of student projects, theses, and dissertations, as appropriate. Faculty members are expected to mentor and advise students, including supervising research projects. Research : Establishing and maintaining a high-quality research program in cybersecurity or a closely related area. This includes publishing peer-reviewed scholarly work and disseminating results through academic venues. The faculty member is expected to pursue external funding through grants and industry collaborations to support research activities and, where appropriate, engage in interdisciplinary projects and industry partnerships. Excellence in scholarship should be demonstrated through a record of research accomplishments or clear potential for producing high-quality research outcomes. Service : Contributing to service activities within the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, the College of Engineering, Wichita State University, and the broader profession. Service activities may include committee work, curriculum and program development, accreditation and assessment activities, student recruitment and outreach, professional society engagement, peer review, and community or industry outreach related to cybersecurity. Other Duties : Fulfilling other duties as assigned, consistent with the faculty member\u2019s expertise and departmental needs. Faculty are expected to uphold the highest professional and ethical standards in teaching, research, and service. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements An earned doctorate in cybersecurity, computer science, computer engineering, electrical engineering, or a closely related field with an emphasis on cybersecurity. Candidates must have completed all requirements for the Ph.D. by end of May 2027. Applicants who are at an advanced stage of their doctoral studies will be considered if they provide strong evidence that all degree requirements will be completed by the end of June 2027. Demonstrated potential for effective teaching in cybersecurity and related disciplines. Demonstrated potential for productive research and scholarly activity in cybersecurity, as evidenced by a record of peer-reviewed publications and a strong potential for future research productivity. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Potential to obtain external research funding, or evidence of previous success in securing grants, contracts, or industry-supported research funding. Ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, staff, and external partners in an academic environment. Ability to develop collaborations as part of a multidisciplinary research teams. Excellent written and oral communication skills, and the ability to work effectively with colleagues and students. The candidate should be able to collaborate in a collegial academic environment and adapt to the interdisciplinary and applied learning focus of Wichita State. Ability to provide instruction curriculum to a variety of learners. Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching or assisting with undergraduate or graduate courses in cybersecurity or closely related areas. Experience mentoring students, supervising research projects, or supporting student applied-learning experiences. Experience collaborating across disciplines or with industry, government, community, or critical infrastructure partners. Additional Information: Work Authorization and Immigration Sponsorship Wichita State University may be able to sponsor certain faculty positions for employment-based immigration status where authorized by the hiring department and university policy. Sponsorship eligibility varies by faculty position and will be identified in the individual job posting. For faculty positions eligible for sponsorship, international candidates generally must be eligible for sponsorship in a visa classification compatible with the faculty position. For tenured and tenure-track faculty appointments, visa classifications incompatible with such appointments include F-1 Optional Practical Training (OPT), J-1 Research Scholar, and J-1 Academic Training statuses. 1. Cover Letter: Describing qualifications and alignment with the position. 2. Teaching Statement (maximum 2 pages): Describing teaching interests, experience, and potential cybersecurity or computing courses the candidate could teach or develop. 3. Research Statement (maximum 2 pages): Describing current research accomplishments, future research plans, potential funding directions, and opportunities for student involvement. Priority deadline for applications is December 1, 2026. The appointment date for the position is August 2027. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position \u2013 Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators \u2013 Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) 6e7881e7 Last Name (required) ca20a84b Email (required) a6002b23 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 40659c84 Last Name (required) 4429491f Email (required) 07939076 Job Alert 8b04f17c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Engineering College of Engineering Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 99a5ea1a Last Name (required) 998762fe Email (required) 404b83ca Send This Job To: 8850ef44 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, departme