ge of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/tutor-trio-stem-student-support-services-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Tutor, TRIO STEM Student Support Services", "description": "Tutor, TRIO STEM Student Support Services - Wichita, Kansas, United States Tutor, TRIO STEM Student Support Services - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Tutor, TRIO STEM Student Support Services Strategic Engagement & Planning | Student Tutor, TRIO STEM Student Support Services 499789 Student Department TRIO STEM Student Support Services Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay 12.00 per hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Based on class schedule and tutoring needs Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Tutors provides high\u2011quality academic support to undergraduate participants in the federally funded TRIO Student Support Services STEM Program. Tutors assist students in strengthening their understanding of course content, developing effective learning strategies, and building confidence in their academic abilities. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Provide individual and small group tutoring in assigned subject areas. Help students understand key concepts, work through problems, and develop effective study and problem solving strategies. Adapt tutoring approaches to meet the needs of STEM and health professions students. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements Education: Minimum Sophomore standing; maintain a minimum GPA of 3.0; has achieved a grade of \u201cB\u201d or better in tutored courses. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications Prior tutoring, teaching, mentoring, or peer\u2011education experience. Experience supporting first\u2011generation, low\u2011income, or students with disabilities. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) e0820f81 Last Name (required) 7b205f32 Email (required) 51ba4a4f Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 0cf44b45 Last Name (required) 31a9eb66 Email (required) 16e65c9f Job Alert 8cbbc595 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Strategic Engagement & Planning Strategic Engagement & Planning Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 4fc6a86a Last Name (required) becbdc25 Email (required) 4fdc29b9 Send This Job To: 38c25cc9 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" \u2013 Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries