ul professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 7f5795f0 Last Name (required) b9be4e95 Email (required) 4b9da486 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-director-of-choral-activities-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Director of Choral Activities", "description": "Assistant Professor, Director of Choral Activities - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor, Director of Choral Activities - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor, Director of Choral Activities College of Fine Arts | Faculty Assistant Professor, Director of Choral Activities 499436 On Site Faculty WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Department: School of Music Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Commensurate with qualifications and experience Work Schedule: Varied depending upon class, rehearsal, and performance schedule; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Director of Choral Activities provides leadership for the choral program and opportunities to collaborate across the School of Music, College of Fine Arts, and with schools, churches, and community choral organizations throughout Wichita and the region. This position supports our commitment to excellence in music education, performance, and student development. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and graduate education through conducting and teaching, scholarship and/or creative activity, and service that advances the School of Music's choral program. The School of Music and the College of Fine Arts invites applications for a 9-month, tenure-track Assistant Professor, Director of Choral Activities position beginning August 2027. The faculty member will be expected to conduct multiple choirs including the Concert Chorale, the premiere choral ensemble; teach undergraduate and graduate courses in choral conducting, methods, and literature; recruit, audition, and retain choral students; maintain an active scholarly, creative, or professional agenda; advise and mentor graduate choral conducting students; and contribute to program development and community and professional engagement. The School of Music supports the mission of being an applied learning community of musicians who fulfill professional goals and become lifelong advocates for the arts. The choral program engages singers and choral conductors for careers in performance, education, and additional pathways. The program offers a range of auditioned and non-auditioned ensembles and emphasizes choral literature, vocal pedagogy, and engagement with regional and national choral organizations, festivals, and honor choirs. The School of Music at Wichita State University has a distinguished history that began with the founding of the institution on September 11, 1895, originally known as Fairmount College. From its early days, music was a foundational component of the college's offerings, alongside drawing, as part of the Department of Fine Arts. Music quickly became a hallmark of the college's reputation, contributing to its prominence in the arts. The School of Music remains a vibrant part of Wichita State University, dedicated to nurturing the talents of its students and contributing to the rich cultural fabric of the university and the broader community. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Conducting and Teaching: Conduct the University's principal auditioned choral ensemble(s) and oversee the overall choral program. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in choral conducting, choral methods, and choral literature. Develop and revise curriculum that reflects contemporary practices in choral music education and performance. Recruit, audition, and retain choral students across the School of Music. Mentor and advise graduate conducting students. Organize and lead choral festivals, honor choirs, and outreach clinics with regional schools and community organizations. Scholarship/Creative Activity: Maintain an active program of scholarship, creative activity, or professional engagement in choral music, such as guest conducting, adjudication, commissioning, publication, performance or a related area. Present or perform at regional and national conferences, including those of the American Choral Directors Association (ACDA) and related professional organizations. Service: Participate in service activities within the choral program, School of Music, College of Fine Arts, and Wichita State University. Contribute to curriculum development, program assessment, accreditation activities, student recruitment, and strategic planning. Engage with professional organizations, schools, churches, and community choral organizations in ways that enhance program visibility and student opportunities. Support university initiatives related to applied learning, inclusivity, and community engagement. Other Duties: Administration of program: devise recruitment strategies to grow enrollment in the choral program. Perform other responsibilities consistent with faculty expertise and departmental needs. All faculty members are expected to uphold professional and ethical standards in teaching, scholarship, and service. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements Doctor of Musical Arts (DMA) or Ph.D. in Choral Conducting or a closely related field, required. Required Experience: Demonstrated excellence in choral conducting at the collegiate level or through equivalent professional experience. Effective teaching at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. Evidence may include prior teaching experience, student evaluations, teaching awards, or a teaching philosophy that reflects best practices in instruction. Demonstrated professional, scholarly, or creative achievement relevant to choral conducting or choral music education. Evidence of professional engagement in the choral music field, such as adjudication, guest conducting, or membership in professional organizations. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Excellent written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, industry professionals, and community partners. Commitment to student success and inclusive excellence in choral music education. Ability to recruit and retain choral students and to contribute to the School of Music's broader curricular and programmatic needs. Ability to provide instruction curriculum to a variety of learners. Commitment to collaborative processes and environments. Preferred Qualifications: Experience conducting collegiate choral ensembles as professor of record. Experience teaching choral conducting, methods, and literature at the collegiate level. Record of scholarship, creative activity, or professional accomplishment in choral music. Experience with choral repertoire across diverse styles, traditions, and languages. Experience mentoring graduate conducting students and supervising internships or capstone projects. Experience organizing choral tours, festivals, and honor choirs. Experience with online and hybrid instruction. Demonstrated interest in interdisciplinary collaboration. Additional Information: WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. REQUIRED APPLICANT MATERIALS: 1.Cover Letter/Letter of application addressing qualifications and interest in the position. 2. Teaching Statement describing conducting philosophy, teaching experience, and courses taught. 3. Media URL: Recordings of choral conducting (video links \u2013 up to 15 min. of rehearsal and 15 min. of performance). Review of applications will begin on November 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position \u2013 Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators \u2013 Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) 6c799b6b Last Name (required) b53cba26 Email (required) 7323233d Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) bd9b43a2 Last Name (required) 2912622d Email (required) a25ab4a1 Job Alert bf96deb0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Fine Arts College of Fine Arts Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 5f006393 Last Name (required) ace830de Email (required) a75760eb Send This Job To: 09f9fba7 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" \u2013 Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) e35511df Last Name (required) c1590b5f Email (required) d0c220c4 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/recruitment-and-scholarship-coordinator-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Recruitment and Scholarship Coordinator", "description": "Recruitment and Scholarship Coordinator - Wichita, Kansas, United States Recruitment and Scholarship Coordinator - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Recruitment and Scholarship Coordinator Barton School of Business | Academic/Student Support, Staff Recruitment and Scholarship Coordinator 499570 Academic/Student Support Staff Department: Barton School Student Success Center Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range $39,700/yr, adjusted based on qualifications Work Schedule: General business hours; Evenings regularly during recruitment season & a couple of wknds in the year; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Be the person who builds the relationship, answers questions, coordinates visits, maintains communication, and guide prospective students through the enrollment process. Just like that Wichita State has a new student on campus! You made that happen! The position serves as a primary point of contact for prospective undergraduate students and families, manages recruitment territories, represents W. Frank Barton School of Business at events, and helps convert interest into applications and enrollment. We are looking for someone who can meet students where they are, communicate clearly, build trust quickly, and keep the recruitment pipeline growing. You're not afraid to chat with others about higher education & get excited by being able to tell people about WSU & all it has to offer! Represent Barton in the Market Build Relationships Recruit Freshmen and Transfer Students Convert Interest into Applications Support & Invigorate Campus Visits and Events Use CRM to Track Data Identify Recruitment Opportunities The Kind of Person Who Thrives Here: Someone who gets recharged by talking with others, variety in what they do, and measurable results with ownership over those. You may come from admissions, recruitment, student services, sales, outreach, or another role where relationships and follow-through matter. Organization is the other side of the coin that you must prosses to be successful though. You can speak with students and families, work with counselors and partners, manage events, use data, and stay organized across many conversations at once. You don't wait for students to find Barton, you go where they are, build the connection, make it feel real to the student & families, follow up at the right time, and help Barton be seen as their next step. Job Summary Collaborates with faculty and staff in a specific college, department, program or specific focal area to coordinate and expand student recruitment efforts. Serves as the coordinator for schools and organizations that align with the recruitment strategy. Aligns scholarship resources with recruitment goals. Coordinates scholarship competitions and promoted scholarship opportunities to qualified students. Essential Functions Represents specific University colleges, departments or programs at specified schools, college and community fairs, public presentations, and/or seminars. Participates in on and off campus recruitment programs, including group presentations; greets walk-in and scheduled visitors; maintains knowledge of all facets of the University. May develop, coordinate and execute all aspects of event planning for recruitment and scholarships to facilitate effective presentation of programs or events. Coordinates with related departments to facilitate recruitment, outreach, and/or marketing of related programs and services. May lead staff in the design and implementation of communications and educational content. Monitors scholarship compliance with program rules and regulations, provides status updates, and monitors student academic progress as required. Identifies, promotes and targets scholarships to eligible students. Collaborates with University staff and students to foster academic success. Job Duties Event planning & full execution - AGH scholarship Plan, organize & inform all team members of the event yearly. This includes participants, catering, venue & other aspects needed for a successful event to occur. Required Education and Experience: 60 hours of college course work in education or business Four (4) years of experience in recruiting, retention, admissions, or related fields. An additional 60 hours of college coursework beyond the minimum can be substituted for two (2) years of experience. Required License/Certifications/Training: Valid Kansas drivers license Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to build strong relationships and rapport quickly. public speaking abilities. Knowledge of event planning aspects Familiar with higher ed admissions process and key university personnel Excellent communication skills and the ability to engage effectively with students, families, and institutional partners Proficiency in using CRM systems and other relevant tools Ability to travel regionally and work occasional evenings and weekends as needed Organized and able to accomplish deadline needs Capable of maintain confidentiality Comfortable engaging with diverse populations Preferred Qualifications: Event planning and execution Additional Information: N/A Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) 20c251e1 Last Name (required) 0b7a4350 Email (required) 20fe370f Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 7d4ca01c Last Name (required) 6d2e7789 Email (required) c20d9668 Job Alert bf1c63c1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic/Student Support Staff Academic/Student Support Staff Department(s) Barton School of Business Barton School of Business Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 7f853032 Last Name (required) c94b2f82 Email (required) 83af2147 Send This Job To: 78caa1ed Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" \u2013 Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 59060e1b Last Name (required) b181013a Email (required) 2c235875 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/business-technology-analyst-wichita-kansas-united-states-7fb255e2-b9fd-4d86-bee9-2d867f75d02a": {"title": "Business Technology Analyst", "description": "Business Technology Analyst - Wichita, Kansas, United States Business Technology Analyst - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Business Technology Analyst Financial Operations | Finance, Staff Business Technology Analyst 499506 Finance Staff Department: Financial Services Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range from $65,700 - $85,000/yr; determined based on qualifications Work Schedule: Hybrid & flexible schedule with core business hours of 8a -5p, Monday-Friday; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Do you enjoy solving complex problems, improving business processes, and helping organizations leverage technology to work smarter? Wichita State University's Financial Services team is seeking talented professionals who brings together technology expertise and financial knowledge to support critical university operations. In this role, you'll work at the intersection of finance, technology, research administration, and customer service. You'll collaborate with stakeholders across campus to support enterprise financial systems, improve business processes, develop reporting solutions, and implement technology enhancements that directly impact faculty, staff, and researchers. You'll participate in strategic initiatives focused on modernization, automation, service excellence, and continuous improvement while helping shape the future of financial operations at Wichita State University. This position offers the opportunity to work with a diverse technology portfolio including Banner Finance, TouchNet, reporting tools, research administration systems, and other enterprise applications. We're looking for curious, analytical professionals who enjoy understanding how systems work, asking questions, solving problems, and creating solutions that make a meaningful difference. If you're passionate about technology, data, accounting, and continuous improvement, we'd love to hear from you. Job Summary Provides analysis and support of software and processes within the assigned functional area which may include, but is not limited to configuration, testing, documentation, support, maintenance and training for solutions, and working closely with business users, leaders, and technical users throughout the lifecycle of a system and/or project. Essential Functions Provides development, analysis and support for systems. Works closely with business users and managers to refine, develop and prioritize business goals and process enhancements. Provides system support, including implementation, testing, training, new releases, and vendor coordination. Works closely with business users and managers to understand, refine and prioritize business goals and information needs. Manages and supports applications, including support, upgrades and troubleshooting May provide support for interfaces. Job Duties Develop a comprehensive understanding of Accounts Receivable, Accounting, and Research Accounting business processes, financial transactions, internal controls, and reporting requirements to serve as a trusted business systems partner. Collaborate with functional users to analyze business needs, troubleshoot complex system and data issues, identify root causes, and recommend solutions that align with accounting principles, regulatory requirements, and university business processes. Serve as the primary liaison between Financial Services stakeholders and technical teams, translating business requirements into functional specifications and ensuring successful implementation of system enhancements and process improvements. Gather reporting requirements from business users and develop, test, and validate SQL queries to support operational, financial, compliance, and management reporting needs. Act as the subject matter expert for financial data structures and reporting logic, partnering with the Cognos reporting team to design, test, validate, and deploy accurate and meaningful reports and dashboards. Support enterprise financial applications through system testing, upgrades, integrations, documentation, training, and continuous improvement initiatives that enhance efficiency, standardization, data integrity, and customer service. Required Education and Experience: 60 hours of college coursework in related field Two (2) years of experience in technology application support or related field Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to analyze business processes, identify issues, and recommend solutions that improve efficiency, accuracy, and internal controls. Knowledge of accounting principles, financial transactions, and ERP systems such as Banner or similar enterprise applications. Ability to gather reporting requirements, analyze data, and validate reporting results. Familiar with writing, testing, and troubleshooting SQL queries used for reporting, reconciliation, and data analysis. Knowledge to investigate and resolve complex system, data, and process-related issues. Ability to gather and document business requirements and effectively communicate technical solutions to functional users and technical teams. Preferred Qualifications: Coursework in accounting, finance, database management, business analysis, or information systems. Experience with Banner Finance, Banner Accounts Receivable, or a comparable ERP system. Experience supporting Accounts Receivable, Accounting, Research Accounting, grants administration, or other financial operations. Experience working with TouchNet, Cognos, Evisions, or similar enterprise applications. Experience working in higher education, state government, or public sector environments. Experience serving as a liaison between business users and technical teams to develop reporting solutions, troubleshoot issues, and improve business processes. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to position self for inspection, construction or maintenance of equipment and/or buildings including confined, elevated and loud noise spaces. Ability to move, transport, and/or deliver items, supplies, or equipment. Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) 163b6aad Last Name (required) ffa76c2e Email (required) 9f6a8e37 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 14237d3f Last Name (required) 354784c7 Email (required) 886e1743 Job Alert fdac6edb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Finance Staff Finance Staff Department(s) Financial Operations Financial Operations Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State