 mode Machinist Innovation Hub CoE U4 NBE College of Engineering | Temporary Machinist Innovation Hub CoE U4 NBE 499682 Temporary Department Innovation Hub CoE Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay 7000/semester Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. TBD with supervisor Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Shape the next generation of manufacturing professionals. We are seeking an experienced and engaging Lecturer in Machining Technology to teach, mentor, and prepare students for careers in modern manufacturing. This position offers the opportunity to combine industry expertise with hands-on instruction in machining, CNC operations, quality control, and manufacturing best practices within a dynamic academic environment. Job Duties The Lecturer in Machining Technology delivers classroom, laboratory, and project-based instruction in machining and manufacturing processes. The successful candidate will teach conventional and Computer Numerical Control (CNC) machining, blueprint reading, metrology, quality systems, safety practices, and manufacturing process improvement concepts. The lecturer will support student success through hands-on training, curriculum development, industry engagement, and academic advising. 1. Teach undergraduate and/or technical courses in machining, manufacturing, and related engineering technology subjects. 2. Deliver classroom, laboratory, and project-based instruction in: o Manual machining o CNC machining o CNC programming (G-code and M-code) o Blueprint reading and GD&T o Metrology and inspection methods o Manufacturing materials and processes 3. Develop and maintain course materials, assignments, laboratory exercises, and assessments. 4. Evaluate student performance and provide timely feedback. Laboratory Management 1. Operate, demonstrate, and supervise the use of machine shop equipment, including CNC mills, CNC lathes, manual mills, engine lathes, grinders, and related equipment. 2. Ensure safe operation of laboratory facilities and enforce compliance with all safety requirements and Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) standards. 3. Coordinate equipment maintenance, calibration, and inventory of tools and consumables. Student Engagement 1. Advise and mentor students regarding academic progress, career planning, internships, and industry certifications. 2. Support student projects, competitions, applied learning activities, and capstone projects. 3. Maintain regular office hours and provide academic support to students. Curriculum and Program Support 1. Participate in curriculum review and continuous improvement activities. 2. Collaborate with faculty, staff, and industry partners to ensure program relevance and workforce alignment. 3. Assist with accreditation, assessment, and program evaluation efforts. Industry and Continuous Improvement 1. Maintain knowledge of current machining technologies, manufacturing trends, automation, and Industry 4.0 practices. 2. Identify opportunities to improve laboratory operations, instructional effectiveness, and student learning outcomes using continuous improvement methodologies. Required Education This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and/or preferences. Additional Requirements 1. Ability to lift up to 50 pounds with or without reasonable accommodation. 2. Ability to stand, walk, bend, and work in laboratory environments for extended periods. 3. Strong mathematical skills, including fractions, decimals, geometry, trigonometry, and machining calculations. 4. Ability to operate machine tools safely and effectively. 5. Demonstrated commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and student success. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and/or preferences. Preferred Qualifications 1. Bachelor's or Master's degree in Manufacturing Engineering, Engineering Technology, Industrial Technology, Mechanical Engineering, or a related discipline. 2. Previous teaching, corporate training, apprenticeship instruction, or workforce development experience. 3. Experience editing and troubleshooting G-code and CNC programs directly at machine controls. 4. Industry-recognized certifications such as: o NIMS Certifications o SME Certifications o FANUC Certifications o OSHA Safety Training 5. Experience machining diverse materials, including: o Aluminum o Stainless steel o Tool steels o Plastics o Composites 6. Knowledge of CAD/CAM software and computer-aided manufacturing systems. 7. Experience with Lean Manufacturing, Six Sigma, Kaizen, 5S, and continuous improvement methodologies. 8. Familiarity with quality management systems and manufacturing standards. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 292b6ddd Last Name (required) 799dbd2d Email (required) e4ddd904 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 6ad80654 Last Name (required) 9273fb27 Email (required) d24bc2e1 Job Alert cc01f0f9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Temporary Temporary Department(s) College of Engineering College of Engineering Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) a5b6e5e9 Last Name (required) 57ab73bf Email (required) 3bd4dabe Send This Job To: 0cb88e4a Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" \u2013 Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) f9cd5b5b Last Name (required) a8ea068e Email (required) f1aef9d5 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-hardware-security-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Hardware Security", "description": "Assistant Professor of Hardware Security - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor of Hardware Security - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Hardware Security College of Engineering | Faculty Assistant Professor of Hardware Security 499424 On Site Faculty Department: Electrical and Computer Engineering Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Range beginning $95,000/yr, commensurate with qualifications Work Schedule: Dependent on teaching assignment and research program needs; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering in the College of Engineering invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Hardware Security . We seek an innovative scholar and educator who will contribute to the department\u2019s teaching mission, research profile, and applied learning initiatives. The successful candidate will be expected to teach undergraduate and graduate courses, develop and sustain a productive and externally visible research program, mentor students, and provide service to the department, college, university, profession, and community. We are seeking applicants whose technical interests in hardware security complement and augment the Department\u2019s existing strengths and who are well positioned to develop collaborations as part of multidisciplinary research teams. Applicants with expertise in all areas of hardware security are encouraged to apply. Our hiring priorities include secure computer architecture, hardware Trojans and supply chain security, secure chip design, PCB security, secure FPGA/ASIC design and verification, embedded and IoT hardware security, fault injection, reverse engineering, hardware side-channel attacks, edge security, embedded AI, and physical attack resistance. The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering hosts three undergraduate programs (BS in Computer Engineering, BS in Cybersecurity, and BS in Electrical Engineering), one master's program (MS in Electrical and Computer Engineering), and a Ph.D. program in Electrical Engineering and Computer Science. In addition, the department houses eight graduate certificate programs. The department serves over 500 undergraduate students and 100 graduate students. WSU has been designated as a Center of Academic Excellence in Cyber Defense (CAE-CD) by the National Security Agency. This designation recognizes that WSU cybersecurity programs meet rigorous academic standards and prepare cybersecurity professionals to that will reduce vulnerabilities in our national infrastructure. The department is highly integrated with industry partners across the country and is home to the Hub for Cybersecurity Education and Awareness, the Center for Energy Studies, CommSys Lab, CAPPLab, and the Energy Systems Lab. In addition to these companies, the campus is home to Airbus, NETApp, the National Institute for Aviation Research (NIAR), the Deloitte Smart Factory @ Wichita, the Crash Dynamics Lab, the Hub for Advanced Manufacturing and Research (HAMR), and the National Institute for Health Solutions and Innovation (NIHSI). Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Teaching : Develop and teach undergraduate and graduate courses in hardware security and related areas of computer engineering. Potential teaching areas include processor and system security, secure system-on-chip (SoC) design, trusted computing, hardware Trojans, side-channel attacks, embedded and edge AI systems, FPGA- and ASIC-based system design, Internet of Things (IoT) systems, computer architecture, and other closely related topics. Responsibilities include curriculum development, effective instruction across appropriate delivery modalities, assessment of student learning, academic advising and mentoring, and supervision of undergraduate and graduate student research projects, theses, and dissertations, as appropriate. Research : Establish and maintain a high-quality research program in hardware security or a closely related area. This includes publishing peer-reviewed scholarly work and disseminating research results through recognized academic venues. The faculty member is expected to pursue external funding through grants and industry collaborations to support research activities and, where appropriate, engage in interdisciplinary projects and industry partnerships. Excellence in scholarship should be demonstrated through a record of research accomplishments or clear potential for high-quality research productivity. Service : Contribute to service activities within the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, the College of Engineering, Wichita State University, and the broader profession. Service activities may include committee work, curriculum and program development, accreditation and assessment activities, student recruitment and outreach, professional society engagement, peer review, and community or industry outreach related to hardware security. Other Duties : Fulfill other duties as assigned, consistent with the faculty member\u2019s expertise and departmental needs. Faculty members are expected to uphold the highest professional and ethical standards in teaching, research, and service. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements An earned doctorate in cybersecurity, computer science, computer engineering, electrical engineering, or a closely related field with an emphasis on hardware security. Candidates must have completed all requirements for the Ph.D. by May 2027. Applicants who are at an advanced stage of their doctoral studies will be considered if they provide strong evidence that all degree requirements will be completed by the end of June 2027. Demonstrated potential for effective teaching in hardware security and closely related areas. Demonstrated potential for productive research and scholarly activity in hardware security, as evidenced by a record of peer-reviewed publications and a strong potential for future research productivity. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Potential to obtain external research funding, or evidence of previous success in securing grants, contracts, or industry-supported research funding. Ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, staff, and external partners in an academic environment. Ability to develop collaborations as part of a multidisciplinary research teams. Excellent written and oral communication skills, and the ability to work effectively with colleagues and students. The candidate should be able to collaborate in a collegial academic environment and adapt to the interdisciplinary and applied learning focus of Wichita State. Ability to provide instruction curriculum to a variety of learners. Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching or assisting with undergraduate or graduate courses in hardware security or closely related areas. Experience mentoring students, supervising research projects, or supporting student applied-learning experiences. Experience collaborating across disciplines or with industry, government, community, or critical infrastructure partners. Additional Information: Work Authorization and Immigration Sponsorship Wichita State University may be able to sponsor certain faculty positions for employment-based immigration status where authorized by the hiring department and university policy. Sponsorship eligibility varies by faculty position and will be identified in the individual job posting. For faculty positions eligible for sponsorship, international candidates generally must be eligible for sponsorship in a visa classification compatible with the faculty position. For tenured and tenure-track faculty appointments, visa classifications incompatible with such appointments include F-1 Optional Practical Training (OPT), J-1 Research Scholar, and J-1 Academic Training statuses. 1. Cover Letter: Describing qualifications and alignment with the position. 2. Teaching Statement (maximum 2 pages): Describing teaching interests, experience, and potential cybersecurity or computing courses the candidate could teach or develop. 3. Research Statement (maximum 2 pages): Describing current research accomplishments, future research plans, potential funding directions, and opportunities for student involvement. Priority deadline for applications is December 1, 2026. The appointment date for the position is August 2027. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position \u2013 Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators \u2013 Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) b8665167 Last Name (required) 6afed235 Email (required) dc085070 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) b4b29229 Last Name (required) 