se a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-economics-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Economics", "description": "Assistant Professor of Economics - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor of Economics - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Economics Barton School of Business | Faculty Assistant Professor of Economics 499585 On Site Faculty Work Authorization and Immigration Sponsorship Wichita State University may be able to sponsor certain faculty positions for employment-based immigration status where authorized by the hiring department and university policy. Sponsorship eligibility varies by faculty position and will be identified in the individual job posting. For faculty positions eligible for sponsorship, international candidates generally must be eligible for sponsorship in a visa classification compatible with the faculty position. For tenured and tenure-track faculty appointments, visa classifications incompatible with such appointments include F-1 Optional Practical Training (OPT), J-1 Research Scholar, and J-1 Academic Training statuses. Department: Barton School of Business - Department of Marketing & Economics Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Salary set at $109,535/yr Work Schedule: Dependent on teaching assignment and research program needs;work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Candidates will have an exciting opportunity to contribute to the future of economics education and research at Wichita State University. The position will play an important role in strengthening undergraduate and graduate economics education, producing academic research that advances knowledge, and contributing to innovative academic and applied-learning initiatives that connect economics with industry and the broader community. Wichita State University is classified as a high research activity institution and provides faculty with opportunities and institutional support for research, interdisciplinary collaboration, external funding, and industry-engaged scholarship. The Department of Economics in the W. Frank Barton School of Business at Wichita State University invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-track position as Assistant Professor of Economics, beginning Fall 2027. You will teach undergraduate and graduate courses, establish clear learning objectives, develop curriculum and instructional materials that accomplish those objectives, and provide students with the support needed to succeed. We welcome candidates who can contribute expertise in economics and statistics and build productive professional relationships within the community and across the university. Wichita State University places applied learning at the center of student experience. Every degree program at Wichita State includes a guaranteed applied learning or research experience, providing students with opportunities to develop relevant professional skills and meaningful experience before graduation. The successful candidate will have opportunities to integrate these experiences into economics education through applied projects with industry, case studies, research, and engagement with local businesses and the larger community. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties The successful candidate will be expected to: 1. Teaching: Teach two courses per semester (four courses per academic year) at the undergraduate and graduate levels, with courses offered in face-to-face, hybrid, blended, and fully online formats. Each course is three credit hours. Teaching assignments may include, depending on the candidate's expertise and program needs, Principles of Microeconomics, Labor Economics, Business Statistics, and related courses with the opportunity to develop courses in the candidate's area of expertise. The successful candidate will establish key objectives for classes, develop curriculum and syllabi, present course material through lectures and learning activities, and answer students' questions and provide support to help them succeed. 2. Applied Learning and Community Engagement: Foster applied learning in course design by developing meaningful opportunities for students to engage with industry, local businesses, and the larger community through applied projects, case studies, professional engagement, and other experiential learning activities. 3. Research: Develop and maintain an active and sustainable program of academic research consistent with AACSB Scholarly Academic (SA) expectations and the requirements for tenure and promotion at the Barton School of Business. The successful candidate will be expected to publish high-quality scholarly research in respected and leading economics or related academic journals and advance knowledge through sustained scholarly activity. 4. Service and Engagement: Contribute meaningful service to the department, Barton School of Business, university, profession, and local community. Service may include active involvement in committees, student mentorship, student recruitment and retention initiatives, professional organizations, outreach activities, and other activities that advance the mission of the department and school. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements A Ph.D. in Economics from an accredited institution. Applicants who are at an advanced stage of their doctoral studies (ABD) will be considered if they provide strong evidence that all degree requirements will be completed prior to the June 2027. Evidence of an established record of scholarly research or a strong research pipeline with demonstrated ability or potential to publish in high-quality economics or related academic journals. Evidence of, or demonstrated potential for, effective teaching in economics at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Evidence may include teaching evaluations, curriculum or course development, applied-learning activities, experience with face-to-face, hybrid, blended, or fully online instruction, or other indicators of teaching effectiveness. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of economics and statistics. Ability to build professional relationships within the community and across the university at all levels. Ability to provide instruction of curriculum to a variety of learners. Commitment to collaborative processes and environments. Preferred Qualifications: Research and/or teaching interests in labor economics and/or environmental economics. Use of empirical methods, econometric techniques, or data-intensive approaches to address applied economic questions. Additional Information: Work Authorization and Immigration Sponsorship Wichita State University may be able to sponsor certain faculty positions for employment-based immigration status where authorized by the hiring department and university policy. Sponsorship eligibility varies by faculty position and will be identified in the individual job posting. For faculty positions eligible for sponsorship, international candidates generally must be eligible for sponsorship in a visa classification compatible with the faculty position. For tenured and tenure-track faculty appointments, visa classifications incompatible with such appointments include F-1 Optional Practical Training (OPT), J-1 Research Scholar, and J-1 Academic Training statuses. REQUIRED MATERIALS 1. Cover Letter/Letter of application addressing how the candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience align with the position. 2. Teaching Statement: A statement (1-2 pages) describing teaching approach/philosophy and experience (including course topics the candidate can teach, mentoring experience, and any evidence of teaching effectiveness). 3. Research Statement: A statement (1-2 pages) describing research approach/philosophy and experience. A priority deadline for application review is October 31, 2026. The appointment for the position is August 2027. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position \u2013 Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators \u2013 Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) ddf585c8 Last Name (required) 0c761bc1 Email (required) c82b85b3 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 3c068300 Last Name (required) b6182964 Email (required) 0716326f Job Alert 2d8b8ed5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) Barton School of Business Barton School of Business Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 46b75e65 Last Name (required) d46ae54d Email (required) 41d75d1e Send This Job To: 64c7a5e9 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" \u2013 Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 8ea2e366 Last Name (required) 531f9c5c Email (required) c1e74d89 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-criminal-justice-corrections-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice - Corrections", "description": "Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice - Corrections - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice - Corrections - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice - Corrections College of Liberal Arts & Sciences | Faculty Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice - Corrections 499464 On Site Faculty Department: School of Criminal Justice Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $65,000 Work Schedule: Monday - Friday, may vary depending on class schedule; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The School of Criminal Justice (SCJ) at Wichita State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position starting on August 2, 2027 in Criminal Justice with the ability to teach and conduct research in the area of Corrections. We seek a dynamic and innovative scholar committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The successful candidate will contribute to our undergraduate and graduate programs, engage in impactful research, and participate in departmental, college, and university committees. The salary for this 9-month position will be $65,000. As one of the oldest criminal justice programs in the United States, our school offers bachelor's and master's degrees in Criminal Justice, a fully online bachelor's degree in Homeland Security, a bachelor's degree in Forensic Science, and master\u2019s degrees in Forensic Biology and Forensic Firearms. Due to the school's strong partnership with local and state agencies, faculty have abundant research opportunities. The SCJ is housed in the Law Enforcement Training Center on WSU\u2019s Innovation Campus \u2013 a partnership building shared with the Wichita Police Department and the Sedgwick County Sheriff\u2019s Office. The SCJ has close partnerships with the Midwest Criminal Justice Institute and with the US Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms, and Explosives (ATF), which has two buildings on the Innovation Campus housing the Crime Gun Intelligence Center of Excellence, the NIBIN National Correlation and Training Center II, and the ATF Wichita Field Office. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in criminal justice, including corrections. The standard teaching load for research-active faculty is three classes per semester. Develop and maintain an active research agenda that leads to refereed publications. Seek external funding for research projects, individually or collaboratively, with faculty or local/state agencies. Mentor and advise students. Participate in departmental, college, and university service activities. Engage with the community and contribute to public scholarship. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements PhD or other terminal degree in criminal justice, sociology, criminology, or other related field completed prior to August 2027. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching in multiple modalities (e.g., online, hybrid, in-person) Demonstrated potential for publishing in peer-reviewed journals. Ability to work collaboratively with colleagues and students from diverse backgrounds. Additional Information: Please complete the Faculty Profile including the names and contact information of three (3) references and upload the following documents: 1) A cover letter 2) Current CV which clearly outlines practical experience in corrections 3) A statement of teaching philosophy For full consideration, completed applications should be submitted by November 2, 2026. For additional information, please contact david.eichhorn@wichita.edu. WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position \u2013 Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators \u2013 Frequent 60-90% Apply Now First Name (required) 0544a1f3 Last Name (required) d94df01b Email (required) 63351ca9 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 3ee9604f Last Name (required) c41b5d7a Email (required) 66e4bfa4 Job Alert 22567363 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Liberal Arts & Sciences College of Liberal Arts & Sciences Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With So