udy 0350W 499752 Student Department College of Eng. ESSC Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay 12/hr Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. TBD with supervisor. Dependent upon course schedule Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Serve as the first point of contact for the GEEKs Tutoring Center by providing outstanding customer service to students, faculty, and visitors while supporting the daily operations of the center. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties \u2022 Welcome students and visitors to the tutoring center. \u2022 Check students in and out for tutoring appointments. \u2022 Answer questions regarding tutoring services and center operations. \u2022 Maintain accurate records and assist with daily administrative tasks. \u2022 Monitor the tutoring space and communicate operational concerns to professional staff. \u2022 Assist with opening and closing procedures as assigned. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements MUST BE WORK-STUDY ELIGIBLE. \u2022 Must be enrolled as a Wichita State University student. \u2022 Excellent customer service and communication skills. \u2022 Strong attention to detail. \u2022 Ability to maintain confidentiality. \u2022 Dependable with consistent attendance. \u2022 Ability to work independently after training. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications \u2022 Currently a College of Engineering student. \u2022 Previous customer service or office experience. \u2022 Experience using Microsoft Office and basic computer applications. \u2022 Strong organizational and multitasking skills. \u2022 Familiarity with Wichita State resources is preferred. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 5f627572 Last Name (required) 4db5d384 Email (required) 861f527e Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 2c760600 Last Name (required) a12abdbd Email (required) 44e68594 Job Alert 9cc330c0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) College of Engineering College of Engineering Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 4f8ddccc Last Name (required) d21d44a9 Email (required) 129d6ea4 Send This Job To: 6fea0407 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text m