t control requirement. Job Story Join the GEEKs Tutoring Center as a peer tutor and help College of Engineering students achieve academic success. Tutors provide course-specific academic support while creating a welcoming and collaborative learning environment that promotes student persistence, confidence, and engagement. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties \u2022 Provide one-on-one and small-group tutoring for College of Engineering courses. \u2022 Assist students in developing effective study strategies and problem-solving skills. \u2022 Maintain accurate tutoring records and complete required documentation. \u2022 Foster a welcoming, inclusive, and professional learning environment. \u2022 Collaborate with GEEKs staff and participate in required training and meetings. \u2022 Refer students to additional campus resources when appropriate. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements MUST BE WORK-STUDY ELIGIBLE. \u2022 Must be enrolled as a Wichita State University and College of Engineering student. \u2022 Must have successfully completed the courses they will tutor with strong academic performance. \u2022 Maintain good academic standing. \u2022 Demonstrate strong communication and interpersonal skills. \u2022 Ability to maintain confidentiality and professionalism. \u2022 Ability to work scheduled shifts throughout the semester. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications \u2022 Previous tutoring, mentoring, teaching assistant, or peer leadership experience. \u2022 Strong organizational and time management skills. \u2022 Demonstrated commitment to helping fellow students succeed. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 3a7cab98 Last Name (required) 1ff512d9 Email (required) 0eb255e9 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) e9213f43 Last Name (required) ae535b3e Email (required) 8932fab5 Job Alert 13ca9c7f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) College of Engineering College of Engineering Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 3c22e7a1 Last Name (required) f1274841 Email (required) dd27e387 Send This Job To: 59c39a64 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State