o complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) b94efbc0 Last Name (required) d53ced2d Email (required) 3b143141 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-integrated-marketing-communication-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Integrated Marketing Communication", "description": "Assistant Professor of Integrated Marketing Communication - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor of Integrated Marketing Communication - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Integrated Marketing Communication College of Liberal Arts & Sciences | Faculty Assistant Professor of Integrated Marketing Communication 499428 On Site Faculty Department: Elliott School of Communication Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $70,000 - $75,000 Work Schedule: Schedule may vary depending on course offerings; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Elliott School of Communication at Wichita State University seeks a full-time, 9-month, tenure-eligible assistant professor in the Integrated Marketing Communications area, the largest concentration in the school. We are looking for collegial candidates with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in research, teaching, and service for an appointment beginning August 2, 2027, with a salary range of $70,000 to $75,000 (maximum). Specifically, we seek scholars who bring special expertise in Integrated Marketing Communications (Public Relations and Advertising). The successful candidate will have opportunities to teach in both the graduate and undergraduate program depending on needs of the school, including courses in a new professionally oriented graduate degree in communication that complements our traditional MA academic track. IMC courses may include media analytics, strategy, social media, account management, measurement and evaluation techniques, and skills classes. Graduate courses may include quantitative research methods, communication theory, and IMC graduate seminars. Candidates will be expected to develop a productive research program and provide service to the university and the profession. Wichita State University is located in the heart of the largest media market in the state. We are committed to applied learning, which is supported by the broad network of alumni and other supporters working in the metro area. The Elliott School of Communication includes 10 full-time faculty, 12 GTAs, and two administrative staff. We are an integrated communication program, offering a common core of classes before students choose from three emphasis areas: integrated marketing communication, journalism and media production, and comm studies. Additionally, the ESC includes The Research Partnership, a full-service marketing research agency that contracts for a wide range of services including focus groups, phone, mail and online surveys, one-on-one interviews, and mystery shops for local and national government agencies, nonprofits, and large and small businesses. ESC faculty are encouraged to take advantage of our research facilities and participate, as desired, in our ongoing projects. Tenure track faculty members typically teach 6 courses per academic year. Tenure track faculty are expected to teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online) and to incorporate applied learning into the course design, whenever possible. The successful candidate will establish and maintain a sustainable research program in the communication disciple that results in peer-reviewed scholarly publications. Tenure track faculty are expected to contribute service to the department, college, university, and the profession. The workload for this position is 60% teaching, 30% research, and 10% service. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiatives, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Teaching : Develop and teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate level in IMC. This includes designing curriculum and instructional materials, delivering high-quality instruction in various modalities (in-person, online, or hybrid), and assessing student learning. The faculty member will mentor and advise students, including supervising research projects or theses as appropriate, and incorporate applied learning opportunities (e.g. projects with industry or community partners) into the coursework whenever possible. Research/Scholarly Activity : Establish and maintain an active research program in communication. This includes publishing peer-reviewed scholarly work and disseminating results in academic venues. Excellence in scholarship should be demonstrated by a record of research accomplishments that follow the departmental tenure and promotion guidelines. Service : Participate in service activities within the department, college, and university, as well as in professional organizations. Service duties include committee work, curriculum development, program assessment, student recruitment, and community outreach. The faculty member will contribute to the governance and strategic initiatives of the department and may also engage in service to the broader profession (e.g. reviewing for journals, involvement in academic societies). Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements PhD in Communication must completed prior to August 2027. Teaching experience at the collegiate level. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students. Demonstrated potential to establish an independent and productive research program. Demonstrated ability or potential to work collaboratively and collegially with individuals from a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. Preferred Qualifications: A record of scholarly productivity appropriate to career stage. Experience teaching qualitative methods and/or media analytics. Additional Information: Please complete the Faculty Profile including the names and contact information of three (3) references and upload the following documents: 1. Cover letter of interest 2. Curriculum Vitae Review of candidates will begin on November 2, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. If you have questions, please contact search chair and ESC director Dr. Lisa Parcell at lisa.parcell@wichita.edu. WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position \u2013 Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators \u2013 Frequent 60-90% Apply Now First Name (required) 7c3bbc4d Last Name (required) ca417661 Email (required) ed6f4f40 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) d4636d3b Last Name (required) 4e4e8631 Email (required) 5d45fb11 Job Alert 8c9858f3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Liberal Arts & Sciences College of Liberal Arts & Sciences Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) c579abea Last Name (required) 2275a598 Email (required) 8607697b Send This Job To: 012af711 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" \u2013 Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 4d48edce Last Name (required) ee47ca39 Email (required) 9ec6bc69 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-educator-assistant-clinical-professor-and-director-of-transition-to-teaching-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Educator/Assistant Clinical Professor and Director of Transition to Teaching", "description": "Assistant Educator/Assistant Clinical Professor and Director of Transition to Teaching - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Educator/Assistant Clinical Professor and Director of Transition to Teaching - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Educator/Assistant Clinical Professor and Director of Transition to Teaching College of Education | Faculty Assistant Educator/Assistant Clinical Professor and Director of Transition to Teaching 499442 On Site Faculty Department: School of Teaching and Learning Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $80,000 Work Schedule: 8am to 5pm, Monday \u2013 Friday, with some flexibility for evenings and weekends as needed. Course offerings include Saturdays. Work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The School of Teaching and Learning in the College of Education at Wichita State University invites applications for a 12-month full-time assistant clinical professor of education and director of the Transition to Teaching program. We seek an expert in areas related to, but not limited to, alternative teacher education, preparing individuals who are changing careers to become teachers, and middle and high school teacher education. We are looking for a collaborative colleague to lead our alternative certification program in the School of Teaching and Learning and join an engaged and collaborative faculty at Kansas\u2019s only urban public research university. The academic appointment for this position will be effective June 7, 2027. As a faculty member in the School of Teaching and Learning, the successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate level classes in the fall, spring, and summer as part of our alternative teacher preparation program. The new faculty member will also work with various populations of students, colleagues, and community, engage in grant seeking activities, and provide service to the program, department, college, university, and profession. About the University and the School of Teaching and Learning Wichita State University is located in the heart of the Midwest in the largest city in Kansas. Our beautiful 330-acre campus recently experienced rapid expansion, with renovation projects and new housing and campus life initiatives. Our enrollment of roughly 17,000 ranges from traditional undergraduate and graduate students to professionals adding new skills or changing fields. We have online programs and thriving campus life/residential students. The School of Teaching and Learning at Wichita State provides high-quality teacher training in early childhood, elementary, and middle/secondary fields. Over 90% of our students receive teaching contracts upon graduation and we are the major source of teachers in the Wichita metropolitan area. Within T2T, students complete their applied learning experiences in the classroom while maintaining employment as teachers of record while throughout their time in the program. Our faculty publish at the regional, national, and international level, present at major conferences in our respective fields, and serve on accreditation boards and professional committees. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for teaching and service, as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties This position will lead the Transition to Teaching program in the School of Teaching and Learning. Faculty members share responsibility for programmatic and instructional decisions within and across program options. The position is a 12-month appointment and carries a 4:4 load for fall/spring semesters, with an additional 6 credit hours of teaching in the summer semester. The director receives a 1-credit release each semester as part of administrative duties for leading the program. The Assistant Educator/Assistant Clinical Professor position include 80% teaching of undergraduate and graduate level courses as assigned, with a focus on content specific pedagogy, research, capstone, and internship or field experience courses. This also includes mentoring and supervising T2T teachers in both years of the program and coordinating school placements. The faculty member will provide service to departmental, college, university, professional and community constituting 20% of this role. Primarily the service role will include the Director of the Transition to Teaching program: developing and maintaining relationships with local school districts and agencies; attend relevant meetings, maintaining student data, leading the program annual report, contributing to accreditation and university reports, and directing recruitment and retention for T2T program. The faculty member may collaborate with colleagues to seek grants related to alternative certification programs. This position requires regular on-campus presence at Wichita State University. The selected candidate must reside in Kansas within a reasonable commuting distance of the WSU main campus. Required Education and Experience: Graduate level degree or Equivalent Experience in the Field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements A Masters or Ed.D or Ph.D. in Education, in teacher preparation or related field, completed prior to start date. Experience in K-12 teaching Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Evidence of potential for excellence in teaching. Willingness to employ various strategies in instructional delivery and learning activities, flexible teaching methods, and applied learning approaches. Evidence of communication and interpersonal skills to work effectively with diverse students and colleagues. Ability to work collaboratively with other faculty and professionals. Ability to work supportively with returning adult college students/career professionals. Ability to develop relationships with community partners to enhance supervision and coordination of school placements. Preferred Qualifications: Earned Ed.D or Ph.D. in Teacher Preparation-Secondary Education or related field. Three years\u2019 professional-level 6-12 teaching experience. Previous university level teaching experience, including online teaching Evidence of working with adult college students. Experience mentoring pre-service or in-service teachers. Experience in university level course development and implementation. Evidence of leadership in education. Additional Information: Please complete the Faculty Profile including the names and contact information of three (3) references and upload the following documents: 1. Cover letter including teaching statement 2. Curriculum Vitae Review of applications will begin on November 2, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position \u2013 Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators \u2013 Frequent 60-90% Apply Now First Name (required) 11316cc5 Last Name (required) 4cbcabf2 Email (required) 35954e1e Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 6dd49c78 Last Name (required) 4a2e343d Email (required) a45a8f35 Job Alert 8c0b5168 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Education College of Education Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 3c392c6d Last Name (required) 5c0c0a73 Email (required) 4170ff4c Send This Job To: 307d81ee Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" \u2013 Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) a7b207ba Last Name (required) 7bb6cd35 Email (required) ebf1b0ee Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-biomedical-sciences-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor - Biomedical Sciences", "description": "Assistant Professor - Biomedical Sciences - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor - Biomedical Sciences - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor - Biomedical Sciences College of Liberal Arts & Sciences | Faculty Assistant Professor - Biomedical Sciences 499491 On Site Faculty Department: Department of Biological Sciences Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $70,000 Work Schedule: M-F 8-5; Variable dependent on schedule; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Position Overview: The Department of Biological Sciences in the Fairmount College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at Wichita State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Biomedical Sciences. We seek applicants with teaching and research expertise in the fields of Microbiology, Virology, Genetics, and/or Parasitology. The successful candidate will be expected to teach undergraduate and graduate courses, develop a productive research program, and provide service to the university and profession. This position is a 9-month appointment with an anticipated start date of August 2, 2027. Department Description: The Department of Biological Sciences offers majors in Biology with either an Ecological/Environmental/Organismal or a Biomedical emphasis. There are approximately 340 undergraduate majors and the department\u2019s Master of Science in Biology program currently includes 19 graduate students. There are 11 faculty members and seven full-time departmental support staff/administrators. The department is committed to excellence in teaching, research, and student success. The department is an affiliate of the Kansas Idea Network of Biomedical Research Excellence (K-INBRE). It houses modern laboratory space that includes analytical/molecular and cell culture equipment, microscopy and protein chemistry core facilities, an accredited animal facility, and access to the Kansas State University and Wichita State University High Performance Computing clusters. Core Responsibilities Teaching: Develop and teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate level in the candidate\u2019s area of expertise. This includes designing curriculum, delivering high-quality instruction, and assessing student learning. The faculty member will mentor and advise students, including supervising undergraduate and M.S. research projects. Research/Scholarly Activity: Establish and maintain an active, externally funded research program in Microbiology, Virology, Genetics, and/or Parasitology involving undergraduate students and M.S. graduate students. This includes publishing peer reviewed scholarly work and disseminating results in academic venues. Service: Participate in service activities within the department, college, and university, as well as in professional organizations. Service duties include committee work, curriculum development, program assessment, student recruitment, and community outreach. The faculty member will contribute to the governance and strategic initiatives of the department and may also engage in service to the broader profession. Other: Fulfill other duties as assigned, in accordance with the faculty member\u2019s talents and departmental needs. All Wichita State faculty are expected to uphold professional and ethical standards in teaching, research, and service. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Teaching: Develop and teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate level in the candidate\u2019s area of expertise. This includes designing curriculum, delivering high-quality instruction, and assessing student learning. The faculty member will mentor and advise students, including supervising undergraduate and M.S. research projects. Research/Scholarly Activity: Establish and maintain an active, externally funded research program in Microbiology, Virology, Genetics, and/or Parasitology involving undergraduate students and M.S. graduate students. This includes publishing peer reviewed scholarly work and disseminating results in academic venues. Service: Participate in service activities within the department, college, and university, as well as in professional organizations. Service duties include committee work, curriculum development, program assessment, student recruitment, and community outreach. The faculty member will contribute to the governance and strategic initiatives of the department and may also engage in service to the broader profession. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements PhD in Biology or related field and must be completed prior to August 2027. Teaching experience is broadly defined i.e. teaching assistantships, mentoring, participation in course lectures, etc. Please clarify in your teaching statement. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to teach undergraduate and graduate classes in area of expertise. Effective written and oral communication skills. Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students. Demonstrated potential to establish an independent and productive research program. Demonstrated ability or potential to work effectively in collaborative environments and engage constructively with individuals from a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. Preferred Qualifications: Postdoctoral research experience is preferred, but strong candidates lacking postdoctoral experience will be considered. Additional Information: Please complete the Faculty Profile including the names and contact information of three (3) references and upload the following documents: 1) Letter of application 2) Current curriculum vita 3) Statement of teaching philosophy and goals 4) Statement of research interests and goals 5) Copies of unofficial academic transcripts Applicants must apply by October 19, 2026 for full consideration. WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position \u2013 Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators \u2013 Frequent 60-90% Apply 