nt, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" \u2013 Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) d5bfc33d Last Name (required) 2dae77db Email (required) 2fe73f07 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-cad-cam-hamr-operations-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "NIAR CAD/CAM HAMR Operations Student Assistant", "description": "NIAR CAD/CAM HAMR Operations Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR CAD/CAM HAMR Operations Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR CAD/CAM HAMR Operations Student Assistant NIAR Institute | Student NIAR CAD/CAM HAMR Operations Student Assistant 499744 Student Department NIAR CAD/CAM Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $15 - 18 per hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Flexible with class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a \u201cU.S. Citizen\u201d. Job Story NIAR\u2019s Hub for Advanced Manufacturing and Research (HAMR) is seeking a student with strong communication, organization, and customer service skills to support facility operations. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties This role focuses on ensuring a smooth day-to-day experience for building occupants and visitors by checking and stocking amenities (e.g., coffee and soda supplies), assisting with events and tour scheduling and preparation, and supporting package/mail tracking and occupant notifications. Depending on building needs, the student may assist other staff, help coordinate activities for visitors and partners, and provide support throughout the HAMR facility. The position may also assist with general coordination tasks across HAMR and provide support for special events as needed. This position is ideal for students interested in gaining hands-on operations and customer service experience in a dynamic research environment. Under supervision, students will: \u2022 Support daily facility operations, including opening/closing procedures, cleanliness checks, and readiness of common areas. \u2022 Check, stock, and track amenities (coffee, soda, snacks, paper goods), monitor inventory levels, and coordinate reorders with staff. \u2022 Assist with scheduling and preparing for events and tours, including room reservations, A/V checks, signage, seating layouts, and setup/teardown. \u2022 Assist visitors and tour groups, manage check-ins, and provide wayfinding support. \u2022 Track incoming packages/mail and promptly notify building occupants; maintain logs and coordinate internal deliveries as directed. \u2022 Maintain shared calendars and documentation, including event schedules, inventory records, and standard operating procedures. \u2022 Support special events at HAMR with onsite logistics and customer service. \u2022 Perform other related duties as assigned. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Additional Requirements \u2022 Strong communication and customer service skills. \u2022 Excellent organization, attention to detail, and reliability. \u2022 Experience with event setup or facilities support (preferred but not required). \u2022 Comfort with inventory management and basic tracking tools (e.g., Excel, SharePoint). \u2022 Basic knowledge of A/V equipment setup. \u2022 Ability to work collaboratively, take initiative, and meet deadlines. Additional Information Ability to lift and carry up to 25 lbs. Ability to move, transport, and/or deliver items, supplies, or equipment. Students must have their own transportation, as some local travel between facilities may be required. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) b56be934 Last Name (required) f6b1e7e3 Email (required) f57ffd99 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 9f5b3bcb Last Name (required) 97f0a77c Email (required) 4b6f8c34 Job Alert 564976fe Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messa