tters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 7371e301 Last Name (required) 5d7ff3c3 Email (required) 61493d72 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-animal-ecology-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor - Animal Ecology", "description": "Assistant Professor - Animal Ecology - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor - Animal Ecology - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor - Animal Ecology College of Liberal Arts & Sciences | Faculty Assistant Professor - Animal Ecology 499478 On Site Faculty Department: Department of Biological Sciences Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $70,000 Work Schedule: M-F 8-5; Variable dependent on schedule; work is performed on-site and in person Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Position Overview: The Department of Biological Sciences in the Fairmount College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at Wichita State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Animal Ecology. We welcome applicants whose research focuses on vertebrate or invertebrate systems across any area of animal ecology, including behavioral ecology. We are particularly interested in applicants who will include use of the WSU Field Stations in their teaching and research programs. The successful candidate will be expected to teach undergraduate and graduate courses, develop a productive research program, and provide service to the university and profession. This position is a 9-month appointment with an anticipated start date of August 2, 2027. Department Description: The Department of Biological Sciences offers majors in Biology with either an Ecological/Environmental/Organismal or a Biomedical emphasis. There are approximately 340 undergraduate majors and the department\u2019s Master of Science in Biology program currently includes 19 graduate students. There are 11 faculty members and seven full-time departmental support staff/administrators. The department is committed to excellence in teaching, research, and student success. The WSU Field Stations span four reserves totaling over 5000 acres, featuring both restored and native tall and mid-grass prairies. The Ninnescah Reserve is the base of operations for our Field Station Manager and includes research and storage/maintenance buildings. A 2025 square foot space on the Wichita main campus is dedicated to organismal biology coursework and WSU\u2019s natural history collections. The department houses modern laboratory space that includes analytical/molecular equipment, an accredited animal facility, and access to the Kansas State University and Wichita State University High Performance Computing clusters. Core Responsibilities - Teaching: Develop and teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate level in the candidate\u2019s area of expertise. This includes designing curriculum, delivering high-quality instruction, and assessing student learning. The faculty member will mentor and advise students, including supervising undergraduate and M.S. research projects. Research/Scholarly Activity: Establish and maintain an active, externally funded research program in animal ecology involving undergraduate students and M.S. graduate students. This includes publishing peer reviewed scholarly work and disseminating results in academic venues. Service: Participate in service activities within the department, college, and university, as well as in professional organizations. Service duties include committee work, curriculum development, program assessment, student recruitment, and community outreach. The faculty member will contribute to the governance and strategic initiatives of the department and may also engage in service to the broader profession. Other: Fulfill other duties as assigned, in accordance with the faculty member\u2019s talents and departmental needs. All Wichita State faculty are expected to uphold professional and ethical standards in teaching, research, and service. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Teaching: Develop and teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate level in the candidate\u2019s area of expertise. This includes designing curriculum, delivering high-quality instruction, and assessing student learning. The faculty member will mentor and advise students, including supervising undergraduate and M.S. research projects. Research/Scholarly Activity: Establish and maintain an active, externally funded research program in animal ecology involving undergraduate students and M.S. graduate students. This includes publishing peer reviewed scholarly work and disseminating results in academic venues. Service: Participate in service activities within the department, college, and university, as well as in professional organizations. Service duties include committee work, curriculum development, program assessment, student recruitment, and community outreach. The faculty member will contribute to the governance and strategic initiatives of the department and may also engage in service to the broader profession. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements PhD in Biology or related field to be completed prior to August 2027. Teaching experience is broadly defined i.e. teaching assistantships, mentoring, participation in course lectures, etc. Please clarify in your teaching statement. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to teach undergraduate and graduate classes in area of expertise. Effective written and oral communication skills. Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students. Demonstrated potential to establish an independent and productive research program. Demonstrated ability or potential to work effectively in collaborative environments and engage constructively with individuals from a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. Preferred Qualifications: Postdoctoral research experience is preferred, but strong candidates lacking postdoctoral experience will be considered. Additional Information: To apply, please complete the Faculty Profile including the names and contact information of three (3) references and upload the following documents: 1) Letter of application 2) Current curriculum vita 3) Statement of teaching philosophy and goals 4) Statement of research interests and goals 5) Copies of unofficial academic transcripts Applicants must apply by October 19, 2026 for full consideration. WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position \u2013 Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators \u2013 Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Must also have the ability to perform work under field conditions as necessary. Apply Now First Name (required) b0d4e53b Last Name (required) f4eff099 Email (required) 29a9b189 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 9da1f663 Last Name (required) 53eee568 Email (required) 1bb1580d Job Alert 3e796301 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Liberal Arts & Sciences College of Liberal Arts & Sciences Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 09c7085a Last Name (required) 11a7cb1e Email (required) 87728788 Send This Job To: 4cfb8d0f Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" \u2013 Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 03c3d6b0 Last Name (required) a13cd77a Email (required) 7f861c40 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-9-month-counseling-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor 9 month - Counseling", "description": "Assistant Professor 9 month - Counseling - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor 9 month - Counseling - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor 9 month - Counseling College of Education | Faculty Assistant Professor 9 month - Counseling 499410 On Site Faculty Department: Counseling, Educational Leadership, Educational and School Psychology (CLES) Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: $65,000 Work Schedule: Monday - Friday - afternoon and evening classes; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Counseling, Educational Leadership, Educational and School Psychology (CLES) Department in the College of Education at Wichita State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Counseling beginning August 2, 2027. We seek a counselor educator who is committed to excellence in graduate teaching, clinical supervision, scholarship, student mentorship, and service. The successful candidate will contribute to the continued growth of the Counseling Program through high-quality instruction, supervision of counseling students, an active program of research, and engagement with professional and community partners. The successful candidate will teach graduate courses in counseling in face-to-face, hybrid, and online formats. Teaching responsibilities may include counseling core courses, clinical skills courses, practicum, internship, supervision, research methods, statistics, program evaluation, assessment, dissertation preparation, or other courses aligned with the candidate\u2019s expertise and departmental needs. Candidates with expertise in research methodology, quantitative methods, qualitative methods, mixed methods, statistics, program evaluation, counselor education research, or related areas that support graduate and doctoral education are especially encouraged to apply. This position also includes supervising graduate students in clinical training experiences, advising master\u2019s and doctoral students, maintaining a productive scholarly agenda, contributing to accreditation and assessment activities, and providing service to the department, college, university, profession, and community. The Counseling, Educational Leadership, Educational and School Psychology (CLES) Department prepares highly skilled, scholarly, and socially responsible professionals who serve individuals, families, schools, organizations, and communities through counseling, leadership, education, research, and service. The department offers a range of graduate programs, including the Master of Education in Counseling, Master of Education in Educational Leadership, Doctor of Education in Educational Leadership, Master of Education in Educational Psychology, Ph.D. in Education and Behavioral Studies with tracks in Educational Psychology and Clinical Mental Health Counselor Education and Supervision, and Educational Specialist in School Psychology. The Counseling Program includes CACREP-accredited master\u2019s programs in Clinical Mental Health Counseling and School Counseling, as well as a doctoral track in Clinical Mental Health Counselor Education and Supervision. The program is also connected to the WISE Counseling Clinic, which provides supervised clinical training for graduate counseling students while offering accessible counseling services to the community. Faculty in the CLES Department work in a collaborative academic environment that values strong teaching, applied learning, clinical training, research productivity, student mentorship, interdisciplinary collaboration, and service to the profession and community. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Core Responsibilities may include: Teaching - Teach graduate courses in the Counseling Program in face-to-face, hybrid, and online formats. - Teach courses across the counseling curriculum, which may include counseling theories, counseling techniques, group counseling, career counseling, diagnosis, assessment, practicum, internship, supervision, research methods, statistics, program evaluation, dissertation preparation, or other courses based on program needs and faculty expertise. - Contribute to doctoral-level instruction, including research-related coursework and dissertation preparation, as appropriate. - Develop and deliver effective instructional materials, learning activities, and assessments. - Support applied learning experiences that prepare students for professional counseling practice, supervision, leadership, and scholarship. - Advise and mentor graduate students in academic, professional, clinical, and scholarly development. Clinical Supervision and Professional Preparation - Supervise graduate students in practicum and internship experiences, including placements in the WISE Counseling Clinic and community settings. - Support students\u2019 development of counseling skills, ethical decision-making, professional identity, and readiness for practice. - Develop, foster, and maintain relationships with community agencies, schools, clinical sites, and other professional partners to support student placements, referrals, and applied learning opportunities. - Contribute to the ongoing development and quality improvement of clinical training processes. Research and Scholarly Activity - Develop and maintain an active program of scholarly research consistent with expectations for tenure-track faculty. - Publish peer-reviewed scholarship and present research at professional conferences. - Pursue internal and external funding opportunities, as appropriate. - Mentor graduate students in research, scholarly writing, conference presentations, and dissertation development. - Contribute research expertise that strengthens the department\u2019s master\u2019s and doctoral programs. - Support departmental research capacity in areas such as counseling outcomes, counselor education, supervision, research methodology, statistics, program evaluation, assessment, or related areas. Service - Provide service to the Counseling Program, CLES Department, College, University, profession, and community. - Participate in program governance, curriculum development, recruitment, assessment, and accreditation-related activities. - Contribute to CACREP accreditation maintenance and continuous program improvement. - Engage with professional counseling organizations and related scholarly communities. - Support the department\u2019s mission through collaboration, collegiality, and professional leadership. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements Earned Doctorate or ABD from a CACREP-accredited university in counseling, and/or counselor education ( all requirements for the doctorate must be completed prior to August 2, 2027 ). Professional identity as a Counselor Educator as evidenced by affiliations with either/or the American Counseling Association (ACA), American School Counseling Association (ASCA), American Mental Health. Counselor Association (AMHCA), or the Association for Counselor Education & Supervision (ACES). LPC Licensure-eligible in the State of Kansas. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Potential for establishing a record of publication and scholarship. Commitment to fostering an environment in which all students, faculty, staff, and community partners feel welcome, valued, supported, and engaged. Knowledge of CACREP standards. Willingness to accommodate a variety of learning styles and strategies in instructional delivery and learning activities, including online and blended learning, flexible teaching methods, and applied learning approaches. Strong communication and interpersonal skills to work effectively with a broad pool students and colleagues. Ability to work collaboratively with other faculty and professionals Preferred Qualifications: Experience as a licensed professional counselor or clinical mental health counselor. Evidence of successful teaching experience in a CACREP-accredited program and experience in supervising counseling practicum and internship students. Expertise in one or more research areas such as quantitative, qualitative, mixed methods. Experience teaching research methods, statistics, program evaluation, assessment, dissertation preparation, or related graduate-level research courses. Additional Information: To apply, please complete the faculty profile which includes the names and contact information for three (3) professional references and be prepared to upload the following: 1. Cover Letter addressing how your qualifications and experience align with the position 2. Teaching Philosophy Statement 3. Research Philosophy Statement 4. Counseling Philosophy Statement Review of applications will begin November 2, 2026 and will continue until the position has been filled. WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position \u2013 Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators \u2013 Frequent 60-90% Apply Now First Name (required) 9983dc1d Last Name (required) 3aa6a9bb Email (required) a254e44b Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) b55f0519 Last Name (required) 843d2fa6 Email (required) 9b19f4e3 Job Alert ae607bd5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Education College of Education Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 3ed8c06a Last Name (required) c5a526e0 Email (required) c490d22a Send This Job To: 3f3f4d38 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" \u2013 Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 3e414bcd Last Name (required) 19684dd9 Email (required) c4715298 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-organic-chemistry-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Organic Chemistry", "description": "Assistant Professor of Organic Chemistry - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor of Organic Chemistry - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Organic Chemistry College of Liberal Arts & Sciences | Faculty Assistant Professor of Organic Chemistry 499365 On Site Faculty Department: Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Salary range begins at $74,000 Work Schedule: Monday - Friday, 8am - 5pm, may vary based on schedule; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry in the Fairmount College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at Wichita State University invites applications for a benefit-eligible, tenure-track faculty position in Organic Chemistry at the rank of Assistant Professor beginning on August 2, 2027. We seek an innovative scholar and dedicated educator who will contribute to the department's strengths in teaching, research, mentoring, and service. Wichita State values collaboration, community engagement, student success, and applied learning, and we welcome candidates whose experiences and interests will advance these goals. The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry offers ACS-certified undergraduate degree programs in Chemistry and Biochemistry and graduate programs leading to the M.S. and Ph.D. degrees in Chemistry. The department is committed to excellence in teaching, research, and student mentoring. Faculty enjoy extensive opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration both within the department and across Wichita State University. The department maintains a strong culture of undergraduate and graduate research and supports student access to a broad range of modern research instrumentation. Shared facilities include a recently installed Bruker 500 MHz NMR spectrometer and advanced analytical instrumentation. Faculty and students also have access to Wichita State's high-performance computing resources to support computational and data-intensive research. Faculty also benefit from opportunities for collaboration with researchers and clinicians across Wichita State's growing health sciences enterprise and the University of Kansas Medical Center (KUMC). Wichita State is a founding partner in the new Wichita Biomedical Campus, a transformative downtown development that will bring together Wichita State, WSU Tech, KU School of Medicine-Wichita, and the KU School of Pharmacy in a shared environment designed to strengthen interdisciplinary education, research, and innovation in the health sciences. The campus will provide new opportunities for collaborations spanning chemistry, biochemistry, medicinal chemistry, drug discovery, health sciences, and biomedical research. Additional opportunities for collaboration exist through Wichita State's nationally recognized Innovation Campus, which brings together faculty, students, industry partners, entrepreneurs, and community organizations in a unique environment that promotes innovation, workforce development, and applied research. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Core Responsibilities \u2022 Teaching: Develop and teach courses at the undergraduate and/or graduate level in Organic Chemistry. This includes designing curriculum and instructional materials, delivering high-quality instruction in various modalities (in-person, online, or hybrid), and assessing student learning. The faculty member will mentor and advise undergraduate and graduate (MS and PhD) students, including supervising research projects or theses as appropriate, and incorporate applied learning opportunities into the coursework whenever possible. \u2022 Research/Scholarly Activity: Establish and maintain an active research program in Organic or Medicinal Chemistry. This includes publishing peer-reviewed scholarly work and disseminating results in academic venues. The faculty member is expected to seek external funding (grants or industry collaboration) to support research activities and, where applicable, engage in interdisciplinary projects or partnerships with industry. Excellence in scholarship should be demonstrated by a record of research accomplishments or clear potential for high-quality research output. \u2022 Service: Participate in service activities within the department, college, and university, as well as in professional organizations. Service duties include committee work, curriculum development, program assessment, student recruitment, and community outreach. The faculty member will contribute to the governance and strategic initiatives of the department and may also engage in service to the broader profession (e.g. reviewing for journals, involvement in academic societies). \u2022 Other, if applicable: Fulfill other duties as assigned, in accordance with the faculty member\u2019s talents and departmental needs. All Wichita State faculty are expected to uphold professional and ethical standards in teaching, research, and service. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements Ph.D. in Organic Chemistry, Medicinal Chemistry, Chemical Biology, or a closely related field by the start date of employment. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students. Demonstrated potential to establish an independent and productive research program. Demonstrated ability or potential to work effectively in collaborative environments and engage constructively with individuals from a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. Preferred Qualifications: Postdoctoral or equivalent research experience. A record of scholarly productivity appropriate to career stage. Experience mentoring student researchers. Experience obtaining or contributing to externally funded research projects. Interest in developing interdisciplinary collaborations across academic, government, healthcare, or industry sectors Additional Information: Priority will be given to completed applications received by November 1, 2026. Review will continue until the position is filled. Application Materials In addition to a curriculum vitae, applicants should submit the following materials: Cover Letter - A cover letter describing your interest in the position and how your qualifications, experiences, and career goals align with the responsibilities and expectations of this faculty appointment. Teaching Statement (1-2 pages) - A statement describing your teaching philosophy, formal and informal teaching experiences, and plans for effective instruction and mentoring. Applicants should also identify undergraduate and graduate courses they are prepared to teach and/or develop. Research Statement (maximum 5 pages) - A statement outlining your research accomplishments, current interests, and future research directions. The statement should describe plans for establishing an independent, externally funded research program and highlight opportunities for involving undergraduate and graduate students. Applicants are encouraged to discuss potential interdisciplinary collaborations and connections with industry relevant to Wichita State University. WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position \u2013 Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators \u2013 Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Sedentary: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. Sedentary work involves remaining stationary most of the time. Apply Now First Name (required) 08da230c Last Name (required) 62235052 Email (required) ed8244a1 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 766ce420 Last Name (required) 4a2e6ae0 Email (required) 01e26275 Job Alert 7b00ee3a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Liberal Arts & Sciences College of Liberal Arts & Sciences Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 11e341c3 Last Name (required) 6bc60bc1 Email (required) 0aba95bb Send This Job To: 46fee6d1 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" \u2013 Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 88214b95 Last Name (required) a4dd4326 Email (required) 35523c03 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-accounting-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Accounting", "description": "Assistant Professor of Accounting - Wichita, Kansas, United States Assistant Professor of Accounting - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Accounting Barton School of Business | Faculty Assistant Professor of Accounting 499619 On Site Faculty Work Authorization and Immigration Sponsorship Wichita State University may be able to sponsor certain faculty positions for employment-based immigration status where authorized by the hiring department and university policy. Sponsorship eligibility varies by faculty position and will be identified in the individual job posting. For faculty positions eligible for sponsorship, international candidates generally must be eligible for sponsorship in a visa classification compatible with the faculty position. For tenured and tenure-track faculty appointments, visa classifications incompatible with such appointments include F-1 Optional Practical Training (OPT), J-1 Research Scholar, and J-1 Academic Training statuses. Department: School of Accountancy Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Salary set at $170,000/yr Work Schedule: Dependent on class and research schedule;work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The candidate will have an exciting opportunity to help shape the future of accounting education and research at Wichita State University. The position will play an important role in advancing the School of Accountancy, strengthening partnerships with the accounting profession and broader business community, and contributing to the development of innovative academic and applied-learning initiatives that respond to the evolving needs of the accounting profession. The Barton School of Business is accredited through AACSB International in both business and accounting. Fewer than 1% of business schools worldwide hold this double accreditation. The School of Accountancy in the W. Frank Barton School of Business at Wichita State University invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-track position as Assistant Professor of Accounting, beginning August 8, 2027. Candidates will contribute to our growing undergraduate and Master of Accountancy (MAcc) programs that prepare students for successful careers in public accounting, industry, government, and nonprofit organizations. The candidate will join a collaborative academic environment committed to excellence in teaching, impactful scholarship, student success, and meaningful engagement with employers and the accounting profession. The School of Accountancy has strong relationships in the community, creating dynamic relationships for research, students and so much more. Barton School of Business at Wichita State University places applied learning at the center of student experience. Every degree program at Wichita State includes a guaranteed applied learning or research experience, providing students with opportunities to develop relevant professional skills and meaningful experience before graduation. The successful candidate will have opportunities to integrate these experiences into accounting education through industry-engaged projects, experiential learning, research, internships, and partnerships with the regional business and accounting community. Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for research, teaching, and service as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties A candidate is expected to: 1. Teaching : Teach two courses per semester (four courses per academic year) in the School of Accountancy at the undergraduate and graduate levels, with courses offered in in-person, hybrid, and online formats. Teaching assignments will be based on the candidate's expertise and program needs and may include courses across a broad range of accounting disciplines. The successful candidate will also contribute to curriculum development, assessment, continuous improvement, and the advising and mentoring of undergraduate and graduate students. 2. Research : Develop and maintain an active and sustainable research program consistent with AACSB Scholarly Academic (SA) expectations and the requirements for tenure and promotion at the Barton School of Business. The successful candidate will be expected to produce high-quality scholarly research with the potential for publication in respected and leading journals in accounting or closely related fields and to disseminate research through appropriate academic and professional venues. Collaborate with faculty colleagues, students, and external partners on scholarly initiatives when appropriate. 3. Applied Learning and Professional Engagement : Incorporate applied and experiential learning into course design and develop meaningful opportunities for students to engage with the accounting profession and broader business community through applied projects, case studies, employer engagement, internships, professional organizations, and other experiential learning activities. 4. Service and Engagement : Contribute meaningful service to the School of Accountancy, Barton School of Business, university, profession, and broader community. Service may include participation in committees, accreditation and curriculum assessment, student mentoring, student recruitment and retention initiatives, professional organizations, employer partnerships, advisory activities, community outreach, and other activities that advance the mission of the School and Barton School. Required Education and Experience: Terminal degree in direct field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements Earned a doctorate (Ph.D., D.B.A., or equivalent terminal degree) in Accounting or a closely related field. Applicants who are at an advanced stage of their doctoral studies (ABD) will be considered if they provide strong evidence that all degree requirements will be completed prior to August 2027. Evidence of an established record of scholarly research or a strong research pipeline with demonstrated potential for sustained publication in high-quality accounting or related academic journals consistent with the expectations of an AACSB-accredited institution. Evidence of effective teaching in accounting or related areas at the university level. Evidence may include teaching evaluations, course development, applied-learning activities, instructional technologies or software, experience with multiple instructional delivery formats, or other indicators of teaching effectiveness. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to provide instruction curriculum to a variety of learners. Commitment to collaborative processes and environments, with students, faculty and community patners. Demonstrated ability to mentor students and contribute to student success. Excellent written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills. Commitment to student success and inclusive excellence in the field. Preferred Qualifications: Professional certification, such as a CPA, and/or significant professional accounting experience. Doctoral degree completed or in progress at an AACSB-accredited institution. Experience incorporating emerging technologies, analytics, artificial intelligence, or related innovations into accounting education or research. Pursue externally funded or industry-supported research. Experience with applied learning, interdisciplinary collaboration, or meaningful engagement with the accounting profession. Additional Information: W ork Authorization and Immigration Sponsorship Wichita State University may be able to sponsor certain faculty positions for employment-based immigration status where authorized by the hiring department and university policy. Sponsorship eligibility varies by faculty position and will be identified in the individual job posting. For faculty positions eligible for sponsorship, international candidates generally must be eligible for sponsorship in a visa classification compatible with the faculty position. For tenured and tenure-track faculty appointments, visa classifications incompatible with such appointments include F-1 Optional Practical Training (OPT), J-1 Research Scholar, and J-1 Academic Training statuses. REQUIRED MATERIALS 1. Cover Letter/Letter of application addressing how the candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience align with the position. 2. Teaching Statement: A statement (1-2 pages) describing teaching approach/philosophy and experience (including course topics the candidate can teach, mentoring experience, and any evidence of teaching effectiveness). 3. Research Statement: A statement (1-2 pages) describing research approach/philosophy and experience. A priority deadline for application review is October 31, 2026. The appointment for the position is August 2027. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position \u2013 Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators \u2013 Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Apply Now First Name (required) 88d2fb2f Last Name (required) 273515aa Email (required) 9c2e7db8 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) caa65397 Last Name (required) a09cb4ad Email (required) b2032959 Job Alert 2bb684ee Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) Barton School of Business Barton School of Business Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) eb5daaa2 Last Name (required) 38ee229e Email (required) 2fe81794 Send This Job To: 89415088 Share