equired to support events.;work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story Are you a legal professional seeking a meaningful leadership role that supports a healthy work-life balance? Would you be interested in a position that allows you to have a direct impact on student success? If so, Wichita State University is seeking a dynamic and experienced legal professional to serve as the inaugural Manager of Student Legal Services! This leadership role provides direct legal services to students and support of the strategic oversight of the newly established program. This position is ideal for a licensed attorney with courtroom experience, a strong public service orientation, and the ability to lead a small team in a dynamic, student-centered environment. The successful candidate will have strong communication, leadership, and program development skills. Job Summary Manage, coordinate, and administer the day-to-day activities of student legal services programs and services. Oversee the implementation and evaluation of student legal services, ensuring alignment with University goals and initiatives and compliance with applicable rules and regulations. Essential Functions \u2022 Provide legal consultations, advocacy, and full legal representation to eligible students on a variety of criminal and civil matters; including performing conflict of interest checks related to representation. \u2022 Design and conduct student education, training and outreach initiatives in alignment with programming goals and objectives. \u2022 Establish sustainable processes, key performance metrics, management tools and reporting capabilities. Utilize data to develop new or revise current programs and services. Communicate quality and progress metrics to department, staff, and/or stakeholders. \u2022 Cultivate new and expand existing strategic partnerships and lead initiatives to support program success. Consult with stakeholders to assess needs and ensure effective support. \u2022 Oversee program budget according to needs. Monitor and adjust plans as resource requirements change. \u2022 Supervise assigned staff; including performance management, work allocation, training, promotion and enforcement of internal procedures and controls, and problem resolution. Evaluate performance and make recommendations for staff actions. Required Education and Experience: Juris Doctorate degree from an American Bar Association (ABA) accredited institution and admission to the Kansas State Bar Four (4) years of experience as a practicing attorney, with one (1) year in a leadership role. Required License/Certifications/Training: Licensed to practice law in the state of Kansas. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Public speaking Legal writing and research Strong Interpersonal skills Document management Presentation Skills Regulatory compliance Report writing Risk Management Additional Information: WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position. Frequent 60-90% Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Frequent 60-90% Ability to interpret effectively, accurately and impartially, both receptively and expressively. Frequent 60-90% Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Sedentary: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. Sedentary work involves remaining stationary most of the time. Apply Now First Name (required) 514f3d89 Last Name (required) 73c4ef25 Email (required) d6608439 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information a