 with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) e9459d49 Last Name (required) 83c3aaae Email (required) c23bceed Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/lighting-sound-and-projection-design-assnt-educator-teaching-professor-performing-arts-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Lighting, Sound, and Projection Design - Assnt Educator/Teaching Professor -Performing Arts", "description": "Lighting, Sound, and Projection Design - Assnt Educator/Teaching Professor -Performing Arts - Wichita, Kansas, United States Lighting, Sound, and Projection Design - Assnt Educator/Teaching Professor -Performing Arts - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Lighting, Sound, and Projection Design - Assnt Educator/Teaching Professor -Performing Arts College of Fine Arts | Faculty Lighting, Sound, and Projection Design - Assnt Educator/Teaching Professor -Performing Arts 499385 On Site Faculty WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. Department: School of Performing Arts Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Commensurate with qualifications and experience. Work Schedule: Varied depending upon class, rehearsal, and production schedule; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: No export control requirement. Job Story The School of Performing Arts is a comprehensive school offering BFA and BA degrees in Performing Arts with concentrations in Acting, Dance, Design and Technical Theatre, Musical Theatre, and Theatre. Grounded in a shared core curriculum, the school emphasizes collaboration across disciplines and extensive applied learning opportunities. A hallmark of the School of Performing Arts is its commitment to undergraduate leadership through production curriculum, with students actively designing, performing, managing, and producing work across a diverse range of artistic projects. To enhance and broaden students\u2019 knowledge and career preparation, the School of Performing Arts offers several certificates, including Directing, Stage Management, Voice Acting, Choreography, and Commercial Dance. Students may also pursue interdisciplinary minors such as Dance, Dance Education, Dance and Psychology, Drama and Psychology, Theatre, Musical Theatre, Performing Arts and Business, and Performing Arts Marketing. Many of these programs and courses are developed in collaboration with the School of Digital Arts, the School of Music, the Honors College, and the Fairmount College of Liberal Arts and Sciences, reinforcing an interdisciplinary approach and expanding opportunities for students to engage across fields and build versatile, career-ready skill sets. Learn more at www.wichita.edu/spa The School of Performing Arts in the College of Fine Arts invites applications for a full-time (9 month), non-tenure track position in Lighting, Sound, and Projection to begin August 2027 with the university. We seek an experienced and dynamic educator, mentor, designer, and artistic leader who will play a central role in shaping the future of design and production within a highly collaborative interdisciplinary performing arts environment. This position offers a unique opportunity to develop sound and projection curriculum, mentor emerging designers, foster undergraduate creative leadership, and contribute to a vibrant production culture. Because production is central to the school's applied curriculum and mission, this position serves as both an artistic and educational leader. Rather than functioning primarily as a production designer, the successful candidate will mentor and guide student designers in lighting, sound, and projection across theatre, musical theatre, dance, film, and interdisciplinary projects. Through coaching, artistic supervision, and collaborative project development, they will help students translate classroom learning into meaningful creative practice while building professional portfolios and leadership skills. The Wichita State Advantage Located in Wichita, Kansas, the School of Performing Arts offers faculty the opportunity to work within a close-knit and highly collaborative artistic community where professionals and alumni actively lead area theatres, dance studios, and arts organizations. These relationships create meaningful partnerships that support student internships, applied learning, and community-engaged work, while also providing faculty with strong professional networks beyond the university. Wichita offers an affordable quality of life paired with a community of scholars, creators, and professionals. Employees can build meaningful connections with colleagues while enjoying a cost of living that supports personal and professional well-being. Together, these qualities create an environment where people can thrive and feel connected. The city features a growing and vibrant arts ecosystem, including regional theatres, dance companies, music venues, film and media initiatives, and a nationally recognized downtown arts district. Faculty benefit from access to local cultural institutions, galleries, public art, and festivals, as well as a central location that offers convenient travel options. This combination of affordability, accessibility, and an engaged creative community make Wichita an appealing place to live, work, and build a meaningful career in the performing arts. Learn more: www.choosewichita.com Job Summary Teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels using various instructional deliveries (e.g., traditional (face-to-face), hybrid, and fully online). To foster applied learning into the course design and engage with industry and local business community applied projects. To advance knowledge through scholarly activities (e.g., active involvement in committees, student mentorship, recruitment and retention initiative, outreach activities, etc.) Essential Functions Meet expectations for teaching and service, as set forth by the department and college. Job Duties Core Responsibilities Develop and teach lighting technology and design courses while helping expand curricular opportunities in sound design, projection design, and emerging media practices. Teaching responsibilities include designing curriculum and instructional materials, delivering high-quality instruction in various modalities (in-person, online, or hybrid), and assessing student learning. Through classroom instruction, advising, and production mentorship, they will help students develop the artistic, technical, and collaborative skills necessary for successful careers in the performing arts. Lighting and sound are foundational elements of every production season and support all performance venues and degree programs. In addition to teaching responsibilities, the faculty member will engage in significant service through leadership in lighting and electrical safety and supervise student interns in a lighting shop and production environments. Required Education and Experience: Graduate level degree or Equivalent Experience in the Field Teaching experience Faculty Requirements Evidence of achievement in lighting design. Evidence of achievement in sound design. Evidence of experience in projection design. Demonstrated ability to teach undergraduate courses in lighting and sound design. Demonstrated ability to use and teach industry standard software such as Vectorworks, Dante, Lightwright, QLab, etc. Demonstrated ability to use and teach industry standard hardware to include ETC Family Lighting Consoles. Demonstrated ability to teach and apply current industry standards and best practices related to audio production, including the legal and ethical use of sound libraries, licensed music, copyrighted materials, intellectual property, and digital media assets. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Familiar with production in a variety of settings such as a proscenium theatre, black box theatre, site specific locations and film. Ability to provide instruction curriculum to a variety of learners. Commitment to collaborative processes and environments. Preferred Qualifications: MFA in Theatre/Design and Technical Theatre with a focus in lighting and sound design; OR BA/BFA in Theatre/Design and Technical Theatre with commensurate professional experience in lighting and sound design. Professional experience as a lighting and sound designer. Three years\u2019 teaching experience at full-time or equivalent course load in higher education. Evidence of achievement in projection/media design. Experience supervising student interns/employees. Ability to teach theatre courses beyond lighting and sound technology. Additional Information: WSU is not able to provide immigration sponsorship for this position. REQUIRED MATERIALS 1. Cover Letter/Letter of application addressing how the candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience align with the position. 2. Teaching Statement: A statement (1-2 pages) describing teaching approach/philosophy and experience (including course topics the candidate can teach, mentoring experience, and any evidence of teaching effectiveness). 3. Digital Portfolio: File or link to file(s) or website of professional digital work 4. Optional Materials: Any additional materials the candidate would like to share such as sample publications, teaching evaluations, reviews, etc. Priority deadline for applications is 10/16/26. The appointment for the position is August 2027. For more information contact: Professor Amy Baker Schwiethale, Chair - Assistant Teaching Professor/Educator of Performing Arts \u2013 Lighting, Sound & Projection, Email: amy.baker@wichita.edu Physical Requirements: Ability to remain in a stationary position \u2013 Frequent 60-90%; Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators \u2013 Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Requires the ability to safely hang, focus, install, and maintain lighting, sound, and projection equipment. Must be able to climb ladders, work at heights, and lift up to 50 pounds. Apply Now First Name (required) 984e5f83 Last Name (required) 73fa5d84 Email (required) 52f34295 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 0df028d6 Last Name (required) 27b1bfe2 Email (required) f1cde116 Job Alert 8b397d7d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Department(s) College of Fine Arts College of Fine Arts Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 93ee5df7 Last Name (required) 1c4a544a Email (required) 216da499 Send This Job To: abe2074a Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Senior Purchasing Agent \"An office is a place where dreams come true\" \u2013 Michael Scott. Do you enjoy solving problems, building relationships, and helping organizations make smart purchasing decisions? Are you interested in a career that combines strategy, compliance, customer service, and business operations? Litigation Paralegal and Contracts Manager Keep the details sharp. The process moving. The university protected. The Office of General Counsel needs a highly organized, thoughtful professional who can bring structure to complex legal matters while keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 106ed1a4 Last Name (required) 792b0af0 Email (required) 9ac13f41 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests