ped to perform, automated inspection, robotic processing, automated damage repair. Alongside developing these systems, you will be responsible for enabling digital twin technologies through simulation, verification, and closed loop sustainment. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Additional Requirements Pursuing a Bachelor' s or Master's degree. Enthusiastic and willing to learn from a variety of specialist in the field of intelligent manufacturing. Must be able to work a minimum of 20 hours a week. Ability to work well in a team environment and effectively communicate ideas and solutions. Self-motivated and able to work without constant supervision. Ability to lift and carry up to 25lbs. Strong organizational and time-management skills. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) f6e19ba8 Last Name (required) 67730c6c Email (required) 9bd9f785 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 1fc08334 Last Name (required) 07e47f73 Email (required) 1a6e6d76 Job Alert f89d3c15 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institu