oth independently and collaboratively, demonstrating a responsible work ethic and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. You take ownership of your work, consistently completing projects on time and meeting established deadlines while maintaining accuracy and attention to detail. You are a critical thinker who not only executes tasks but also identifies opportunities to improve processes and enhance outcomes. With the courage to speak up, you confidently share ideas, insights, and recommendations that contribute to continuous improvement and innovation within the team. You communicate clearly and professionally, building strong relationships with peers and stakeholders. You collaborate effectively, contribute to team success, and remain flexible when priorities shift. You are comfortable thinking on your feet and in your seat responding to challenges with creativity, sound judgment, and a proactive approach. Above all, you go above and beyond to support the mission of our WSU HR Department consistently demonstrating initiative, adaptability, and a commitment to excellence. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties \u2022 Understanding the aspects of professional development and gaining knowledge of related resources \u2022 Developing, updating, editing, and producing learning materials \u2022 Creating training modules in an online platform \u2022 Improving the usability and accessibility of training materials \u2022 Delivering classroom and virtual training modules \u2022 Preparing classroom learning materials \u2022 Assisting with developing and updating content for learning courses \u2022 Assisting with production of online learning pathways \u2022 Assisting with professional development marketing and communications \u2022 Other duties as directed Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements \u2022 Availability for 20 hours per week between 8 a.m.-5 p.m. Monday-Friday during academic year and summer \u2022 Must be proficient with English grammar and writing skills \u2022 Intermediate skills with Microsoft Office Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and/or preferences. Preferred Qualifications Student from various academic areas such as HR Management, Communications, Marketing, Business Administration, or Information Technology An interest in learning about professional development and adult learning Experience using Articulate, Captivate, or other course content creation software Experience developing creative PowerPoint presentations Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 880ede26 Last Name (required) 396eb21b Email (required) a7a5cafa Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 72fd8d21 Last Name (required) ddb1d305 Email (required) 79cadfb5 Job Alert 98a70c8c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at th