t communicator, we want you on our team -- Apply today! Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties 1. Attending all Tutor Training sessions at the beginning and ending of each semester. 2. Checking your email inbox regularly unless notified otherwise. 3. Providing weekly tutoring in at least one subject to students assigned to you. 4. Assisting in the development of positive study habits, study skills, and learning modalities of tutored students. 5. Providing regular feedback to SSS Academic Advisors on your student\u2019s academic progress. 6. Completing and submitting your Weekly Progress Assessments and web time sheets electronically by the due date as required. 7. Attending a Mid-Semester Conference with all students you are tutoring and their advisors. 8. Contributing to the continuous improvement of the quality of the tutorial process. 9. Completing a Tutor Perception survey at the end of each academic year, or the last semester you tutor. 10. Actively participating in related activities of the tutorial component to achieve the required outcomes of Student Support Services. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements Minimum Requirements: - Enrolled as a sophomore, junior, senior or graduate student at WSU - Have a cumulative 3.0 GPA or better - Earned a grade of B- or better in the courses student will be tutoring Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications - Good communication skills. - A strong desire to help first generation, limited income students and students with disabilities. - All applications accepted, but preference will be given to students who can tutor in Accounting, Economics, Biology, Chemistry, Physics, and Spanish. Additional Information Please update 'advertising copy' to reflect the advertised pay of $13.00 per hour. Thank you. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 29bd756b Last Name (required) 6f78d435 Email (required) ca2753a7 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) aaaadf3e Last Name (required) 306f69b1 Email (required) a98d2774 Job Alert 5266cafb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic/Student Support Student Academic/Student Support Student Department(s) Strategic Engagement & Planning Strategic Engagement & Planning Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 890c94fe Last Name (required) b402190d Email (required) 02f2f