d to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a \u201cU.S. Citizen\u201d. Job Story Looking to gain hands-on experience with advanced computing, research technologies, and data systems while building skills that are highly valued in today's technology workforce? We are seeking Shockers who are interested in developing technical, analytical, and professional skills through a paid applied learning student position. This opportunity provides real-world experience supporting Wichita State University's advanced computing and research infrastructure, including high-performance computing (HPC) and research cyberinfrastructure services used by students, faculty, and researchers across a variety of disciplines. Students will gain experience working in Linux-based environments, assisting users, solving technical challenges, creating documentation, and supporting research-focused technology services. Through this applied learning experience, students will strengthen their problem-solving abilities, technical communication skills, and understanding of professional IT support practices while contributing to the university's research and innovation mission. Supervision and mentorship will ensure meaningful experiences that align with academic preparation and career goals. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Applied Learning position provides practice in developing technical and professional competencies through: \u2022 supporting users of research computing and data systems \u2022 troubleshooting account access, software environment, and system usage issues \u2022 applying analytical and problem-solving skills to diagnose and resolve technical concerns \u2022 working in Linux-based and scientific computing environments \u2022 creating, updating, and maintaining user documentation and knowledge resources \u2022 developing technical communication skills through interactions with students, faculty, and researchers \u2022 monitoring system status and escalating issues through established support procedures \u2022 gaining experience with research software ecosystems and computing workflows \u2022 maintaining accurate records of support requests, activities, and resolutions \u2022 collaborating with professional staff on projects that support research and instructional computing services Assistance may include responding to service requests, onboarding new users, developing training materials, documenting procedures, participating in technology-related projects, supporting workshops or outreach activities, and performing other duties as assigned. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements US Citizen Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and/or preferences. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 8cefff06 Last Name (required) 18b7d531 Email (required) e9b961b0 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) b336c67e Last Name (required) 92e9099c Email (requ