success-center-wichita-kansas-united-states-6a76ea89-e375-4b65-bbcb-c31292ec7ba4": {"title": "Work Study Only- Student Assistant- Business Student Success Center", "description": "Work Study Only- Student Assistant- Business Student Success Center - Wichita, Kansas, United States Work Study Only- Student Assistant- Business Student Success Center - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Work Study Only- Student Assistant- Business Student Success Center Barton School of Business | Student Work Study Only- Student Assistant- Business Student Success Center 499562 Student Department Business Student Success Center Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $10.00 per hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Flexible hours available Monday - Friday 8 AM to 5 PM Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Looking for a flexible, on campus job to help develop your professional and customer service skills while working in a friendly and supportive environment? The Barton School of Business Student Success Center in Woolsey Hall is looking for a work study eligible student assistant to join our team to help staff our front desk to welcome guests, schedule student appointments, and assist with outreach to current and prospective students among other tasks. All majors are invited to apply! Normal office hours are Monday through Friday from 8 AM to 5 PM but work schedules are flexible around your class schedule. Student workers can expect to be scheduled 10-20 hours per week on average. Must be federal work study eligible. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Provide coverage for the front desk including welcoming guests, answering phones, transfer calls, take messages, and contacting students to schedule appointments. Assist with projects as required (i.e. prepare materials for distribution, create spreadsheets, event set-up, etc.) Assist the Director of Advising and other staff as requested. Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Additional Information Must be approved for federal work study aid through FAFSA. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) a1254918 Last Name (required) 7d5ef891 Email (required) c8b8fe5e Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 2c2afea7 Last Name (required) 0be85020 Email (required) a244034e Job Alert b6ee776f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Barton School of Business Barton School of Business Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Messa