dent Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 966b3ec8 Last Name (required) e50258b7 Email (required) 8233c8aa Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/environmental-health-and-safety-compliance-specialist-senior-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "Environmental Health and Safety Compliance Specialist, Senior", "description": "Environmental Health and Safety Compliance Specialist, Senior - Wichita, Kansas, United States Environmental Health and Safety Compliance Specialist, Senior - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode Environmental Health and Safety Compliance Specialist, Senior Physical Plant | Staff Environmental Health and Safety Compliance Specialist, Senior 499394 Staff Department: Facilities Services Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Starting at $29.45 per hour and commensurate with experience Work Schedule: 7:45 am - 4:30 pm Monday - Friday; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a \u201cU.S. Citizen\u201d. Job Story We are excited to announce an opportunity for a Senior Environmental Health and Safety Compliance Specialist to join our university community and play a vital role in fostering a safe, healthy, and compliant campus environment. This position coordinates with various areas to complete assigned environmental health and safety functions and inspections. Provides guidance and assistance and is responsible for promoting a safe and healthy workplace. Implements plans based on contracts, regulations, applicable laws and audit/inspection results to ensure that compliance is maintained. May provide training to employees in areas including, but not limited to, environmental, health and safety management best practices, and assisting with hazard identification and control. Job Summary Coordinates with various areas to complete assigned environmental health and safety functions and inspections. Provides guidance and assistance and is responsible for promoting a safe and healthy workplace. Implements plans based on contracts, regulations, applicable laws and audit/inspection results to ensure that compliance is maintained. May provide training to employees in areas including, but not limited to, environmental, health and safety management best practices, and assisting with hazard identification and control. Essential Functions \u2022 Leads and/or coordinates investigations of safety related incidents involving applicable University and/or community partners. Audits and ensures safety plans are in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. \u2022 Conducts audits of lab/department. Generates audit reports for corrective action as needed. \u2022 Maintains records for and ensures compliance with regulatory requirements. Communicates on safety related needs and develops program action plans. \u2022 Reviews and analyzes safety-related data. Prepares reports for regulatory agencies, committees and/or leadership. \u2022 Manages a hazardous materials and waste program that complies with all regulatory and requirements. \u2022 Provides educational training related to safety and emergency preparedness practices. \u2022 Coordinates and/or facilitates project tasks as assigned; Documents and tracks project progress compared to goal Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent Seven (7) years of related experience. Every 30 hours of college coursework can be substituted for one (1) year of experience, up to 120 hours. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of deep, practical understanding of local, state, and federal regulations (e.g., OSHA, EPA, DOT). Knowledge of occupational health hazards, including chemical exposure limits, ergonomics, and noise/air monitoring. Ability to perform Root Cause Analysis (RCA) and develop corrective and preventive actions. Knowledge and proficiency in utilizing EHS software platforms, analyzing safety metrics, and generating compliance reports. Ability to coach, influence, and drive a proactive safety culture across all levels of the organization\u2014from floor workers to senior executives. Skill to translate complex technical and regulatory findings into actionable, clear policies and training programs. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in science related field. Additional Information: Due to ITAR regulations, the chosen candidate must be a US Citizen to be considered for this role. Physical Requirements: Ability to ascend and descend ladders and/or stairs. Frequent 60-90% Ability to inspect work, materials, equipment, and/or supplies and identify any errors, needs, and/or determining factors. Frequent 60-90% Ability to remain in a stationary position. Rare 0-30% Ability to use tools, equipment, and technology necessary to do the job. This includes dexterity in instrument manipulation. Frequent 60-90% Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Medium Work: Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally and/or up to 20 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force to constantly move objects. Apply Now First Name (required) 2739d948 Last Name (required) d0c7c482 Email (required) 9dee12fa Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 07cd3e29 Last Name (required) 4e92ff4b Email (required) fee26c69 Job Alert 3ad8815e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staff Department(s) Physical Plant Physical Plant Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State Un