s ITS Telecommunications Student Assistant - Back Office - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode ITS Telecommunications Student Assistant - Back Office Information Technology | Student ITS Telecommunications Student Assistant - Back Office 499611 Student Department Information Technology Services - Telecommunications Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay From $11 to $12 per hour, dependent on experience. Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Dependent on Class Schedule, during Office hours of Mon-Fri, 8AM-5PM Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a \u201cU.S. Citizen\u201d. Job Story ITS Telecommunications Student Assistant: Telecommunications is part of WSU\u2019s Information Technology Services. We provide and support telephone and network connectivity for all WSU locations. This is a regular student position. Students of all majors are encouraged to apply. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Duties will vary but include the following: \u00b7 Data collection/connection audits. \u00b7 Connection updates. \u00b7 Materials receiving, sorting and inventory. \u00b7 Telephone testing. \u00b7 Office tasks such as recycling, cleaning, filing, and running errands. \u00b7 Assist technicians with work orders Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements Required skills: \u00b7 Familiarity with Microsoft office suite. \u00b7 Experience working with a team and independently. We need a time commitment of at least 20 hours a week during our normal business hours, weekdays 8am to 5pm. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications This is an entry-level position, however, preference given to applicants that can demonstrate previous experience in the following areas: \u00b7 Previous technical work experience (not limited to IT fields). \u00b7 Customer service experience. \u00b7 Experience reading blue prints. \u00b7 Experience with Microsoft Visio. \u00b7 Experience using hand tools. Additional Information Former students in this position that have demonstrated technical and organizational abilities have developed into student technicians. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 957de915 Last Name (required) c57bf9b9 Email (required) b69726cd Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) ae34cd71 Last Name (required) c30e7acd Email (required) 394f606e Job Alert 48be0680 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Information Technology Information Technology Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submi