nt WSU 0350R", "description": "NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R - Wichita, Kansas, United States NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R Information Technology | Student NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R 499572 Student Department Information Technology Services - Telecommunications Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay From $11 to $12 per hour, dependent on experience. Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Dependent on Class Schedule, during Office hours of Mon-Fri, 8AM-5PM Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story ITS Telecommunications Student Administrative Assistant: Telecommunications is part of WSU\u2019s Information Technology Services. We provide and support telephone and network connectivity for all WSU locations. This is a regular student position. Students of all majors are encouraged to apply. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties The ITS Telecommunications group provides voice and data services to support the University's mission. We support thousands of network and voice connections, cabling and fiber optic infrastructure throughout Wichita State\u2019s main and satellite campuses. This position is listed as part time. That means 40 hours through the spring, summer and winter breaks and 30 hours (20 hours for international students) during the semesters. Student workers must be available to start within 2 weeks. We will be interviewing during the application process and may close this listing early if viable candidates are found. Job Purpose: The ITS Telecommunications student admin is an entry-level position. The person in this position will perform routine tasks, participate in projects, and gain technical working skills. To apply for this position, you MUST have excellent Microsoft Office skills. You should know how to open and modify a Word document, enter formulas in Excel and navigate through Outlook. Job responsibilities: \u00b7 Answer and route phone calls for the department \u00b7 Enter all work orders into the department software system \u00b7 Reset caller ID's for University phones; reset voicemail passwords; create long distance PIN codes \u00b7 Audit systems weekly and daily to ensure all work orders are entered \u00b7 Monthly billing entry \u00b7 Errands for the department \u00b7 Procedure update and creation \u00b7 Monitoring of shared inbox Equipment used: \u00b7 Computer \u00b7 Telephone \u00b7 Calculator Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements \u00b7 Typing, computer skills, office knowledge \u00b7 Microsoft Office experience \u00b7 Ability to work independently \u00b7 Demonstrated ability to learn Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications \u00b7 Advanced experience using Microsoft Office and learning from an advanced user \u00b7 Ability to interact effectively with customers \u00b7 Knowledge of office responsibilities \u00b7 Customer service experience Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 31393f7b Last Name (required) ee9e726f Email (required) 147040c8 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichit