logies including Large Language Models (LLMs), Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, cloud infrastructure, and containerized applications. The ideal candidate will contribute to real production systems while learning industry best practices in AI development, DevOps, and cybersecurity. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties \u2022 Assist in developing and testing RAG-based chatbot solutions and AI applications \u2022 Support deployment and maintenance of containerized applications using Docker and orchestration tools \u2022 Help implement CI/CD pipelines and Infrastructure as Code (IaC) practices \u2022 Assist with data pipeline development and database operations (PostgreSQL, vector databases) \u2022 Support integration of AI models and APIs into production systems \u2022 Participate in code reviews and documentation of technical solutions \u2022 Assist with monitoring, logging, and optimization of AI application performance Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Additional Requirements \u2022 Pursuing a Bachelor\u2019s or Master\u2019s degree. \u2022 Excellent communication skills and ability to work in a team environment \u2022 Self-motivated with ability to learn new technologies quickly with minimal supervision \u2022 Ability to work with and understand complex systems. \u2022 Basic understanding of Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning and Cyber Security and an interest in it as a potential career. \u2022 Strong organizational and time-management skills. \u2022 Strong problem-solving and analytical thinking abilities \u2022 Enthusiastic and willing to learn from a variety of specialists in the fields of AI/ML, IoT, and intelligent manufacturing. \u2022 Working knowledge of general-purpose programming languages such as Python. \u2022 Basic understanding of Large Language Models (LLMs) and natural language processing concepts \u2022 Experience with version control systems (Git/Gitlab) \u2022 Must be able to work a minimum of 20 hours a week. Preferred Qualifications \u2022 Completion of at least one AI/ML course (e.g. Intro to Machine Learning). \u2022 Experience building a personal computer and/or administering a network. \u2022 Basic understanding of RESTful APIs and web services \u2022 Experience with SQL or other database management systems \u2022 General understanding of cybersecurity practices \u2022 General knowledge of networking \u2022 Experience in containerization (Docker, Kubernetes) Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 83ed6fe7 Last Name (required) 34453b13 Email (required) a540752c Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 54d5f4ca Last Name (required) 6a5b92ec Email (required) f848bd9d Job Alert fe0ccde2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form a