help make the lab successful, presentable to customers, and accomplish projects in a timely manner. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties \u00b7 Support staff with reverse engineering projects. \u00b7 Interpret existing engineering and quality data. \u00b7 Model components from various data sources. \u00b7 Assist staff with research project development. \u00b7 Assisting staff on the industry level support. \u00b7 Operate and help maintain tools and equipment. \u00b7 Help keep a clean and safe work environment. \u00b7 Assisting staff with the development of training materials. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Preferred Qualifications \u00b7 Experience utilizing a CAD software program. \u00b7 Excellent oral and written communication skills. \u00b7 Proficiency with Microsoft Office Products. \u00b7 Ability to read and interpret engineering drawings and bill of material systems. \u00b7 Have great attention to detail. \u00b7 Ability to lift and carry up to 25lbs. \u00b7 Ability to work with complex systems. \u00b7 Able to work 20+ hours each week. \u00b7 Effectively prioritize and manage workflow. \u00b7 Ability to work independently on extensive tasks. Additional Information Students must have their own transportation, as some local travel between facilities may be required. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) e1f842dc Last Name (required) f628c5b0 Email (required) ceab6500 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your pho