ir test equipment, prepare test setups, and test fixturing, maintain lab organization. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Additional Requirements Must be a motivated, detail-oriented, and hands-on person willing to continuously learn and improve their skills. Preferred Qualifications CAD experience Machining and/or experience with tools and soldering Knowledge of standard test equipment (multimeters, oscilloscopes, signal generators/analyzers, data acquisition systems) Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment, including but not limited to phones, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) fc5a395c Last Name (required) a709c98b Email (required) b6918150 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 6faff4e3 Last Name (required) 43a6cacc Email (required) df28d21a Job Alert 2735bac9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or cli