ates NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R College of Education | Student NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R 499512 Student Department School of Teaching and Learning Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $11/hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Flexible Hours Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story The Student Assistant will support ongoing research projects related to special education, teacher education, motivation, and psychological well-being. The student will assist with a range of research-related tasks under faculty supervision. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties - Assist with organizing and managing research materials, including articles, survey documents, interview protocols, and data files - Support data collection activities, such as preparing survey materials, recruitment documents, and participant tracking spreadsheets - Assist with qualitative data organization, coding, and theme development - Support quantitative data entry, cleaning, and basic organization - Help prepare tables, figures, reference lists, and manuscript materials - Attend research team meetings and provide updates on assigned tasks - Complete other research-related tasks as assigned Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Preferred Qualifications Current undergraduate or graduate student at Wichita State University Interest in education, special education, psychology, teacher preparation, or related fields Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Strong written communication skills Ability to work independently and complete tasks by agreed-upon deadlines Experience with Microsoft Word, Excel, Google Drive, or similar tools Interest in learning research methods, literature review procedures, survey research, or qualitative/quantitative data analysis Prior experience with research, data entry, qualitative coding, or citation management software is preferred but not required Additional Information This position is expected to require approximately 10 hours per week, with no scheduled work hours during semester break and spring break. The specific work schedule is flexible and will be determined based on the student\u2019s availability and project needs. Some tasks may be completed independently, while regular check-in meetings with the faculty supervisor will be scheduled as needed. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) f8f32423 Last Name (required) 0882905c Email (required) fec4cbce Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 607a2efb Last Name (required) 414d59b4 Email (required) 090371f1 Job Alert fa473dc6 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. 