t(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-cnc-machinist-ii-atlas-wichita-kansas-united-states-fcb86b4a-dfb4-4ce6-97ec-f003b6bc5eba": {"title": "NIAR CNC Machinist II - ATLAS", "description": "NIAR CNC Machinist II - ATLAS - Wichita, Kansas, United States NIAR CNC Machinist II - ATLAS - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode NIAR CNC Machinist II - ATLAS NIAR Institute | Aviation, Staff NIAR CNC Machinist II - ATLAS 499550 Aviation Staff Department: NIAR Advanced Technologies Lab for Aerospace Systems Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Commensurate with experience Work Schedule: Typically, Monday - Friday 8:00am - 5:00pm; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a \"U.S. Person\u201d. Job Story Join the NIAR ATLAS team and play a key role in shaping precision manufacturing at Wichita State University. We\u2019re looking for a skilled CNC Machinist who enjoys hands-on work, solving problems, and transforming detailed technical designs into exact, high\u2011quality components. If you thrive in an environment where craftsmanship, accuracy, and continuous improvement are valued, this full-time, on-site role offers the opportunity to grow your expertise while contributing to innovative research and production. Job Summary Responsibilities include set up and operation of various tools and equipment to create, modify, or repair precision parts. Monitors the machinery and conducts regular quality checks to ensure they are running properly and that the parts are being produced according to specifications. Essential Functions Machines and fabricates components by preparing and operating machines; works from complex drawings, prototype sketches, electronic files and/or verbal instructions. Responsible for production of high precision parts and performs complex setups required to produce parts Troubleshoots issues with equipment, new programs, and/or products; detects equipment malfunctions and maintains machinery to ensure functionality Provides training and oversight of new hires and students Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent by hire date Three (3) years of experience as a CNC Machinist; Every 30 hours of related college coursework and/or technical training can be substituted for one (1) year of experience. Required License/Certifications/Training: Ability to become certified to operate forklifts, respirator use, and crane operation. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Demonstrates strong verbal and written communication skills Demonstrates and maintains value-added time management skills. Demonstrate good work ethics and lead by example. Attention to detail Ability to meet deadlines Ability to read and follow technical drawings and diagrammed instructions Ability to use precision tools to take accurate measurements Attention to detail and self-motivated Additional Information: Join the NIAR ATLAS team and play a key role in shaping precision manufacturing at Wichita State University. We\u2019re looking for a skilled CNC Machinist who enjoys hands-on work, solving problems, and transforming detailed technical designs into exact, high\u2011quality components. If you thrive in an environment where craftsmanship, accuracy, and continuous improvement are valued, this full-time, on-site role offers the opportunity to grow your expertise while contributing to innovative research and production. Physical Requirements: Ability to position self for inspection, construction or maintenance of equipment and/or buildings including confined, elevated and loud noise spaces. Ability to inspect work, materials, equipment, and/or supplies and identify any errors, needs, and/or determining factors. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Ability to move, transport, and/or deliver items, supplies, or equipment. Ability to use tools, equipment, and technology necessary to do the job. This includes dexterity in instrument manipulation. Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to ascend and descend ladders and/or stairs. Apply Now First Name (required) 813d8d80 Last Name (required) c3da99aa Email (required) 2725290b Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) fae43726 Last Name (required) bf05d11b Email (required) 9a878665 Job Alert e116a38a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Aviation Staff Aviation Staff Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 9f9c8bac Last Name (required) f715f6fa Email (required) cb73ce26 Send This Job To: b6d303df Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State Univ