ile keeping university business moving. This role sits at the intersection of legal research, contracts, records management, and university operations; supporting work that requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to connect the right people with the right information. Records and Registration Specialist Make a Difference Through Accuracy, Service, and Support Do you take pride in getting the details right? Are you naturally organized, dependable, and committed to providing outstanding service? If so, we invite you to join our team. WSU Libraries Student Assistant \u2013 Access Services WSU Libraries is seeking a student assistant with morning and weekend availability, to provide services offered within Access services, gaining experience in multiple areas of the library, including Circulation, Stacks, and Interlibrary Loan. Not sure if Wichita is right for you? Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 03824e6e Last Name (required) b9ff483f Email (required) 24a7b383 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"}, "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/isme-student-assistant-work-study-wichita-kansas-united-states": {"title": "ISME Student Assistant - Work Study", "description": "ISME Student Assistant - Work Study - Wichita, Kansas, United States ISME Student Assistant - Work Study - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Kiosk mode ISME Student Assistant - Work Study College of Engineering | Student ISME Student Assistant - Work Study 499539 Student Department Industrial, Systems and Manufacturing Engineering Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $15 Per Hour Work Schedule ; work is performed on-site and in person. Office is open 8-5 Monday-Friday. Schedule will depend on student\u2019s class schedule. Export Compliance Requirement No export control requirement. Job Story Industrial, Systems, and Manufacturing Engineering (ISME) department is seeking reliable and professional Work-Study Student Assistants to provide front office support and assist with daily administrative operations. This role serves as a key point of contact for visitors, students, faculty, and staff. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties \u2022 Answer and direct incoming phone calls in a courteous and professional manner \u2022 Warmly welcome and assist visitors; check-in guests and notify appropriate faculty/staff of arrivals \u2022 Respond to general inquiries and provide basic information about the department/programs \u2022 Sort and distribute incoming mail to faculty and staff \u2022 Monitor and restock office supplies as needed \u2022 Help maintain a clean, organized, and welcoming office environment \u2022 Monitor and update bulletin boards, digital displays, and informational materials physically available in the office \u2022 Provide administrative support and assist with special projects as assigned Required Education High School diploma or equivalent. Enrolled in a minimum of 6 credit hours at Wichita State University. Additional Requirements \u2022 Must be eligible for Federal Work-Study \u2022 Minimum GPA of 2.5 \u2022 Availability to work 10-20 hours per week between Monday\u2013Friday, 8:00 AM\u20135:00 PM \u2022 Strong communication and customer service skills \u2022 Dependable, detail-oriented, and able to work both independently and as part of a team \u2022 Self-motivated with a strong work ethic and initiative \u2022 Ability to manage multiple tasks and prioritize effectively \u2022 Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite; willingness to learn new systems \u2022 Prior phone or office experience is helpful Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and preferences. Additional Information Selection will be based on work-study eligibility, schedule availability, and the ability to follow instructions. The position is open until filled. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) 50cf96d5 Last Name (required) 1d58262d Email (required) 2f577e4b Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or c